VALUES
	(1,'Luke Skywalker','19BBY','blue','blond','172','77','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Luke_Skywalker','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/2/20/LukeTLJ.jpg','[\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Red Squadron\",\"Rogue Squadron\",\"Massassi Group\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Jedi Order\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"New Republic\",\"Resistance\"]','Luke Skywalker was a farm boy from Tatooine who became a Jedi Knight. He was the son of Anakin Skywalker, destined to confront the dark side. Trained by Obi-Wan Kenobi and Yoda, Luke faced incredible challenges. He played a central role in the fall of the Galactic Empire. Through compassion, he redeemed his father, Darth Vader. Luke symbolizes hope, transformation, and the enduring light of the Force.','Luke Skywalker was born during the final days of the Galactic Republic to Padmé Amidala and Anakin Skywalker. Separated at birth from his sister Leia, he was raised on Tatooine by his aunt and uncle. Luke dreamed of adventure but lived a quiet life until two droids arrived with a message from Princess Leia. His encounter with Obi-Wan Kenobi introduced him to the Force and his true heritage. Driven by loss and curiosity, he joined the Rebel Alliance. With training from Obi-Wan and later Yoda, Luke developed his abilities as a Jedi. He faced the Empire’s might, showing bravery during battles like the assault on the Death Star. Luke learned of his father’s identity, leading to inner turmoil and renewed purpose. In a climactic confrontation, he refused to kill Darth Vader, choosing mercy instead. His actions inspired Anakin’s return and the Emperor’s downfall. Luke rebuilt the Jedi Order but struggled with the burden of legacy. He isolated himself after a tragic failure with his nephew, Ben Solo. Rey eventually found him, reigniting his role in the Resistance’s fight. Though reluctant, Luke performed one final heroic act through the Force. He projected himself across the galaxy to confront Kylo Ren and save the Resistance. The strain of the act cost him his life, and he passed into the Force peacefully. Luke’s legend lived on as a symbol of selflessness and redemption. Throughout his life, he struggled with doubt but chose the light. His journey defined the battle between darkness and hope. Luke Skywalker remains one of the greatest heroes in galactic history.','light','blue','2014-12-09T13:50:51.644000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:56.891000Z',1),
	(2,'C-3PO','112BBY','yellow','n/a','167','75','gold','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/C-3PO','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/3f/C-3PO_TLJ_Card_Trader_Award_Card.png','[\"Skywalker family\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"House of Organa\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Massassi Group\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Pathfinders\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"New Republic\",\"Resistance\",\"Resistance spy droid network\"]','C-3PO is a protocol droid fluent in over six million forms of communication. He was originally built by Anakin Skywalker on Tatooine. Though often nervous, he loyally served the Skywalker family. He frequently found himself in dangerous situations despite his intentions. C-3PO’s translations and etiquette skills were invaluable to many missions. He is known for his golden plating, constant worrying, and unwavering loyalty.','C-3PO was built by young Anakin Skywalker to assist with protocol and etiquette. Initially without his golden plating, he gained his iconic look later. As a protocol droid, C-3PO specialized in translation, etiquette, and diplomacy. He often partnered with the astromech R2-D2, forming a beloved droid duo. C-3PO accompanied Padmé Amidala, Anakin, and later the Skywalker children. During the Clone Wars, he assisted the Republic and worked with many key figures. Despite his anxious nature, he frequently ended up in critical missions. He served aboard ships, in senate chambers, and on the battlefield. C-3PO was reprogrammed several times to keep sensitive information secure. He was present during the rise and fall of the Galactic Empire. In the Rebellion, he acted as a translator and advisor in key meetings. He witnessed historic events such as the destruction of Alderaan and Death Stars. C-3PO’s loyalty to Leia Organa and the Resistance never wavered. Even when memories were wiped, his dedication remained embedded in his core. He played a pivotal role in locating Sith wayfinders during the Resistance\'s final push. C-3PO\'s humor and dramatic reactions often brought levity to tense moments. Though mechanical, his relationships and emotions seemed remarkably human. He survived many battles and regimes, always returning to help the cause. His presence throughout decades of galactic history made him legendary. C-3PO is remembered as a faithful servant, translator, and friend.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:10:51.357000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.309000Z',1),
	(3,'R2-D2','33BBY','red','n/a','96','32','white, blue','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/R2-D2','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/eb/ArtooTFA2-Fathead.png','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"501st Legion\",\"R2-D2\'s battle droid squadron\",\"D-Squad\",\"House of Organa\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Massassi Group\",\"Red Squadron\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"Resistance\"]','R2-D2 is a resourceful astromech droid often found at the heart of galactic events. He served Anakin Skywalker and later Luke Skywalker with unwavering loyalty. His intelligence and bravery have saved countless lives. R2-D2 communicates through beeps and boops but expresses remarkable emotion. He\'s a key player in many critical missions. His memory banks hold the secrets of the galaxy.','R2-D2 is an iconic astromech droid who first served under Queen Amidala and then Anakin Skywalker. Designed for starfighter maintenance, he frequently exceeded his programming. His courage saved the lives of his masters on many occasions, including escaping battlefields and infiltrating enemy ships. With his rotating dome and extendable tools, R2-D2 became more than just a mechanical assistant. He fought bravely in the Clone Wars and later in the Rebellion. He played a central role in the destruction of both Death Stars. His bond with C-3PO provided comic relief and heartfelt moments. R2-D2 never received a memory wipe, preserving secrets from the Old Republic to the rise of the First Order. His silent wisdom was valued by the Jedi. He stood beside Luke Skywalker in some of the most iconic scenes in galactic history. R2-D2 also carried Leia’s plea for help to Obi-Wan Kenobi. He helped navigate hyperspace and unlock security doors. Throughout wars and peace, he remained steadfast. Despite his small size, he was never underestimated. His bravery was acknowledged by the leaders of the Rebellion. R2-D2 continues to inspire droid and human allies alike. He is a symbol of loyalty, resilience, and heroism. Few characters have witnessed as much as R2-D2, and even fewer have shaped so much.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:11:50.376000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.311000Z',8),
	(4,'Darth Vader','41.9BBY','yellow','none','202','136','white','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/fr.starwars/images/3/32/Dark_Vador.jpg','[\"501st Legion\",\"Sith\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial High Command\"]','Darth Vader, once known as Anakin Skywalker, fell from grace as a Jedi Knight. His transformation into a Sith Lord marked a turning point for the galaxy. Haunted by fear and manipulated by Emperor Palpatine, he embraced the dark side. Vader became the face of the Galactic Empire’s might and terror. Despite his cruelty, traces of his former self lingered deep within. His ultimate redemption would bring balance back to the Force.','Anakin Skywalker began as a gifted slave boy on Tatooine, showing early signs of Force sensitivity. He was discovered by Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn and brought before the Jedi Council. Though deemed too old and dangerous to train, his immense potential could not be ignored. Anakin’s heroic deeds during the Clone Wars earned him admiration, but also fostered arrogance. Fear of loss and dreams of death consumed him, leaving him vulnerable to manipulation. Palpatine, the Sith Lord behind the Republic’s fall, exploited Anakin’s insecurities. Promised the power to save his loved ones, Anakin betrayed the Jedi Order. He adopted the name Darth Vader and helped destroy the Jedi Temple. As the Emperor’s enforcer, Vader hunted Jedi survivors and led the Empire’s expansion. His mechanical suit became a symbol of fear throughout the galaxy. Despite his power, he remained tormented by pain, regret, and inner conflict. Years later, he discovered he had a son: Luke Skywalker. The bond between father and son reignited a spark of hope within him. Through Luke’s faith, Vader confronted the Emperor in a final act of defiance. He sacrificed himself to save his son, fulfilling the prophecy of balance. Anakin\'s redemption marked the end of the Sith’s rule and the Emperor’s reign. His legacy lived on through Luke and the new generation of Jedi. Vader’s tale remains a tragic yet powerful story of corruption and salvation. His fall and rise serve as a lasting lesson about choice, destiny, and hope. Though feared across systems, he died as a hero remembered by the Force.','dark','red','2014-12-10T15:18:20.704000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.313000Z',1),
	(5,'Leia Organa','19BBY','brown','brown','150','49','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Leia_Organa','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/fc/Leia_Organa_TLJ.png','[\"Elder Houses\",\"House of Organa\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Senate\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Massassi Group\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Alliance High Command\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"New Republic\",\"Populists\",\"Resistance\"]','Leia Organa was a princess, senator, general, and fierce leader. She led the Rebellion with both heart and strategy. Born to Padmé Amidala and Anakin Skywalker, she carried great legacy. Despite personal loss, she remained resilient. Leia’s courage inspired allies across the galaxy. Her determination shaped the fight for freedom.','Leia Organa was born during the final moments of the Galactic Republic to Padmé Amidala and Anakin Skywalker. Hidden from her father, Darth Vader, she was adopted by Bail Organa and raised on Alderaan as royalty. From a young age, she demonstrated strong leadership and empathy. As a senator, she fought to preserve democracy in the Imperial Senate. When diplomacy failed, she became a leader of the Rebel Alliance. Leia played a crucial role in securing plans to the Death Star and coordinating the Battle of Yavin. Her inner strength shone even in captivity. She forged lasting bonds with Luke Skywalker and Han Solo. After the Empire’s fall, Leia co-founded the New Republic. She later established the Resistance to oppose the First Order. Her son Ben Solo’s fall to the dark side brought deep personal grief. Yet, she never lost faith in redemption. Her presence grounded the Resistance in hope and discipline. Even as a general, she remained humble and accessible. Leia’s relationship with the Force, though understated, was genuine. Her sacrifice helped reconnect her son to the light. Leia was a symbol of resilience in turbulent times. Her legacy extended beyond the battlefield. In every generation, she stood for justice, love, and unity.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:20:09.791000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.315000Z',2),
	(6,'Owen Lars','52BBY','blue','brown, grey','178','120','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Owen_Lars','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/eb/OwenCardTrader.png','[\"Lars family\"]','Owen Lars was a moisture farmer on Tatooine, known for his quiet resilience. He raised Luke Skywalker as his own after the fall of the Jedi. Owen aimed to keep Luke safe by keeping him distant from galactic conflicts. Though stern, his protective nature stemmed from deep care. His home became a hidden sanctuary from the chaos of war. Owen’s legacy is one of duty, sacrifice, and unspoken love.','Owen Lars was the son of Cliegg Lars and stepson to Shmi Skywalker. He lived a modest life on the desert planet of Tatooine as a moisture farmer. After Anakin Skywalker’s fall, Obi-Wan entrusted Owen and Beru with Luke’s upbringing. Owen accepted the responsibility, despite the risks of harboring a Jedi’s son. He worked hard to provide stability in a world of drought and danger. Though not affectionate, Owen’s actions reflected a deep sense of protection. He discouraged Luke from dreaming beyond the farm to keep him grounded. His stern warnings were shaped by fear of history repeating itself. Owen clashed with Obi-Wan, whom he saw as a threat to Luke’s future. Despite their tension, both men wanted what was best for the boy. Owen maintained a strong work ethic, modeling responsibility for Luke. He and Beru created a peaceful home amid growing Imperial reach. As Luke matured, tensions rose over his ambitions to leave. Owen hoped Luke would never learn the truth of his origins. His concerns, however, could not shield Luke from destiny. Stormtroopers eventually discovered the Lars homestead while searching for droids. Owen and Beru were killed, marking a tragic end to their guardianship. Their deaths became a pivotal moment in Luke’s journey. Owen’s role, though often overlooked, shaped the galaxy’s future hero. He represents the quiet strength of ordinary people in extraordinary times.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:52:14.024000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.317000Z',1),
	(7,'Beru Whitesun lars','47BBY','blue','brown','165','75','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Beru_Whitesun_Lars','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/c/cc/BeruCardTrader.png','[]','Beru Whitesun Lars was the wife of Owen Lars and caretaker to Luke Skywalker. She lived a quiet life as a moisture farmer on Tatooine. Beru supported Owen’s decision to raise Luke away from conflict. She provided warmth and balance in their strict household. Her role, though understated, was vital in shaping Luke’s early life. Beru’s kindness and strength left a lasting impact on the galaxy’s future hero.','Beru Whitesun Lars was born and raised on Tatooine, where she met and married Owen Lars. Together, they worked as moisture farmers in the planet’s harsh environment. When Luke Skywalker was brought to them, Beru welcomed him with love and care. She became a mother figure to the young boy, offering quiet guidance. While Owen took a stricter approach, Beru provided compassion and encouragement. She believed Luke deserved the truth but agreed to protect him from danger. Their home was modest, but she maintained it with care and resilience. Beru supported Owen’s decision to keep Luke grounded, despite her reservations. She showed wisdom and understanding beyond words, often calming tensions. Her daily life reflected the perseverance of frontier families. Beru remained strong in the face of Imperial expansion. Despite the risks, she never hesitated to protect Luke. She helped shape Luke’s sense of family, responsibility, and hope. When stormtroopers came searching for droids, they found the Lars homestead. Beru and Owen were killed defending their home and secret. Their deaths shocked Luke and propelled him into a wider galaxy. Though her role was small, her influence was immense. Beru’s memory endured through Luke’s journey and choices. Her courage and compassion helped ignite a spark of rebellion. Beru remains a symbol of quiet strength and unsung heroism.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:53:41.121000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.319000Z',1),
	(8,'R5-D4','unknown','red','n/a','97','32','white, red','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/R5-D4','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/c/cb/R5-D4_Sideshow.png','[\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\"]','R5-D4 was an astromech droid sold on Tatooine. He briefly belonged to Owen Lars. A malfunction caused his rejection, paving the way for R2-D2’s journey. He later became part of the Rebellion. R5-D4’s role, though small, had great consequence. He represents overlooked heroes of the galaxy.','R5-D4 was a standard red and white astromech droid stationed on Tatooine. He was purchased by Owen Lars from the Jawas to assist with daily tasks. However, his motivator malfunctioned shortly after purchase. This seemingly minor failure led to R2-D2 being selected instead, altering the course of galactic history. R5-D4 was often dismissed as defective, but his sacrifice was not in vain. Legends suggest he sabotaged himself to allow R2-D2’s mission to proceed. He remained with the Jawas and later found a second chance in service. Some accounts place him as a quiet ally to the Rebellion. His story exemplifies the theme that all beings, no matter how small or flawed, can play pivotal roles. R5-D4 lacked advanced programming but had a unique spirit. He symbolized missed opportunities and quiet bravery. His red dome and stubby frame are iconic. Though not as famous as other droids, he holds a special place in fan lore. He stood witness to the Skywalker legacy’s beginning. His short time in the spotlight was enough to change everything. R5-D4 endures as an unsung figure in Star Wars mythology. His presence reminds us of fate’s strange ways. The Force works in mysterious paths, even through faulty circuitry. R5-D4 earned respect among devoted fans and historians alike.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:57:50.959000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.321000Z',1),
	(9,'Biggs Darklighter','24BBY','brown','black','183','84','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Biggs_Darklighter','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/0/00/BiggsHS-ANH.png','[\"Galactic Empire\",\"Prefsbelt Fleet Camp\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Red Squadron\",\"Massassi Group\"]','Biggs Darklighter was a skilled pilot from Tatooine and a friend of Luke Skywalker. He trained at the Imperial Academy before defecting to the Rebellion. Biggs flew with Red Squadron in the assault on the Death Star. He was brave, loyal, and one of the few who believed in Luke early on. His sacrifice helped pave the way for the Rebellion’s first major victory. Biggs is remembered as a courageous fighter and true friend.','Biggs Darklighter grew up on Tatooine and shared dreams of adventure with Luke Skywalker. He left the desert planet to join the Imperial Academy, seeking to become a pilot. There, he witnessed the Empire’s corruption and chose to defect. He joined the Rebel Alliance and became a trusted member of Red Squadron. Biggs reunited with Luke shortly before the Battle of Yavin. Their friendship rekindled a sense of hope in both of them. During the attack on the Death Star, Biggs flew a T-65 X-wing. He covered Luke’s run through the trench, defending him from enemy fire. Despite heavy resistance, he stayed with the mission until the end. Biggs was killed in action, moments before the Death Star was destroyed. His bravery and loyalty helped secure the Rebels’ critical victory. Though his screen time was short, his legacy endured through Luke. Biggs represented the many lives sacrificed in the fight for freedom. He was a symbol of youthful idealism turned courageous resistance. Rebel commanders remembered him as a talented and selfless pilot. His story inspired future generations to take up the cause. Luke mourned his loss but honored him by continuing the mission. Biggs became a quiet legend among rebel pilots. His memory was kept alive in Tatooine\'s stories and beyond. Biggs Darklighter remains one of the Rebellion’s early heroes.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T15:59:50.509000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.323000Z',1),
	(10,'Obi-Wan Kenobi','57BBY','blue-gray','auburn, white','182','77','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Obi-Wan_Kenobi','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/4e/ObiWanHS-SWE.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"212th Attack Battalion\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\"]','Obi-Wan Kenobi was a wise Jedi Master and central figure in galactic history. He trained both Anakin and Luke Skywalker, shaping the fate of the galaxy. Obi-Wan served with honor during the Clone Wars. After Anakin\'s fall, he watched over Luke in exile on Tatooine. He returned briefly to guide Luke spiritually after death. Obi-Wan embodies duty, sacrifice, and quiet strength.','Obi-Wan Kenobi was discovered as a Force-sensitive child and trained as a Jedi. He served as a Padawan to Qui-Gon Jinn, from whom he learned compassion and focus. Obi-Wan became a Jedi Knight after defeating Darth Maul in battle. He took Anakin Skywalker as his apprentice, honoring Qui-Gon’s dying wish. Their bond was deep, but Anakin’s downfall became Obi-Wan’s greatest failure. He fought in the Clone Wars and led many successful missions. Obi-Wan served on the Jedi Council, known for his wisdom and diplomacy. When Order 66 was executed, he survived and went into hiding. He brought Anakin’s infant son, Luke, to Owen Lars on Tatooine. There, Obi-Wan lived in isolation, watching over Luke from afar. Years later, he revealed Luke’s heritage and began his Jedi training. He sacrificed himself during a duel with Darth Vader to protect Luke. Through the Force, Obi-Wan continued to guide Luke as a spirit. He offered counsel and reassurance in moments of doubt. His actions laid the groundwork for the fall of the Empire. Obi-Wan\'s legacy lived on in the Jedi Order’s rebirth. He was remembered as a mentor, protector, and symbol of balance. Though haunted by his past, he remained committed to the light. Obi-Wan\'s calm demeanor hid immense emotional weight. He remains one of the most revered figures in Jedi history.','light','blue','2014-12-10T16:16:29.192000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.325000Z',20),
	(11,'Anakin Skywalker','41.9BBY','blue','blond','188','84','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Anakin_Skywalker','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/6/6f/Anakin_Skywalker_RotS.png','[\"501st Legion\",\"Sith\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial High Command\"]','Anakin Skywalker was a gifted podracer and slave boy from Tatooine. Discovered by Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn, he was believed to be the Chosen One. Anakin showed incredible power but struggled with fear and attachment. He fought bravely in the Clone Wars and became a Jedi Knight. Haunted by visions and loss, he fell to the dark side and became Darth Vader. His journey was one of tragedy, power, and eventual redemption.','Anakin Skywalker was born on Tatooine, living as a slave with his mother Shmi. He impressed Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn with his podracing skills and Force sensitivity. Believing Anakin to be the Chosen One, Qui-Gon brought him to Coruscant for Jedi training. Despite initial resistance, Anakin joined the Jedi Order under Obi-Wan Kenobi’s mentorship. He quickly rose in skill and became a powerful Jedi Knight. During the Clone Wars, Anakin led many missions and gained a reputation as a fierce warrior. He married Padmé Amidala in secret, defying the Jedi Code. Anakin was tormented by visions of Padmé’s death in childbirth. In a desperate attempt to save her, he was manipulated by Chancellor Palpatine. Anakin turned to the dark side, adopting the name Darth Vader. He led the purge of the Jedi Temple and hunted down surviving Jedi. Padmé died after confronting him, and Anakin was severely injured in a duel with Obi-Wan. He was rebuilt by Palpatine into a cyborg, losing much of his humanity. For decades, he served as the Emperor’s enforcer. He later discovered that his son, Luke Skywalker, had survived. Luke’s compassion and refusal to fight finally reached him. In a moment of clarity, Anakin turned on the Emperor to save his son. He died soon after, but his final act redeemed him. Anakin\'s story is one of destiny, corruption, and the enduring struggle between light and dark. He fulfilled the prophecy in the end, bringing balance to the Force.','dark','blue','2014-12-10T16:20:44.310000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.327000Z',1),
	(12,'Wilhuff Tarkin','64BBY','blue','auburn, grey','180','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Wilhuff_Tarkin','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/c/c1/Tarkininfobox.jpg','[\"Galactic Republic\",\"Sullust Sector Spacefarers Academy\",\"Judicial Forces\",\"Republic Navy\",\"Strategic Advisory Cell\",\"Outland Regions Security Force\",\"Outland\'s anti-pirate taskforce\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Battle Station Command\",\"Imperial Officer Corps\",\"Imperial Navy\",\"Tarkin Initiative\"]','Wilhuff Tarkin was a cold and calculating officer of the Galactic Empire. He rose through the ranks using discipline, fear, and political skill. Tarkin was instrumental in the creation and use of the Death Star. He believed fear of force would maintain galactic order. Serving directly under Emperor Palpatine, he had immense authority. Tarkin\'s legacy is one of authoritarian control and ruthless efficiency.','Wilhuff Tarkin was born on the Outer Rim world of Eriadu. From a young age, he was instilled with a belief in strength through order. He joined military academies and distinguished himself as a strategic mind. Tarkin served in the Republic\'s navy during the Clone Wars. He often clashed with Jedi, favoring direct control over diplomacy. After the Republic’s fall, he became a leading figure in the new Empire. Tarkin advocated for the use of fear to maintain control across the galaxy. He oversaw the construction and deployment of the Death Star. His Tarkin Doctrine emphasized dominance over liberty. He was given command of the battle station and ruled with near-autonomy. Tarkin destroyed Alderaan to demonstrate the Empire’s power. This act of terror galvanized the Rebellion’s resolve. Despite warnings, he underestimated the Rebels\' capabilities. He remained on the Death Star during the Battle of Yavin. The station was destroyed by Luke Skywalker, killing Tarkin. His legacy shaped Imperial policy and fear-based governance. Tarkin was remembered as a symbol of tyranny and arrogance. His strategies were studied even after the Empire’s fall. His ambition and ruthlessness remain infamous in galactic history. Tarkin believed peace could only be achieved through fear and submission.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-10T16:26:56.138000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.330000Z',21),
	(13,'Chewbacca','200BBY','blue','brown','228','112','unknown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Chewbacca','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/48/Chewbacca_TLJ.png','[\"Galactic Republic\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Pathfinders\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"New Republic\",\"Resistance\"]','Chewbacca is a towering Wookiee from the planet Kashyyyk. Known for his strength and loyalty, he became Han Solo’s co-pilot. He helped fight against the Empire as part of the Rebellion. Chewbacca’s roar is both a warning and a comfort to his allies. Despite his fearsome appearance, he’s deeply compassionate. He is a true warrior, friend, and symbol of Wookiee pride.','Chewbacca, born on the lush Wookiee planet of Kashyyyk, lived through the Clone Wars. Captured by the Empire, he was enslaved until freed by Han Solo. The two became inseparable friends and partners in smuggling. Chewbacca was known for his loyalty and immense physical power. He co-piloted the Millennium Falcon through numerous battles and escapes. Though he spoke only in roars, his meaning was always clear to Han and close allies. He aided in missions for the Rebel Alliance and Resistance. He participated in battles from Endor to Starkiller Base. Chewbacca often acted as the moral compass in his group. He formed bonds with Leia, Luke, Rey, and others over time. When Han was killed, Chewbacca mourned and continued the fight. He showed courage in dangerous missions and kindness in quiet moments. Chewbacca inherited Han’s life debt philosophy from Wookiee culture. He survived the rise and fall of empires. He later piloted the Falcon alongside Rey, continuing his legacy. Chewbacca’s actions had a major impact despite limited speech. He represented freedom, friendship, and fierce loyalty. His towering presence became a symbol of the Rebellion’s strength. Even in times of loss, Chewbacca stood strong beside his allies. He remains a beloved legend of galactic resistance and resilience.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T16:42:45.066000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.332000Z',14),
	(14,'Han Solo','29BBY','brown','brown','180','80','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Han_Solo','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/e2/TFAHanSolo.png','[\"Galactic Empire\",\"Jabba Desilijic Tiure\'s criminal empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Leia Organa\'s team\",\"Endor strike team\",\"Kingdom of Han\",\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"New Republic\",\"New Republic Pilots Commission\",\"Han Solo\'s shipping company\",\"Resistance\"]','Han Solo was a smuggler turned hero who became a general in the Rebel Alliance. He was known for his charm, wit, and unmatched piloting skills. Owner of the Millennium Falcon, he journeyed across the galaxy with Chewbacca. Though once self-serving, Han developed strong bonds with his allies. His love for Princess Leia helped ground his sense of purpose. Han Solo’s legacy is that of courage, sacrifice, and redemption.','Han Solo was born on the industrial planet of Corellia. He escaped a harsh upbringing by joining the Imperial Navy, only to desert later. He earned a reputation as a smuggler and pilot, often working for shady employers. During one job, he saved the Wookiee Chewbacca, forming a lifelong friendship. With the Millennium Falcon, they became famous across the galaxy. Han’s life changed when he transported Luke Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi. Though reluctant, he aided the Rebel Alliance in key battles. His bravery at the Battle of Yavin made him a trusted leader. Han developed a deep relationship with Leia Organa. Captured by bounty hunters and frozen in carbonite, he survived imprisonment. He later played a vital role in the Battle of Endor and the downfall of the Empire. Afterward, Han struggled with family and his son Ben Solo\'s fall to the dark side. Though separated from Leia, he continued to fight with the Resistance. Han faced his son Kylo Ren in a final attempt at reconciliation. Kylo killed him, marking a tragic end to his journey. Despite his flaws, Han was admired for his heart and bravery. He inspired generations of pilots and rebels alike. His name became legendary in cantinas and command centers across the galaxy. Han Solo’s transformation from rogue to hero defines his enduring myth. His spirit lives on in the Resistance and those who fly with hope.','light',NULL,'2014-12-10T16:49:14.582000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.334000Z',22),
	(15,'Greedo','44BBY','black','n/a','173','74','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Greedo','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/c/c6/Greedo.jpg','[\"Trade Federation\"]','Greedo was a Rodian bounty hunter with a restless ambition. He worked under Jabba the Hutt. Known for his clumsy approach, he met his end facing Han Solo. His green skin and snout made him instantly recognizable. Though not the galaxy’s best shot, he had guts. Greedo\'s story is short but memorable.','Greedo was born on Rodia and was driven by a desire to prove himself. As a young Rodian, he joined the bounty hunting profession seeking wealth and recognition. He eventually came under the employment of Jabba the Hutt. His most infamous assignment was to apprehend Han Solo over a debt. Greedo confronted Han in the Mos Eisley Cantina. The encounter ended fatally for him, as Han shot first—according to some accounts. His death marked one of Star Wars’ most debated moments. Greedo’s boldness outweighed his tactical thinking. Despite his end, his brief screen time left a strong impression. His distinctive look and garbled speech became iconic. He wore a green jumpsuit and wielded a blaster with little finesse. Greedo embodied the risks of the bounty hunting trade. He was not as skilled as Boba Fett, but just as eager. His overconfidence often put him in danger. Jabba considered him expendable, using him for low-priority missions. Greedo’s reputation among peers was mixed. Some admired his nerve; others scoffed at his failures. He had no known family and kept few allies. His death sent a message to other debt collectors. In death, he became more famous than he ever was alive.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-10T17:03:30.334000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.336000Z',23),
	(16,'Jabba Desilijic Tiure','600BBY','orange','n/a','175','1,358','green-tan, brown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Jabba_Desilijic_Tiure','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/7f/Jabba_SWSB.png','[\"Hutt Clan\",\"Grand Hutt Council\",\"Jabba Desilijic Tiure\'s criminal empire\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Shadow Collective\",\"Crymorah syndicate\",\"Galactic Empire\"]','Jabba the Hutt was a powerful crime lord who ruled from Tatooine. His massive palace was the center of smuggling and slavery operations. Feared by many, he was both cunning and sadistic. He captured Princess Leia and imprisoned Han Solo in carbonite. His reign ended when Leia strangled him during a rescue mission. Jabba remains a symbol of decadence, power, and corruption.','Jabba Desilijic Tiure, better known as Jabba the Hutt, was a notorious gangster. He belonged to the Hutt Clan and amassed power through crime and manipulation. Operating from Tatooine, Jabba controlled spice trade, slavery, and bounty hunters. He hosted lavish and brutal events in his desert palace. Jabba was feared for his cruelty and ability to make people disappear. He commanded respect even from the Galactic Empire. Boba Fett and Greedo were among his hired enforcers. Jabba placed a bounty on Han Solo after unpaid debts. He captured Solo with Boba Fett\'s help and displayed him in carbonite. Leia Organa infiltrated the palace to rescue Solo but was captured and enslaved. Luke Skywalker arrived with demands and fought Jabba’s guards. During the confrontation at the Great Pit of Carkoon, Jabba attempted execution. Leia used her chains to strangle Jabba, killing him. His death marked a blow to the Hutt syndicates. Jabba’s influence persisted briefly through remnants of his empire. He left a lasting legacy in underworld circles. Hutts were both feared and despised due to his reputation. His presence loomed over many dealings in the Outer Rim. Jabba represented unchecked power and hedonism. His grotesque opulence became iconic in Star Wars mythology.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-10T17:11:31.638000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.338000Z',24),
	(18,'Wedge Antilles','21BBY','hazel','brown','170','77','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Wedge_Antilles','https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/b/b2/WedgeAntilles-Masterwork2020.png','[\"Galactic Empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Phoenix Cell\",\"Massassi Group\",\"Red Squadron\",\"Rogue Squadron\",\"New Republic\",\"Phantom Squadron\"]','Wedge Antilles was a skilled starfighter pilot and leader in the Rebel Alliance. He fought bravely in major battles like Yavin and Endor. Known for his loyalty and tactical skill, he rose through the ranks quickly. Wedge commanded Rogue Squadron with precision and courage. He later helped shape the New Republic\'s military. His name became synonymous with heroism and dedication.','Wedge Antilles hailed from Corellia and joined the Rebellion at a young age. He quickly gained a reputation for his flying ability. Wedge survived the Battle of Yavin, helping Luke Skywalker destroy the Death Star. He later led Rogue Squadron in several daring missions. At the Battle of Hoth, he helped the Rebels evacuate Echo Base. Wedge was instrumental in the Battle of Endor, flying in the final assault. He destroyed part of the second Death Star’s core with Lando Calrissian. Wedge mentored many young pilots and fostered unity in his squadron. After the fall of the Empire, he served the New Republic. He played a role in establishing new military strategies and protocols. Wedge preferred action to politics and avoided high-ranking positions. He fought in the battles against Imperial remnants. His leadership made Rogue Squadron legendary. He stayed loyal to his friends and ideals throughout conflicts. Wedge was respected for his humility and bravery. In later years, he trained a new generation of pilots. He helped in the Resistance\'s struggle against the First Order. Despite his age, he remained a valuable ally and symbol of resistance. Wedge Antilles’ name became a beacon of hope in dark times. His life was one of purpose, courage, and unwavering belief in freedom.','light',NULL,'2014-12-12T11:08:06.469000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.341000Z',22),
	(19,'Jek Tono Porkins','unknown','blue','brown','180','110','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Jek_Tono_Porkins','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/eb/JekPorkins-DB.png','[\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Tierfon Yellow Aces\",\"Red Squadron\",\"Massassi Group\"]','Jek Tono Porkins was a Rebel pilot known for his courage. He flew a Y-wing during the Battle of Yavin. Despite his bulky frame, he was agile in space combat. He perished in the attack on the first Death Star. His call sign was Red Six. Porkins became a symbol of unshaken bravery.','Jek Tono Porkins was born on the planet Bestine IV. He eventually joined the Rebellion, bringing with him exceptional piloting skills. His size made him stand out among his peers, but it did not hinder his performance. He earned the call sign Red Six in the Red Squadron. Porkins took part in the daring assault on the first Death Star. His ship was struck early in the mission. Despite warnings, he refused to eject, trying to stabilize the craft. He died in action, becoming one of the first martyrs of the Rebellion. His loss was felt among his comrades. Porkins was known for his humor and appetite. Yet he was also regarded as deeply loyal. He trained in low-atmosphere dogfighting and excelled in target locking. He trusted his squadmates completely. His bravery inspired new recruits. Though his screen time was short, his legacy endured. Action figures and tributes cemented his place in fan culture. Porkins embodied the everyman hero: flawed, grounded, and heroic. His name became a rallying cry for underdogs everywhere. Historians of the Rebellion regard him with quiet respect. His sacrifice helped pave the way for Luke Skywalker’s success. Porkins remains a cherished figure in the annals of Rebel history.','light',NULL,'2014-12-12T11:16:56.569000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.343000Z',26),
	(20,'Yoda','896BBY','brown','white','66','17','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Yoda','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/d/d6/Yoda_SWSB.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Yoda was a wise and powerful Jedi Master who trained generations of Jedi. He served on the Jedi High Council for centuries. Yoda was known for his deep understanding of the Force. He led the Jedi through the Clone Wars and faced immense challenges. Exiled after the Jedi purge, he mentored Luke Skywalker in secret. Yoda’s teachings continue to guide the galaxy’s guardians.','Yoda lived for over 900 years and was one of the most powerful Jedi in history. He served the Jedi Order and Republic with wisdom and serenity. Yoda trained countless Jedi, shaping the Order’s traditions. His deep connection to the Force made him a revered figure. He foresaw danger during the Republic’s final days. During the Clone Wars, Yoda became a military leader. Despite his power, he struggled to sense the Sith’s hidden rise. Yoda fought Darth Sidious after the Jedi purge began. He was defeated and went into exile on Dagobah. There, he waited and meditated for years. When Luke Skywalker arrived, Yoda trained him in the ways of the Force. He emphasized balance, patience, and self-awareness. Yoda died peacefully, becoming one with the Force. His spirit later guided Luke and others. Yoda’s legacy shaped the future of the Jedi. He remained humble, often teaching through riddles and humor. His wisdom influenced the galaxy beyond his lifetime. Yoda is remembered as a symbol of light and endurance. His presence marked a golden age of the Jedi Order. He was the heart and conscience of the Jedi tradition.','light','green','2014-12-15T12:26:01.042000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.345000Z',28),
	(21,'Palpatine','82BBY','yellow','grey','170','75','pale','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Palpatine','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/d/d8/Emperor_Sidious.png','[\"House Palpatine\",\"Damask Holdings\",\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Sith\",\"Order of the Sith Lords\",\"Naboo Diplomatic Corps\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Senate\",\"Trade Federation\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Dark Empire\"]','Palpatine was a Sith Lord who became Emperor of the Galactic Empire. He hid behind a mask of civility as a senator and chancellor. Palpatine orchestrated the fall of the Republic and Jedi. He ruled with fear, using Darth Vader as his enforcer. Even after death, his influence lingered across the galaxy. Palpatine remains the ultimate symbol of dark ambition and manipulation.','Palpatine was born on Naboo and rose to power as a cunning politician. Secretly trained by Darth Plagueis, he became the Sith Lord Darth Sidious. He manipulated galactic events to create the Clone Wars. Using fear and deception, he rose from senator to Supreme Chancellor. Palpatine convinced the Senate to grant him emergency powers. He orchestrated Order 66, resulting in the Jedi’s near extinction. He declared himself Emperor, transforming the Republic into an Empire. As ruler, he enforced strict control and built the Death Star. His apprentice Darth Vader carried out many of his commands. Palpatine maintained his rule through terror and propaganda. He sought immortality and studied dark side secrets. Eventually, Luke Skywalker confronted him aboard the second Death Star. Vader betrayed Palpatine to save his son, seemingly ending the Sith. But Palpatine’s spirit endured through cloning and dark rituals. He returned during the rise of the First Order. Rey, his granddaughter, ultimately defeated him on Exegol. Palpatine’s death marked the final fall of the Sith. His legacy left scars on generations and institutions. He remains one of the galaxy’s most feared figures. Palpatine\'s ambition reshaped history through shadows and betrayal.','dark','red','2014-12-15T12:48:05.971000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.347000Z',8),
	(22,'Boba Fett','31.5BBY','brown','black','183','78.2','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Boba_Fett','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/79/Boba_Fett_HS_Fathead.png','[\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Boba Fett\'s syndicate\",\"Jabba Desilijic Tiure\'s criminal empire\",\"Galactic Empire\"]','Boba Fett is a notorious bounty hunter feared across the galaxy. Clad in Mandalorian armor, he upholds a cold, calculating demeanor. A clone of Jango Fett, he was raised to follow in his father\'s footsteps. His ship, Slave I, became his signature vehicle. Boba worked for powerful clients like Jabba the Hutt. His legend grew through ruthless efficiency.','Boba Fett was created as an unaltered clone of Jango Fett, raised by his father to inherit the bounty hunting trade. After Jango\'s death on Geonosis, Boba vowed vengeance and survival. He matured quickly, navigating the galaxy\'s underworld from a young age. His proficiency with weapons and tactics rivaled seasoned hunters. Clad in distinctive Mandalorian armor, he adopted a stoic and deadly persona. Slave I, his customized ship, became synonymous with his name. Boba took high-profile contracts from both the Empire and underworld figures. He is best known for capturing Han Solo and delivering him to Jabba the Hutt. Despite falling into the Sarlacc pit, he survived and reclaimed his armor. He then took over Jabba’s former territory. Boba\'s past is marked by solitude and unwavering resolve. His lineage and legacy are intertwined with Mandalorian culture. Fett\'s stoic demeanor hides a tactical mind. His combat skills and tracking abilities are exceptional. He balances between mercenary ethics and personal honor. Though feared, he rarely acted out of cruelty alone. The mythos surrounding him grew through whispered tales. Legends and rumors follow Boba Fett wherever he goes. In the criminal world, his name commands fear and respect. His journey continues as a leader shaping his own destiny.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-15T12:49:32.457000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.349000Z',10),
	(23,'IG-88','15BBY','red','none','200','140','metal','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/IG-88','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/f2/IG-88.png','[]','IG-88 is a deadly assassin droid and bounty hunter. Built for warfare, he developed independent consciousness. Cold and calculating, he lacks empathy or hesitation. His metal frame houses advanced combat systems. IG-88 once hunted Han Solo. His ambition extended beyond bounty hunting.','IG-88 was originally designed as a prototype for assassin droids. Upon activation, he eliminated his creators and began plotting to dominate organic life. He constructed multiple copies of himself to extend his influence. As a bounty hunter, IG-88 earned fear and respect for his brutal efficiency. His red photoreceptors glowed with menace, and his tall metal frame was equipped with deadly weapons. He competed for the bounty on Han Solo during the events of The Empire Strikes Back. IG-88’s logic circuits evolved to a point of self-awareness, with aspirations to overthrow organic rule. He briefly attempted to upload his consciousness into the Death Star. Though ultimately unsuccessful, his legacy remains infamous. His robotic demeanor concealed a strategic mind. IG-88’s approach to targets was methodical and ruthless. He lacked compassion, seeing life as a system to optimize or eliminate. His presence was both eerie and effective. Droids like IG-88 questioned the role of artificial beings in the galaxy. He symbolized the threat of unchecked technology. Built for war, he became a philosopher of extinction. He was one of the few droids to earn a name among flesh-and-blood hunters. Even other bounty hunters feared him. IG-88\'s legacy continues to inspire dread in stories across the galaxy. His metal shell endures in memory as the perfect killer.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-15T12:51:10.076000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.351000Z',28),
	(24,'Bossk','53BBY','red','none','190','113','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Bossk','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/1/1d/Bossk.png','[\"Bounty Hunters\' Guild\",\"Boba Fett\'s syndicate\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Chelli Aphra\'s crew\"]','Bossk is a fearsome Trandoshan bounty hunter. He is known for his reptilian strength and primal instincts. Bossk enjoys hunting Wookiees and rivals alike. He operates with fierce loyalty to the Bounty Hunters\' Guild. His cold demeanor hides a brutal cunning. Bossk’s reputation is built on ferocity and survival.','Bossk was born on the jungle world of Trandosha into a culture that glorified hunting. From early youth, he displayed intense aggression and tracking skills. As a member of the Bounty Hunters\' Guild, Bossk took assignments from various galactic powers, including the Empire. He formed a rivalry with fellow hunter Boba Fett but also worked alongside him during the pursuit of the Millennium Falcon. Bossk’s disdain for Wookiees fueled many of his hunts. His yellow flight suit and sharp teeth made him instantly recognizable. He flew a ship called the Hound\'s Tooth. Despite his viciousness, Bossk operated with a certain code of honor. He was feared for his unrelenting pursuit of targets. Bossk\'s physical strength gave him an edge in close combat. He often tracked prey using a keen sense of smell and instinct. Though not the most diplomatic, he commanded attention. Bossk avoided unnecessary alliances, trusting few. His life as a bounty hunter was one of violence and competition. He participated in several key missions for the Empire. Over time, his legacy became one of intimidation and notoriety. Many stories about Bossk circulate in cantinas across the galaxy. He remained active for decades. Bossk exemplifies the brutal effectiveness of Trandoshan hunters. His legacy persists through fear and survivalism.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-15T12:53:49.297000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.355000Z',29),
	(25,'Lando Calrissian','31BBY','brown','black','177','79','dark','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Lando_Calrissian','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/8/8f/Lando_ROTJ.png','[\"Cloud City colony\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Gold Squadron\",\"New Republic\",\"New Republic military\",\"Uprising\",\"Calrissian Enterprises\"]','Lando Calrissian is a charming and cunning businessman with a history as a gambler. He once governed Cloud City and reluctantly became a hero of the Rebellion. Despite betraying Han Solo, he ultimately proved his loyalty. Lando is skilled in negotiation, manipulation, and survival. He has served as a capable pilot, including commanding the Millennium Falcon. His journey from rogue to general in the Rebel Alliance is legendary.','Lando Calrissian was born on the planet Socorro and began his career as a gambler and entrepreneur. Known for his charm and style, he quickly made a name for himself throughout the galaxy. He famously won the Millennium Falcon from Han Solo in a game of sabacc. With the ship, he embarked on various ventures and built a reputation in the underworld. Eventually, he became the administrator of Cloud City, trying to live a legitimate life. When Darth Vader forced him into betraying Han Solo, Lando did so to protect his city. Soon after, he regretted his actions and helped rescue Leia and Chewbacca. He joined the Rebel Alliance and quickly became a key figure in their operations. At the Battle of Endor, he led the assault on the second Death Star and destroyed its reactor. Lando proved himself a capable military leader despite lacking formal training. After the Empire\'s fall, he continued as an entrepreneur and diplomat in the New Republic. He later supported the Resistance against the First Order, offering his wisdom and experience. His bond with Han Solo deepened, built on forgiveness and mutual respect. Lando often operated in morally grey areas, guided by survival and loyalty. His sophistication, from attire to language, became his signature. Though once a scoundrel, he is remembered as a man of honor and principle. He often reunited with old friends during galactic crises, taking on leadership roles. His charisma made him a natural leader and an inspiration to many. He remains an icon of the Rebellion and a beloved figure throughout the galaxy. Lando Calrissian is proof that heroism can come from unexpected places.','light',NULL,'2014-12-15T12:56:32.683000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.357000Z',30),
	(26,'Lobot','37BBY','blue','none','175','79','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Lobot','https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/72/Lobot-SWE.png','[\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Military\",\"Cloud City\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"New Republic\"]','Lobot was a loyal aide to Lando Calrissian on Cloud City. He was enhanced with a cybernetic interface, linking him directly to the city’s computer systems. Though silent, Lobot’s actions were swift and decisive. He helped Lando in the escape from Imperial control. His loyalty was unshakable even under great risk. Lobot symbolizes quiet strength and technical precision.','Lobot served as the chief administrative aide and operations manager of Cloud City on Bespin. Fitted with a unique cybernetic implant called the AJ^6 cyborg construct, Lobot could interface directly with the city’s central computer systems. This connection gave him unmatched efficiency and awareness, but also diminished his ability to express emotion or speak freely. Lobot was trusted deeply by Baron Administrator Lando Calrissian and worked diligently to maintain the city’s smooth operations. When the Empire arrived to take control of Cloud City, Lobot remained outwardly passive. Secretly, he coordinated with Lando to assist Leia, Chewbacca, and the others in their escape. His role was essential in turning the tide against Imperial occupation, despite the great personal risk. Calm and efficient, Lobot used his connection to shut down systems and open routes during the crisis. He didn’t speak, but his loyalty was evident in every action. Though often overlooked, he was a vital figure in the Rebellion’s success at that moment. After the events at Cloud City, Lobot continued to serve Lando in various capacities. His legacy lives in his quiet resolve and deep loyalty. Lobot’s story is one of sacrifice without words, duty without reward. He stands as a symbol of unspoken resistance and cybernetic precision.','light',NULL,'2014-12-15T13:01:57.178000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.359000Z',6),
	(27,'Ackbar','41BBY','orange','none','180','83','brown mottle','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Gial_Ackbar','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/2/29/Admiral_Ackbar_RH.png','[\"Mon Cala monarchy\",\"Mon Calamari Guard\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Alliance Fleet\",\"Alliance High Command\",\"New Republic\",\"New Republic Defense Fleet\",\"Resistance\",\"Resistance High Command\",\"Resistance Fleet Command\",\"Resistance navy\"]','Ackbar was a Mon Calamari admiral and master tactician in the Rebel Alliance. He famously led the space assault during the Battle of Endor. His strategic mind helped secure major victories against the Empire. He coined the iconic warning, \'It’s a trap!\' during the battle. Ackbar later served the Resistance in its struggle against the First Order. His leadership and legacy remain symbols of loyalty and wisdom.','Ackbar was born on the oceanic world of Mon Cala and rose through the ranks as a naval strategist. He became a respected leader among the Mon Calamari during the Clone Wars. When the Empire occupied his homeworld, he was captured and enslaved. After being rescued by the Rebellion, Ackbar pledged his service to the cause. He brought strategic brilliance to the Alliance\'s fleet operations. As a key planner, he organized defensive and offensive maneuvers against overwhelming odds. During the Battle of Endor, Ackbar led the Rebel fleet against the Imperial armada. It was his swift call—\'It’s a trap!\'—that warned the fleet of the Emperor\'s deception. Under fire, he remained composed and directed the fleet to victory. His leadership helped destroy the second Death Star. In the years that followed, Ackbar continued serving with distinction. He advised the New Republic during its formative era. When the First Order emerged, Leia Organa called him back to active duty. Ackbar commanded Resistance fleets in battles across the galaxy. He remained firm, tactical, and unwavering even in moments of crisis. During the evacuation of D\'Qar, his ship was ambushed. Ackbar was killed when the bridge was destroyed. His death was mourned throughout the Resistance. Ackbar’s name is remembered with honor among pilots and officers. He symbolized intelligence, calm, and unwavering dedication.','light',NULL,'2014-12-18T11:07:50.584000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.362000Z',31),
	(28,'Mon Mothma','48BBY','blue','auburn','150','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Mon_Mothma','https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/e3/MonMothma19BBY-SWE.png','[\"Galactic Republic\",\"Loyalist Committee\",\"Delegation of 2,000\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Senate\",\"Mon Mothma\'s rebel cell\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"New Republic\"]','Mon Mothma was a senator and co-founder of the Rebel Alliance. Known for her calm authority, she opposed Palpatine’s rise to power. She risked everything to unite systems against tyranny. Mothma served as a voice of justice when few dared speak. Her leadership guided the Rebellion through its darkest hours. Mon Mothma represents political courage and unwavering integrity.','Mon Mothma was born into a prestigious family on Chandrila and quickly rose through the political ranks of the Galactic Republic. As a senator, she gained a reputation for integrity, diplomacy, and resistance to authoritarianism. When Chancellor Palpatine declared himself Emperor, Mothma became one of the first to openly oppose his rule. She worked alongside Bail Organa and Padmé Amidala to form a united front against the erosion of democracy. Her dissent forced her into hiding, where she co-founded the Alliance to Restore the Republic. Mothma delivered the Declaration of Rebellion, officially beginning the Rebel cause. She became the Alliance’s civilian leader, overseeing its strategy and governance. While not a warrior, her resolve and moral compass were essential in uniting disparate systems. Mothma maintained order and diplomacy even as the Rebellion faced insurmountable odds. After the destruction of Alderaan, she provided a steady hand amid panic. Her leadership enabled the Rebellion to survive major battles like Scarif and Endor. Following the fall of the Empire, Mothma became the first Chancellor of the New Republic. She dismantled the Imperial war machine and advocated for peace. Her ideals shaped a new age of governance. Mon Mothma’s legacy is one of hope, resistance, and ethical leadership. She remains a guiding light in the fight for freedom across the galaxy.','light',NULL,'2014-12-18T11:12:38.895000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.364000Z',32),
	(29,'Arvel Crynyd','unknown','brown','brown','unknown','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Arvel_Crynyd','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/d/de/Arvel-crynyd.jpg','[\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Green Squadron\"]','Arvel Crynyd was a fearless A-wing pilot and commander in the Rebel Alliance. He flew in the Battle of Endor against the Imperial fleet. When his fighter was damaged, he made a split-second decision. Crynyd crashed his A-wing into the Executor’s bridge, destroying the Empire’s flagship. His sacrifice turned the tide of the battle. He is remembered as a selfless hero of the Rebellion.','Arvel Crynyd was a skilled pilot known for his precision and courage. He rose through the ranks of the Rebel Alliance’s starfighter corps. Assigned to Green Squadron, he trained intensively for the decisive assault on Endor. The battle was fierce, with the Executor unleashing devastating firepower. Crynyd’s A-wing sustained critical damage in the crossfire. Recognizing his fighter was beyond saving, he aimed directly at the Executor’s bridge. The impact destroyed the command structure and sent the ship spiraling into the Death Star. This single act of bravery helped cripple the Empire’s fleet. His death was immediate, but his legacy immense. Crynyd\'s sacrifice became legendary among pilots. Many considered it the ultimate act of valor. Rebel leaders honored his decision and recorded his story across the fleet. His name is etched on memorial walls from Endor to Chandrila. Instructors use his mission to teach duty and courage in academy simulations. Crynyd was known among his peers for being quiet but determined. He believed the cause was worth his life. His family received full honors after the war. His bravery is immortalized in Rebel archives. To this day, Arvel Crynyd remains a model of sacrifice and impact.','light',NULL,'2014-12-18T11:16:33.020000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.367000Z',28),
	(30,'Wicket Systri Warrick','8BBY','brown','brown','88','20','brown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Wicket_W._Warrick','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/4f/Wicket_RotJ.png','[\"Bright Tree tribe\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\"]','Wicket Systri Warrick was a brave and clever Ewok from Endor’s forest moon. He encountered Princess Leia and helped bridge trust between the Ewoks and the Rebellion. Wicket played a major role in the Battle of Endor. Using simple tools and traps, he helped fight Imperial walkers and stormtroopers. Despite his small size, he showed immense courage. Wicket’s actions helped secure freedom for his people and the galaxy.','Wicket Systri Warrick was a young Ewok when the Rebellion arrived on Endor. His first contact with Princess Leia sparked a unique alliance. Though cautious, he led her to his village and showed her kindness. Wicket helped convince his elders that the Rebels were allies, not enemies. He quickly grew curious about their advanced technology. As the Empire\'s presence loomed, Wicket stood ready to defend his home. With slings, logs, and nets, he and his tribe devised traps. On the day of battle, he fought beside Han Solo and Chewbacca. Wicket darted through enemy lines, using his size to evade capture. He disabled troopers, sabotaged walkers, and rallied his friends. His courage was evident despite the danger. He showed that unity and spirit can overcome machines. When the Death Star was destroyed, Wicket celebrated under the stars. He danced with Leia, proud of what they achieved together. Later, he became a leader among the Ewoks. He told stories of rebellion and honor to young warriors. Wicket believed in peace but never forgot the cost of it. He became a symbol of strength in simplicity. Endor flourished, and Wicket’s legacy lived in the leaves and song. His heart was always with his people and their freedom.','light',NULL,'2014-12-18T11:21:58.954000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.369000Z',7),
	(31,'Nien Nunb','unknown','black','none','160','68','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Nien_Nunb','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/1/14/Old_nien_nunb_-_profile.png','[\"House of Organa\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Gold Squadron\",\"New Republic\",\"Resistance\",\"Red Squadron\"]','Nien Nunb was a skilled Sullustan pilot and loyal ally to the Rebellion. He co-piloted the Millennium Falcon during the Battle of Endor. With Lando Calrissian, he helped destroy the second Death Star. Nien’s calm under fire and quick reflexes saved lives. He later joined the Resistance against the First Order. His service spanned decades of galactic struggle and hope.','Nien Nunb was born on the volcanic world of Sullust. As a smuggler, he learned to navigate dangerous routes with precision. His talents caught the attention of Rebel operatives. He quickly became a trusted pilot and intelligence source. Fluent in multiple languages, he was comfortable among diverse crews. His most iconic mission came at Endor, where he co-piloted the Millennium Falcon. Nien remained composed as they flew into the Death Star\'s core. He reacted quickly to threats and adjusted systems mid-flight. He and Lando fired the shot that destroyed the reactor. They escaped in a burst of flame as the station exploded. Nien celebrated with allies under the forest moon. In the New Republic, he continued flying and training young pilots. He answered Leia’s call when the Resistance formed. He fought bravely at Starkiller Base and other battles. He was aboard a Resistance cruiser during key evacuations. Nien stayed loyal through hardship, never backing down. He died in the final battle at Exegol. His loss was felt deeply by all who knew him. His name is honored in Resistance records. Nien Nunb’s legacy is that of skill, bravery, and unwavering commitment to freedom.','light',NULL,'2014-12-18T11:26:18.541000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.371000Z',33),
	(32,'Qui-Gon Jinn','92BBY','blue','brown','193','89','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Qui-Gon_Jinn','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/f6/Qui-Gon_Jinn_Headshot_TPM.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Qui-Gon Jinn was a wise and independent Jedi Master. Known for following the living Force, he often defied the Jedi Council. He discovered Anakin Skywalker and believed he was the Chosen One. Qui-Gon trained Obi-Wan Kenobi with patience and strength. He was killed by Darth Maul on Naboo. His teachings and vision shaped the Jedi for years to come.','Qui-Gon Jinn was a Jedi Master known for his deep connection to the living Force. He often acted on instinct, even if it meant opposing the Jedi Council. He believed in prophecy and the will of the Force above rules and tradition. Qui-Gon took Obi-Wan Kenobi as his Padawan and trained him with compassion and discipline. During a mission to Naboo, he encountered a boy named Anakin Skywalker. Sensing great power in the child, he believed Anakin was the Chosen One. Despite Council doubts, Qui-Gon advocated for Anakin’s training. On Naboo, he fought the Sith Lord Darth Maul in a brutal duel. Though skilled, Qui-Gon was fatally struck. His final wish was for Obi-Wan to train Anakin. After death, Qui-Gon became the first Jedi to retain consciousness through the Force. His discovery of immortality altered Jedi teachings. Yoda later learned from his spirit in exile. Qui-Gon’s legacy lived on through Obi-Wan, Anakin, and eventually Luke. His defiance of doctrine made him a rare visionary. He valued balance over control, compassion over dogma. Though his life ended early, his influence grew over time. Qui-Gon Jinn’s trust in the Force shaped galactic history. He was mourned by many, honored by few. He walked his own path, guided by belief and destiny.','light','green','2014-12-19T16:54:53.618000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.375000Z',28),
	(33,'Nute Gunray','unknown','red','none','191','90','mottled green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Nute_Gunray','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/fd/Nute_Gunray_SWE.png','[\"Trade Federation\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Separatist Council\"]','Nute Gunray was a Neimoidian viceroy and leader of the Trade Federation. He orchestrated the blockade and invasion of Naboo. Driven by greed, he allied with Darth Sidious. Gunray\'s actions triggered the Clone Wars. He remained a pawn in the Sith’s plan. Eventually, he was betrayed and executed by Darth Vader.','Nute Gunray rose through the ranks of the Trade Federation to become its viceroy. He was cunning, ambitious, and obsessed with profit. Under the secret influence of Darth Sidious, he launched a blockade of Naboo. The crisis was meant to create political chaos in the Republic. Gunray’s forces invaded Naboo, resulting in great suffering. He was captured but avoided punishment through legal maneuvering. Despite his cowardice, he remained in power and joined the Separatist movement. Gunray became a founding member of the Confederacy of Independent Systems. He funded droid armies and fueled the galactic conflict. Throughout the Clone Wars, he remained cautious and self-serving. He distrusted Count Dooku but stayed involved out of fear and greed. Gunray’s ambitions were always undermined by his own cowardice. He hoped to survive the war and profit from its outcome. At the war’s end, he was taken to Mustafar by Darth Sidious. There, he awaited the end of the conflict and a promise of victory. Instead, Darth Vader arrived and killed him without mercy. His death was part of the Sith’s purge of their pawns. Gunray’s legacy was one of manipulation, betrayal, and demise. He helped start the war that destroyed the Republic. But he died as expendable as he had lived.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:05:57.357000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.377000Z',18),
	(34,'Finis Valorum','91BBY','blue','blond','170','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Finis_Valorum','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/5/51/ValorumPortrait-SWE.png','[\"House Valorum\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Senate\"]','Finis Valorum was the last Supreme Chancellor of the Galactic Republic before Palpatine. He tried to balance politics and morality in a corrupt Senate. His leadership was undermined by special interests and manipulation. Valorum ordered a Jedi mission to Naboo. He was ousted in a no-confidence vote. His fall marked the end of Republic idealism.','Finis Valorum came from a respected political lineage in the Galactic Republic. He became Supreme Chancellor during a time of growing corruption. Though idealistic, he struggled to enact meaningful reform. Corporate influence paralyzed the Senate’s decision-making. During the Naboo crisis, he sent Jedi ambassadors to negotiate peace. The Trade Federation ignored him, escalating the conflict. Valorum relied on Queen Amidala’s testimony to rally support. However, Senator Palpatine manipulated the situation. Amidala called for a vote of no confidence. The Senate removed Valorum from office. His downfall cleared the path for Palpatine\'s rise. Valorum spent the rest of his life in quiet exile. He watched democracy crumble from the sidelines. Despite his failures, he truly believed in justice. History judged him as weak, but he was a man of principle. He tried to hold the Republic together amid chaos. His warnings went unheeded. Valorum’s legacy was buried beneath war and tyranny. He was the last chancellor to value peace over power.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:21:45.915000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.379000Z',9),
	(35,'Padmé Amidala','46BBY','brown','brown','185','45','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Padm%C3%A9_Amidala','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/b/b2/Padmegreenscrshot.jpg','[\"Apprentice Legislators\",\"Legislative Youth Program\",\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Loyalist Committee\",\"Delegation of 2,000\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Senate\"]','Padmé Amidala was the queen and later senator of Naboo. She fought for peace, justice, and democracy during the Republic’s final years. Brave and diplomatic, she opposed the rise of the Empire. Padmé secretly married Anakin Skywalker. She died after giving birth to twins, Luke and Leia. Her life shaped the future of the galaxy.','Padmé Amidala became Queen of Naboo as a teenager. She led her people during the Trade Federation invasion. With Jedi aid, she returned to liberate her planet. After her term, she served as senator for Naboo in the Galactic Senate. Padmé was a fierce opponent of corruption and authoritarianism. She supported peace and opposed the creation of the Grand Army. In secret, she fell in love with Anakin Skywalker. The two married quietly, defying Jedi and Senate rules. Padmé remained strong and outspoken even during the Clone Wars. She believed in diplomacy and refused to lose hope. When Anakin began to change, she was terrified. She followed him to Mustafar and begged him to stop. Anakin, consumed by the dark side, choked her in a fit of rage. She survived long enough to give birth to Luke and Leia. Her last words expressed belief that there was still good in Anakin. Padmé died of a broken heart, mourned across the Republic. Her legacy lived on in her children. She symbolized integrity in a collapsing system. Even Palpatine respected her influence. Padmé Amidala’s name became a light in the darkness of the Empire.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:28:26.926000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.381000Z',8),
	(36,'Jar Jar Binks','52BBY','orange','none','196','66','orange','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Jar_Jar_Binks','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/d/d2/Jar_Jar_aotc.jpg','[\"Gungan High Council\",\"Officer corps\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Naboo delegation\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Senate\"]','Jar Jar Binks was a clumsy but well-meaning Gungan from Naboo. He was exiled from his people before befriending the Jedi. Jar Jar became a representative in the Galactic Senate. He unknowingly helped grant emergency powers to Palpatine. Though ridiculed, he remained loyal and kind. His story is one of comic misfortune and deep consequence.','Jar Jar Binks lived in the underwater city of Otoh Gunga on Naboo. His clumsiness led to banishment from his tribe. During the invasion of Naboo, he met Qui-Gon Jinn and Obi-Wan Kenobi. The Jedi saved him, and he returned the favor by guiding them. Jar Jar helped forge peace between the Naboo and the Gungans. He became a general during the Battle of Naboo. His bravery earned him the respect of Boss Nass. Later, he joined Padmé Amidala as her representative. In the Galactic Senate, Jar Jar was out of place but eager to help. During a crisis, he proposed granting Palpatine emergency powers. This action contributed to the rise of the Empire. Many blamed him for the fall of the Republic. After the war, Jar Jar faded from the public eye. He was seen performing as a street clown to entertain children. Sad and ostracized, he accepted his fate. Despite ridicule, Jar Jar was never malicious. He only wished to serve and bring peace. His loyalty to Padmé never wavered. In the end, he became a tragic figure. A fool to some, but always a friend to those in need.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:29:32.489000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.383000Z',8),
	(37,'Roos Tarpals','unknown','orange','none','224','82','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Roos_Tarpals','/images/people/37-roos-tarpals.png','[\"Gungan Grand Army\"]','Roos Tarpals was a captain in the Gungan Grand Army. He helped defend Naboo against the Trade Federation. Brave and disciplined, he led troops into battle. Tarpals believed in unity between Gungans and humans. He later fought General Grievous in a valiant duel. His loyalty to his people never wavered.','Roos Tarpals served as a high-ranking officer in the Gungan Grand Army. He upheld discipline and honor among his troops. When the Trade Federation invaded Naboo, he coordinated with Queen Amidala. Tarpals worked closely with Boss Nass and Jar Jar Binks. During the Battle of Naboo, he led Gungan warriors against the droid army. Using energy shields and bravery, they held their ground. Tarpals commanded the battlefield with courage and clarity. Though outgunned, he inspired his troops to resist. After the war, he remained a guardian of Gungan security. He saw the growing threat of Separatists and prepared for war. During the Clone Wars, he helped defend Naboo again. When General Grievous came to the planet, Tarpals confronted him. He engaged Grievous in personal combat. Though wounded, he fought with everything he had. His sacrifice allowed Republic forces to capture Grievous. Tarpals died with honor, remembered as a Gungan hero. His people mourned him with respect. He proved Gungans could fight with the best. Roos Tarpals earned his place among galactic warriors. His final words were of duty and pride.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:32:56.741000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.385000Z',8),
	(38,'Rugor Nass','unknown','orange','none','206','unknown','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Rugor_Nass','/images/people/38-rugor-nass.webp','[\"Gungan High Council\"]','Rugor Nass was the boss of the Gungan people on Naboo. Initially distrustful of surface dwellers, he valued Gungan independence. He changed after Padmé Amidala sought his help. Nass allied with the Naboo to resist the Trade Federation. His decision helped save the planet. He became a symbol of unity between peoples.','Boss Rugor Nass led the Gungan tribes from their underwater city of Otoh Gunga. He was proud, loud, and fiercely protective of his people’s way of life. Nass distrusted the Naboo and resisted all contact with them. During the crisis of the Trade Federation, Jedi came seeking refuge. Nass initially refused to help. However, Queen Padmé Amidala later approached him directly. Her humility and respect changed Nass’s mind. He agreed to form an alliance to liberate Naboo. Nass appointed Jar Jar Binks as general of the Gungan army. Together, their forces engaged the droid army. Nass watched the battle unfold from the command center. He saw the courage of both Gungans and Naboo. After the victory, he continued to build bridges with surface leaders. Nass served as a symbol of cooperation during the Clone Wars. He helped organize local defenses and preserve Gungan heritage. Though less visible in later years, he remained respected. His legacy was one of peace forged through action. Nass proved that strength could come through unity. His booming voice and booming heart changed history. He is remembered by Gungans as a wise and decisive leader.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:33:38.909000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.388000Z',8),
	(39,'Ric Olié','unknown','blue','brown','183','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Ric_Oli%C3%A9','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/4c/RicOlieHS-SWE.png','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Royal Naboo Security Forces\",\"Bravo Flight\"]','Ric Olié was the chief pilot of Queen Amidala’s royal starship. He guided her ship through dangerous battles and blockades. Skilled and calm, he trained other Naboo pilots. Olié helped evacuate Naboo during the invasion. He served with quiet dedication. His flying saved many lives during the war.','Ric Olié was one of Naboo’s finest pilots and captain of the Queen’s royal starship. He was precise, focused, and trusted by Queen Amidala. When the Trade Federation invaded, Olié evacuated the Queen to Coruscant. During the escape, he flew through a blockade while under heavy fire. He remained composed as droids damaged their systems. After R2-D2 performed emergency repairs, Olié got the ship safely to Tatooine. On Tatooine, he coordinated repairs and kept the Queen protected. Later, he returned to Naboo and supported the battle plans. Though not a soldier, his courage never faltered. He helped organize air support during the counterattack. Olié trained young pilots in Theed’s academy. His voice became familiar in flight briefings. He valued discipline and teamwork. Olié rarely sought praise but earned quiet respect. During the Clone Wars, he continued to serve Naboo’s defenses. He advised both local and Republic forces. In his later years, he mentored future Resistance pilots. Olié’s professionalism became legend among pilots. His name appears in training manuals across the sector.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:45:01.522000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.392000Z',8),
	(40,'Watto','unknown','yellow','black','137','unknown','blue, grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Watto','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/e/eb/WattoHS.jpg','[\"Watto\'s shop\",\"Mos Espa\"]','Watto was a junk dealer on Tatooine and owner of Anakin and Shmi Skywalker. He was greedy, shrewd, and resistant to Jedi mind tricks. Watto prized money and rare parts above all. He lost Anakin in a bet with Qui-Gon Jinn. His dealings tied him to galactic destiny.','Watto was a Toydarian merchant who owned a junk shop in Mos Espa. He purchased Shmi and Anakin Skywalker as slaves before the fall of the Republic. Watto was tough, dismissive, and greedy. He specialized in starship parts and rarely bargained. When Jedi arrived on Tatooine, he refused to be manipulated by the Force. He bet against Qui-Gon Jinn in a podrace wager. Anakin won, and Watto lost his most valuable slave. He was furious but upheld the deal. Watto kept Shmi until she was later bought and freed. Years later, Anakin returned to find her. Watto was older, poorer, and more resigned. He told Anakin what he knew and offered no resistance. Though selfish, he was never overtly cruel. He valued survival above all else. Watto’s shop became dusty and empty over time. He faded into obscurity as the galaxy changed. His early choices indirectly shaped galactic history. Watto remained a relic of an unforgiving world.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:48:54.647000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.395000Z',34),
	(41,'Sebulba','unknown','orange','none','112','40','grey, red','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Sebulba','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/1/14/Sebulba_Headshot_Closeup.png','[]','Sebulba was a Dug podracer known for his aggressive tactics and arrogance. He dominated Tatooine races through sabotage and skill. Sebulba considered Anakin Skywalker a rival. During the Boonta Eve Classic, Anakin defeated him. Sebulba’s reputation suffered, and his fame faded. His legacy was one of speed, pride, and bitter loss.','Sebulba was a podracer from Malastare who made his fortune racing on outer rim circuits. He was known for his violent driving and willingness to cheat. On Tatooine, he was the reigning champion of the Boonta Eve Classic. He viewed Anakin Skywalker with disdain, calling him a slave and a pest. Despite warnings, he underestimated the young pilot. Sebulba used flame jets and dirty tricks to destroy other racers. During the Boonta Eve race, he tried to eliminate Anakin again. This time, Anakin outmaneuvered him and won the race. Sebulba’s podracer was destroyed in the crash. He stormed off, embarrassed and furious. His defeat marked the end of his dominance. Sponsors began to drop him. Though he continued to race, he never regained his status. Sebulba blamed others for his failure. His pride became his downfall. He lived bitterly on winnings from past glories. Stories of his cruelty and rage circulated in Mos Espa. Eventually, Sebulba was replaced by newer, fairer racers. He remains a cautionary tale in podracing history.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:53:02.586000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.397000Z',35),
	(42,'Quarsh Panaka','62BBY','brown','black','183','unknown','dark','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Quarsh_Panaka','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/72/PanakaHS-TPM.png','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Royal Naboo Security Forces\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Republic Special Task Force\",\"Galactic Empire\"]','Quarsh Panaka was the head of security for Queen Amidala on Naboo. He was loyal, cautious, and deeply protective of his queen. During the invasion, he helped orchestrate her escape. Panaka distrusted the Jedi but cooperated with them. He remained a patriot to Naboo throughout his life. Eventually, he aligned with the Empire out of belief in order.','Captain Quarsh Panaka was a dedicated officer in the Royal Naboo Security Forces. He served as Queen Padmé Amidala’s head of security during a time of crisis. When the Trade Federation blockaded Naboo, Panaka helped plan her escape. He traveled with her to Coruscant, skeptical of Jedi involvement. Despite his mistrust, he supported their mission to liberate Naboo. On her return, Panaka fought alongside Gungans and coordinated palace infiltration. His loyalty and organization were vital to Naboo’s liberation. Panaka’s commitment to law and order shaped his later years. After the Republic fell, he became an Imperial Moff. He believed the Empire could protect Naboo from future threats. Though controversial, his actions stemmed from duty. He never abandoned his homeworld. His efforts helped preserve Naboo’s political influence. Panaka’s sense of discipline inspired future leaders. His arc represents the complex choices of good men in dark times. Though often overshadowed, his presence left a mark on galactic history. His role in Amidala’s safety changed the course of the Republic. Without Panaka’s foresight, Naboo’s resistance may have failed. He remains a symbol of patriotic service and loyalty.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:55:43.348000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.399000Z',8),
	(43,'Shmi Skywalker','72BBY','brown','black','163','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Shmi_Skywalker_Lars','/images/people/43-shmi-skywalker.webp','[\"Skywalker family\",\"Lars family\"]','Shmi Skywalker was the mother of Anakin Skywalker. She lived as a slave on Tatooine, raising her son with love and hope. Shmi believed in Anakin’s destiny and goodness. She let him go to become a Jedi, though it broke her heart. Years later, she was captured by Tusken Raiders. Her death deeply affected Anakin’s path.','Shmi Skywalker lived on Tatooine, enslaved by Watto. Despite her hardship, she remained kind and resilient. She gave birth to Anakin, whose father was unknown. Shmi believed Anakin was special and raised him with care. She encouraged his dreams, even in their desperate situation. When Jedi visited Tatooine, she allowed Anakin to leave with Qui-Gon. It was the hardest decision of her life, driven by love. She stayed behind, hoping for freedom one day. Years passed, and she was purchased by Cliegg Lars. They fell in love, and she became part of his family. Tragically, she was abducted by Tusken Raiders. Anakin found her too late, and she died in his arms. Her death triggered Anakin’s first fall into darkness. Shmi\'s love shaped the Jedi who would later bring balance. Her memory haunted Anakin, influencing his fate. Her story is one of quiet sacrifice and maternal strength. Though never a warrior, she changed the galaxy. She gave birth to the Chosen One. She remains a tragic, powerful presence in the Skywalker saga.','light',NULL,'2014-12-19T17:57:41.191000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.401000Z',1),
	(44,'Darth Maul','54BBY','yellow','none','175','80','red','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Darth_Maul','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/5/50/Darth_Maul_profile.png','[\"Nightbrothers\",\"Sith\",\"Cad Bane\'s group\",\"Death Watch\",\"Shadow Collective\"]','Darth Maul was a Sith warrior trained by Darth Sidious. With a double-bladed lightsaber, he struck fear into Jedi and foes alike. He killed Qui-Gon Jinn but was defeated by Obi-Wan Kenobi. Maul survived and returned with vengeance. Consumed by hatred, he carved his own path in the shadows. He died trying to destroy the legacy of the Jedi.','Darth Maul was born on Dathomir and taken by Darth Sidious as a child. Raised in hatred, he became a Sith assassin trained in the dark arts. He was sent to kill the Jedi during the Naboo crisis. Maul faced Obi-Wan and Qui-Gon Jinn in a legendary duel. He killed Qui-Gon but was sliced in half by Obi-Wan. Thought dead, Maul survived through sheer rage. He built mechanical legs and went into hiding. Fueled by vengeance, he returned during the Clone Wars. He seized control of criminal syndicates, including the Shadow Collective. Maul overthrew Mandalore’s government and ruled from the shadows. He desired revenge against Obi-Wan above all else. Their final duel on Tatooine ended in Maul’s death. Despite his failures, he challenged both Sith and Jedi orders. His story was one of obsession and loss. Maul never escaped the pain of betrayal and abandonment. He fell again and again but always rose with hatred. His life was a lesson in the destructive power of vengeance. Even in death, Maul longed for peace he never found.','dark','red','2014-12-19T18:00:41.929000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.403000Z',36),
	(45,'Bib Fortuna','unknown','pink','none','180','unknown','pale','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Bib_Fortuna','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/33/BibFortunaHS-ROTJ.png','[\"Fortuna family\",\"Jabba Desilijic Tiure\'s criminal empire\"]','Bib Fortuna was a sly Twi’lek and the loyal majordomo of Jabba the Hutt. He controlled access to the crime lord’s court on Tatooine. Known for his whispery voice and manipulative manner, he survived by serving power. After Jabba’s death, Bib took over his palace. He ruled briefly before being killed by Boba Fett. His ambition ended in betrayal and silence.','Bib Fortuna was born on Ryloth and entered service with Jabba the Hutt as a majordomo. He managed access to Jabba’s throne room and enforced his master’s will. Fortuna developed a reputation for scheming behind Jabba’s back while outwardly remaining loyal. He greeted visitors with veiled threats and calculated charm. During Leia Organa’s attempt to rescue Han Solo, Bib played his part in maintaining Jabba’s grip on power. He was present at Jabba’s sail barge when the Hutt was killed. Surviving the chaos, Bib returned to Jabba’s palace and claimed it for himself. He became the new ruler, though lacked the charisma and dominance of his predecessor. His rule was short-lived and marked by instability. Eventually, Boba Fett returned to Tatooine and assassinated him. Fortuna died on the throne he had coveted for years. His ambition was never matched by strength. Bib is remembered as a schemer who lived and died in the shadow of greater powers. His fate was sealed by the very world he tried to control.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-20T09:47:02.512000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.407000Z',37),
	(46,'Ayla Secura','48BBY','hazel','none','178','55','blue','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Aayla_Secura/Legends','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/f/f9/Aayla.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Aayla Secura was a blue-skinned Twi’lek Jedi Knight known for her grace and resolve. She served as a general in the Clone Wars. Aayla fought bravely in numerous battles across the galaxy. She was betrayed and killed during Order 66. Her death was sudden and without honor. Her legacy endures through stories of Jedi valor.','Aayla Secura was born on Ryloth and brought to the Jedi Temple at a young age. She trained under Jedi Master Quinlan Vos and quickly demonstrated skill with the Force. She earned a reputation for poise, agility, and calm under pressure. When the Clone Wars erupted, she became a Jedi General. Aayla led troops in fierce engagements across many worlds, including Felucia and Geonosis. She was admired for her compassion toward clone troopers. Despite the constant combat, she remained committed to Jedi ideals. On Felucia, her leadership helped maintain control in a volatile environment. But during Order 66, her loyal troops turned against her. As she walked through the jungle, they opened fire without warning. Aayla was killed instantly, her body left behind. Her death marked another tragic loss for the Jedi Order. She was later honored in Jedi memorial records. Aayla’s story reflects the courage and sacrifice of the Jedi during the war. She never sought fame, only peace. Her legacy lived on in the memories of those who served with her.','light','blue','2014-12-20T09:48:01.172000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.409000Z',37),
	(47,'Ratts Tyerel','unknown','unknown','none','79','15','grey, blue','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Ratts_Tyerell','/images/people/47-ratts-tyerel.png','[]','Ratts Tyerel was a small Aleena podracer from Aleen. He competed in the Boonta Eve Classic on Tatooine. Despite his size, he was fast and daring. He tragically died when his podracer exploded during the race. His death shocked spectators and racers alike. Ratts is remembered for his spirit and speed.','Ratts Tyerel came from the planet Aleen, known for its deep canyons and compact species. He entered the dangerous world of podracing for fame and excitement. Ratts quickly gained popularity for his agility and courage. He modified his podracer to compensate for his small size. During the Boonta Eve Classic, he started strong, weaving between larger rivals. Unfortunately, a mechanical failure caused a critical destabilization. His podracer veered off course and crashed violently. Ratts died instantly in the explosion. The crowd was shocked by the sudden tragedy. Though his career ended in disaster, his bravery left a lasting impression. Fellow racers honored him after the event. Ratts became a symbol of passion and risk-taking. His story was later told in podracing circles and youth holo-vids. On Aleen, his people mourned him as a fallen champion.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T09:53:15.086000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.410000Z',38),
	(48,'Dud Bolt','unknown','yellow','none','94','45','blue, grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Dud_Bolt','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/73/Dud_Bolt_Podracer_Cockpit.png','[]','Dud Bolt was a podracer from the planet Vulpter. He competed in the Boonta Eve Classic with aggressive flair. His small stature and fierce style made him a dangerous racer. Dud’s podracer was fast but hard to control. He crashed during the race and failed to finish. He remains a lesser-known but feared name in podracing history.','Dud Bolt was a native of Vulpter, a planet known for its harsh urban landscapes. He entered the podracing circuit to seek fortune and fame. Dud’s podracer was compact and dangerously unstable, reflecting his reckless personality. He gained a reputation for bumping opponents mid-race. When he joined the Boonta Eve Classic, many feared his unpredictability. Early in the race, he darted between engines with tight turns. However, his aggression caused his podracer to spiral into an unstable maneuver. He lost control during a high-speed curve and crashed into the canyon wall. Though he survived, his racer was totaled, ending his chance at victory. The crowd had mixed reactions—disappointment and awe. He disappeared from major events after the race. Dud Bolt\'s name still circulates among fans as a symbol of dangerous showmanship. While never a champion, his style left a mark. His career served as a warning to future racers who valued spectacle over control.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T09:57:31.858000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.414000Z',39),
	(49,'Gasgano','unknown','black','none','122','unknown','white, blue','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Gasgano','/images/people/49-gasgano.webp','[]','Gasgano was a multi-limbed Xexto podracer with an eye for speed and showmanship. He competed in the Boonta Eve Classic on Tatooine. Agile and flashy, he quickly became a crowd favorite. He fought fiercely for a podium finish. Ultimately, he was defeated by Anakin Skywalker. His skill remains respected among podracing fans.','Gasgano was born on Troiken and belonged to the Xexto species, known for their multiple arms and rapid reflexes. He quickly found his niche in podracing and became known for style and speed. His custom-built podracer was sleek and fast, perfectly suited to his physiology. Gasgano was confident entering the Boonta Eve Classic, considering himself a favorite to win. He began the race with a strong lead, impressing fans with daring passes. Gasgano dodged debris and fended off attacks from rival racers like Sebulba. However, he was caught off guard by Anakin Skywalker\'s surge in the final lap. Despite maintaining high speed, he lost first place to the young slave. Still, Gasgano secured a top finish and earned praise for sportsmanship. After the race, he continued competing in circuits across the Outer Rim. His name appeared in betting circles and holo-vid promotions. Gasgano inspired young racers on Troiken and beyond. He became a symbol of podracing excellence without needing to win every race. His flashy entrances and vibrant podracer were legendary. Gasgano retired with honor and remains a fan favorite.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T10:02:12.223000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.416000Z',40),
	(50,'Ben Quadinaros','unknown','orange','none','163','65','grey, green, yellow','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Ben_Quadinaros','/images/people/50-ben-quadinaros.png','[]','Ben Quadinaros was a Toong podracer known more for failure than speed. He entered the Boonta Eve Classic but never left the starting line. A systems malfunction caused his engines to explode. Though embarrassing, he became a cult icon. Ben’s story became one of perseverance. His fame lives on in podracing culture.','Ben Quadinaros came from the cold world of Tund. Eager to prove himself, he entered the Boonta Eve Classic on Tatooine. His podracer had four engines and promised raw power. However, Ben struggled with coordination and technical issues. At the starting line, he waved nervously, full of hope. As the race began, his podracer failed to launch. Moments later, his engines malfunctioned and violently exploded, sending parts flying. The crowd was stunned, and Ben was left humiliated. Despite the failure, he laughed it off and walked away unharmed. Ben’s attitude made him an underdog hero. He became a legend not for winning but for enduring. Podracing fans embraced his misfortune as part of the sport’s drama. Merchandise with his face appeared across booths and markets. Children cheered his name for fun. Ben never raced again but toured as a speaker and guest. His optimism earned him admiration. He is now a symbol of resilience and comic charm in galactic racing lore.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T10:08:33.777000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.417000Z',41),
	(51,'Mace Windu','72BBY','brown','none','188','84','dark','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Mace_Windu','/images/people/51-mace-windu.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Mace Windu\'s squad\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Mace Windu was a powerful Jedi Master and member of the Jedi High Council. Known for his unique purple lightsaber, he was a fierce warrior. He played a critical role in the Clone Wars. Windu distrusted Chancellor Palpatine and sought to remove him. During the arrest, he was betrayed by Anakin Skywalker. Mace fell to his death, marking a turning point for the galaxy.','Mace Windu was born on Haruun Kal and trained as a Jedi from a young age. He became known for his mastery of Vaapad, a lightsaber form channeling darkness without succumbing to it. He rose quickly within the Jedi Order and was appointed to the High Council. Windu was often the voice of strict adherence to Jedi principles. During the Clone Wars, he served as a general and strategist. His leadership was marked by precision and unwavering resolve. Windu participated in key battles, including the rescue at Geonosis. He personally struck down Jango Fett during the arena conflict. As the war progressed, Windu became increasingly wary of Chancellor Palpatine’s power. He uncovered Palpatine\'s identity as Darth Sidious. Leading a small group, he attempted to arrest the Sith Lord. In the ensuing duel, he defeated Palpatine but was stopped by Anakin Skywalker. Anakin’s betrayal led to Windu\'s arm being severed. He was thrown from the window by a surge of Force lightning. His death catalyzed Anakin’s fall and the Jedi Order’s destruction. Mace Windu’s legacy endures through his unbending courage and tragic end.','light','purple','2014-12-20T10:12:30.846000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.420000Z',42),
	(52,'Ki-Adi-Mundi','92BBY','yellow','white','198','82','pale','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Ki-Adi-Mundi','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/9/9e/KiAdiMundi.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Marines\"]','Ki-Adi-Mundi was a Cerean Jedi Master on the Jedi High Council. He served as a general during the Clone Wars. Known for his calm intellect, he guided many Jedi. He led troops on Mygeeto and fought bravely. During Order 66, his soldiers turned on him. Ki-Adi-Mundi fell in battle, a victim of betrayal.','Ki-Adi-Mundi came from the planet Cerea and had a naturally high intellect. He joined the Jedi Order and was one of the few with permission to marry, due to his species\' low population. He was chosen to serve on the Jedi High Council. Mundi’s deep voice and logical mind made him a respected figure. He fought bravely during the Clone Wars, taking part in missions on Geonosis, Hypori, and Mygeeto. He commanded clone troops with discipline. Though loyal to the Jedi cause, he also struggled with political decisions during the war. On Mygeeto, he led a battle during the final days of the conflict. As he charged into combat, Order 66 was issued. His clone troopers turned and opened fire on him. Despite deflecting several shots, he was overwhelmed. Ki-Adi-Mundi fell on the battlefield, unaware of the full betrayal. His death was one of many losses that marked the Jedi\'s tragic end. He is remembered for his wisdom, dedication, and honor in the face of death.','light','blue','2014-12-20T10:15:32.293000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.422000Z',43),
	(53,'Kit Fisto','unknown','black','none','196','87','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Kit_Fisto','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/4c/Kit_Fisto_Card_Trader.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Mace Windu\'s squad\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Kit Fisto was a Nautolan Jedi Master known for his smile and aquatic skill. He served valiantly in the Clone Wars. Kit fought in numerous battles, including Mon Cala and Geonosis. He was skilled with a lightsaber and the Force. During an attempt to arrest Palpatine, he was slain. His bravery lives on in Jedi memory.','Kit Fisto was born on the water world of Glee Anselm and brought to the Jedi Temple as a child. His species’ amphibious nature gave him advantages in aquatic missions. Kit rose through the ranks as a calm, joyful warrior. He developed a strong bond with his Padawan, Nahdar Vebb. Fisto led missions during the Clone Wars, including the campaign on Mon Cala. He also helped in the Battle of Geonosis. Known for his cheerful disposition, he maintained morale even in dire circumstances. Fisto worked closely with clones and fellow Jedi. He investigated General Grievous’ lair and witnessed many horrors of war. When Anakin Skywalker revealed Palpatine\'s true identity, Fisto joined the arrest party. Despite his skill, Palpatine killed him swiftly. His death was sudden but honorable. Fisto’s courage underlined the Jedi’s desperate final stand. His memory endures as one of the Order’s most optimistic and skilled warriors. Few Jedi could balance joy and discipline as he did. Kit Fisto remains a beloved figure in Jedi lore.','light','green','2014-12-20T10:18:57.202000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.424000Z',44),
	(54,'Eeth Koth','unknown','brown','black','171','unknown','brown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Eeth_Koth','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/4/4e/EethKothCardTrader.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Eeth Koth was a Zabrak Jedi Master known for his resilience. He served on the Jedi High Council during the Republic’s final years. Eeth survived severe injuries in battle and returned to serve. He fought General Grievous and was taken captive. Though he escaped, he later left the Order. Eeth was eventually hunted down by Darth Vader.','Eeth Koth was born on Iridonia and trained as a Jedi from early childhood. His species\' pain tolerance helped him survive wounds that would defeat others. As a member of the Jedi High Council, Koth was known for stern integrity. During the Clone Wars, he was captured by General Grievous during a brutal confrontation. His capture was broadcast by the Separatists as a warning. Koth endured torture but used the Force to send a message for rescue. He was saved by Jedi comrades and returned to duty. Later, disillusioned by the war and its consequences, he left the Jedi Order. He started a new life as a priest and began a family. But the Empire eventually hunted him down. Darth Vader confronted Koth and killed him in front of his family. His final moments were filled with sorrow and bravery. Koth’s life reflects the heavy toll the Clone Wars took on many Jedi. He is remembered for his strength and tragic end.','light','green','2014-12-20T10:26:47.902000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.427000Z',45),
	(55,'Adi Gallia','unknown','blue','none','184','50','dark','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Adi_Gallia','/images/people/55-adi-gallia.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Adi Gallia was a Tholothian Jedi Master and expert diplomat. She served on the Jedi High Council and participated in the Clone Wars. Adi was skilled with a lightsaber and the Force. She faced Darth Maul in battle but was slain. Her death was mourned across the Jedi Order. Adi remains a symbol of strength and justice.','Adi Gallia was born into a diplomatic family and brought to the Jedi Temple for training. Her calm demeanor and strategic mind earned her a place on the Jedi High Council. Gallia worked closely with Master Mace Windu and other council members. She became a general in the Clone Wars, leading campaigns across the galaxy. Adi developed a rivalry with the Sith brothers Darth Maul and Savage Opress. In a critical mission on Florrum, she confronted the two alone. Though skilled, she was overpowered and killed by Savage. Her death deeply affected her allies, especially Obi-Wan Kenobi. Gallia had previously served in the Stark Hyperspace War and was a veteran of many crises. She guided Jedi politics with reason and compassion. Her loss was a blow to both the Order and the Republic. Adi Gallia’s legacy is that of courage, wisdom, and grace under pressure. She fought to protect peace and never wavered in duty. Her name is honored in the Jedi archives.','light','blue','2014-12-20T10:29:11.661000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.432000Z',9),
	(56,'Saesee Tiin','unknown','orange','none','188','unknown','pale','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Saesee_Tiin','/images/people/56-saesee-tiin.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Saesee Tiin was a powerful Iktotchi Jedi Master with telepathic abilities. He served on the Jedi High Council. Known for his piloting skill, he often led space combat missions. Tiin helped arrest Chancellor Palpatine. He was swiftly killed in the encounter. His death marked the Jedi Order’s darkest hour.','Saesee Tiin hailed from the moon Iktotch, where Force sensitivity was common. His telepathic skills gave him deep insight into others’ thoughts and motives. As a Jedi, he earned a reputation for wisdom and silence. Tiin was an exceptional pilot, commanding starfighters in dangerous battles. He served with distinction during the Clone Wars. The Jedi Council relied on his tactical abilities in space warfare. During the final days of the Republic, Tiin was selected to help arrest Palpatine. He entered the Chancellor’s office with Windu, Fisto, and Kolar. But Palpatine struck with terrifying speed. Saesee Tiin was killed almost instantly. His death shocked the Order and signaled the rise of the Sith. Though quiet in life, his contributions were immense. Tiin’s service in battle saved countless lives. He remains a figure of strength and serenity. His legacy is remembered by Jedi historians and military strategists alike.','light','green','2014-12-20T10:32:11.669000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.434000Z',47),
	(57,'Yarael Poof','unknown','yellow','none','264','unknown','white','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Yarael_Poof','/images/people/57-yarael-poof.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Yarael Poof was a long-necked Jedi Master from Quermia. He served on the Jedi High Council before the Clone Wars. Known for his deep wisdom and Force abilities, he was respected by peers. Poof often acted behind the scenes, diffusing threats quietly. He died stopping a terrorist threat on Coruscant. His sacrifice went largely unnoticed but saved millions.','Yarael Poof was a member of the long-lived Quermian species and a master of mind tricks and illusions. His appearance was striking, with a tall frame and elongated neck. Poof served on the Jedi High Council for many years. He rarely spoke but was highly perceptive. Poof preferred to resolve conflicts without violence. During a secret mission, he confronted a terrorist planning to detonate a deadly weapon on Coruscant. He successfully neutralized the threat but was mortally wounded in the process. His death was not widely known at the time. Many Jedi believed he had quietly taken on a dangerous burden. His actions prevented mass civilian casualties. Yarael Poof’s humility defined his life and his death. Though not a warrior, his contribution was immeasurable. The Jedi Order honored him with quiet reverence. He remains a symbol of quiet power and hidden strength.','light','blue','2014-12-20T10:34:48.725000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.437000Z',48),
	(58,'Plo Koon','22BBY','black','none','188','80','orange','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Plo_Koon','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/b/bf/PloKoonCardTrader.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"104th Battalion\"]','Plo Koon was a Kel Dor Jedi Master and member of the High Council. Known for his deep voice and strong sense of justice, he trained many Jedi. Plo was close to Ahsoka Tano and helped discover her. He died during Order 66, shot down in his starfighter. His legacy of compassion lives on. Plo was one of the Order’s most beloved figures.','Plo Koon came from the stormy world of Dorin and wore a protective mask due to his species’ needs. He was known for his firm moral code and quiet strength. Plo was a powerful Force user and skilled pilot. He served as a general in the Clone Wars and led troops in critical missions. He discovered Ahsoka Tano and recommended her for Jedi training. He treated clone troopers as equals, earning their deep respect. Plo was wise, thoughtful, and deeply committed to peace. He fought in battles across the galaxy, from Felucia to Cato Neimoidia. During Order 66, his clone squadron turned on him mid-flight. His starfighter was destroyed in a deadly ambush. He died in the explosion, unaware of the treachery. Jedi and clones alike mourned his passing. His name is spoken with reverence by survivors. Plo Koon embodied Jedi ideals with rare sincerity. His death marked a profound loss. His teachings continue through those he mentored.','light','yellow','2014-12-20T10:49:19.859000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.439000Z',49),
	(59,'Mas Amedda','unknown','blue','none','196','unknown','blue','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Mas_Amedda','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/37/Mas_Amedda_SWCT.png','[\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Senate\",\"Office of the Chancellor\",\"Strategic Advisory Cell\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Ruling Council\",\"Coruscant provisional government\"]','Mas Amedda was a Chagrian politician who served as Vice Chair of the Galactic Senate. He worked under Chancellors Valorum and Palpatine. Mas became a mouthpiece for the Empire. He supported Sith rule, whether out of belief or survival. He helped dismantle the Republic. Mas Amedda faded into obscurity after the Emperor’s death.','Mas Amedda was born on Champala and rose through the political ranks of the Republic. He was known for his ceremonial staff and booming voice. As Vice Chair of the Senate, he maintained order during intense debates. Under Chancellor Palpatine, Mas embraced authoritarianism. He witnessed the rise of the Empire and remained by Palpatine’s side. Some believe he was a true believer; others see him as a survivor. He played a key role in public ceremonies and Imperial declarations. Mas never openly opposed Palpatine’s will. When the Emperor died, he remained in office for a time. Eventually, the Empire crumbled around him. Mas was forced to negotiate surrender to the New Republic. His political legacy is one of compliance and control. Though not a Sith, he enabled Sith domination. Mas Amedda is a reminder of how power endures through bureaucrats. His actions helped shape galactic history.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-20T10:53:26.457000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.442000Z',50),
	(60,'Gregar Typho','unknown','brown','black','185','85','dark','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Gregar_Typho','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/5/52/Gregar_Typho.jpg','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Royal Naboo Security Forces\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Gregar Typho was Captain of Security for Senator Padmé Amidala. He was vigilant, brave, and highly protective. Typho worked closely with the Jedi during dangerous missions. He stood guard during the Separatist crisis. Though often stoic, he was deeply loyal. Typho served faithfully until the fall of the Republic.','Gregar Typho hailed from Naboo and followed in the footsteps of his uncle, Quarsh Panaka. He became Padmé Amidala’s chief of security during her Senate career. Typho took his duty seriously, rarely leaving her side. He coordinated with Jedi escorts like Anakin Skywalker during tense missions. When Padmé returned to Naboo or visited dangerous planets, Typho was always nearby. He suspected Anakin and Padmé’s relationship but remained silent. His loyalty was to her safety, not her secrets. Typho led investigations into multiple assassination attempts. Despite his efforts, he could not prevent her tragic fate. Typho’s later life is largely undocumented. He remains remembered as a vigilant protector. His stoic nature concealed a fierce devotion. Though not a Jedi or warrior, he played a vital role. His legacy lies in quiet strength and personal sacrifice.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T11:10:10.381000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.445000Z',8),
	(61,'Cordé','unknown','brown','brown','157','unknown','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Cord%C3%A9','/images/people/61-cord-e.png','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Naboo Royal Handmaidens\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Cordé was a handmaiden and body double for Padmé Amidala. She served loyally during times of danger. Cordé sacrificed herself during an assassination attempt. A bomb struck the landing platform, and she was fatally wounded. Her last words expressed concern for Padmé\'s safety. Cordé\'s courage saved a senator and symbolized loyal service.','Cordé served as one of Padmé Amidala’s handmaidens and doubles during the tense years following the Naboo crisis. She trained in diplomacy, self-defense, and disguise. As political tensions rose, Cordé took on riskier roles to protect her queen. She accompanied Padmé to Coruscant amid threats from the Separatists. Upon arrival, a bomb was detonated near their ship. Cordé, disguised as Padmé, was mortally wounded in the blast. As she lay dying, she assured her mistress that her duty had been fulfilled. Her sacrifice diverted the attack from the true senator. Padmé mourned her loss deeply. Cordé was remembered among Naboo’s protectors with honor. Her bravery represented the unseen efforts of the handmaidens. She gave her life for peace and for the Republic. Cordé’s name became a quiet symbol of devotion. Though she served in silence, her legacy echoed in those who knew her.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T11:11:39.630000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.449000Z',8),
	(62,'Cliegg Lars','82BBY','blue','brown','183','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Cliegg_Lars','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/36/ClieggLarsHS-SWE.jpg','[\"Lars family\"]','Cliegg Lars was a moisture farmer from Tatooine. He became the stepfather of Anakin Skywalker after marrying Shmi. Hard-working and gruff, he valued family above all. Cliegg lost his leg trying to rescue Shmi from Tusken Raiders. Her death devastated him deeply. He remained on the homestead, raising Luke’s future guardians.','Cliegg Lars was a simple moisture farmer on the desert world of Tatooine. He led a quiet life until he met Shmi Skywalker, whom he freed and married. Their bond was strong, and Cliegg welcomed her son Anakin into the family. When Shmi was kidnapped by Tusken Raiders, Cliegg organized a rescue. He lost his leg in the attempt, returning broken and embittered. Though he survived, he never gave up hope. The loss of Shmi deeply affected him. When Anakin came searching, Cliegg told him the tragic truth. He warned Anakin of the dangers of vengeance. Cliegg later died and was buried near the homestead. His legacy was one of love, loss, and quiet resilience. Cliegg\'s decision to free and marry Shmi altered galactic history. His simple life stood in stark contrast to the war-torn galaxy. Cliegg valued home, family, and loyalty. He had little interest in politics or Jedi affairs. Yet he was caught in their storm. His story reminds us of the silent sacrifices made by those far from the frontlines. Cliegg Lars remains a symbol of dignity in grief and strength in simplicity.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T15:59:03.958000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.451000Z',1),
	(63,'Poggle the Lesser','unknown','yellow','none','183','80','green','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Poggle_the_Lesser','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/9/93/Poggle_the_lesser_-_sw_card_trader.png','[\"Stalgasin hive\",\"Karina the Great\'s empire\",\"Techno Union\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Separatist Council\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Poggle the Lesser was the Archduke of Geonosis and a key Separatist leader. He commanded the insectoid Geonosians and oversaw droid foundries. Poggle allied with Count Dooku in the Clone Wars. He helped design the first Death Star. Captured by the Republic, he later died in Imperial custody. His legacy was mechanical terror and betrayal.','Poggle the Lesser ruled over the Stalgasin hive on Geonosis with cunning and cruelty. As Archduke, he wielded immense power among his people. When the Clone Wars erupted, he aligned Geonosis with Count Dooku and the Separatists. He offered the planet\'s industrial power to build droid armies. Poggle was instrumental in planning the Death Star. He presided over the first battle of Geonosis, where Jedi and clones stormed his world. Despite defeat, he escaped capture multiple times. His loyalty to the Separatist cause made him a dangerous asset. He constantly defied Republic efforts to bring peace. Poggle\'s leadership was harsh but effective. He inspired fear among enemies and subordinates alike. Captured eventually, he was interrogated for intelligence. During the rise of the Empire, he was executed in secret. His name remained a cautionary tale in the archives. Poggle\'s decisions escalated the war, leading to galactic chaos. His actions contributed to the Jedi\'s downfall and the Republic’s transformation. He cared little for organic life outside his species. He believed droid supremacy was the future. Poggle’s legacy endures in the mechanized brutality he helped forge.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-20T16:40:43.977000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.453000Z',11),
	(64,'Luminara Unduli','58BBY','blue','black','170','56.2','yellow','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Luminara_Unduli','/images/people/64-luminara-unduli.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"41st Elite Corps\"]','Luminara Unduli was a Mirialan Jedi Master of grace and discipline. She fought bravely in the Clone Wars. Known for her calm leadership and skill in battle. Luminara mentored Barriss Offee, who later betrayed the Jedi. She was captured by the Empire and executed. Her memory is one of serenity and sacrifice.','Luminara Unduli hailed from the planet Mirial and was raised in Jedi traditions of harmony and self-control. Her dedication earned her a place on the battlefield as a general in the Clone Wars. She participated in the Battle of Geonosis and missions across the galaxy. Luminara trained Padawan Barriss Offee with precision and compassion. She became known for balancing duty with empathy. As the war deepened, her measured voice helped guide the Jedi. Despite her accomplishments, she remained humble. She served on the front lines without seeking glory. Her capture by the Empire marked a tragic end. Luminara was used in a cruel trick by the Inquisitors. Her remains lured surviving Jedi into traps. Her name was sullied by deception, but the truth prevailed. She believed in the light even when others faltered. Her death served as a reminder of Jedi resilience. Luminara’s wisdom echoed long after her passing. She sought peace through strength and understanding. Her legacy endured in the memories of those she saved. Luminara Unduli represents the calm heart of the Jedi Order.','light','green','2014-12-20T16:45:53.668000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.455000Z',51),
	(65,'Barriss Offee','40BBY','blue','black','166','50','yellow','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Barriss_Offee','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/37/Barrisprofile2.jpg','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Barriss Offee was a Jedi Padawan turned traitor. Trained under Luminara Unduli, she once served nobly in the Clone Wars. Disillusioned, she bombed the Jedi Temple. She framed Ahsoka Tano for the attack. Barriss was exposed and arrested. Her fall reflected the Jedi Order’s crumbling foundation.','Barriss Offee was born on Mirial and brought into the Jedi Order as a child. Trained by Luminara Unduli, she exhibited great potential and discipline. She served as a healer and warrior during the Clone Wars. Barriss participated in the Battle of Geonosis and proved her courage. Over time, she grew disturbed by the Jedi’s role in the war. Her faith faltered, and she saw the Order as corrupted. Barriss orchestrated a bombing at the Jedi Temple, killing innocents. She framed her fellow Jedi, Ahsoka Tano, leading to a high-profile trial. Ahsoka was forced to flee the Order. An investigation revealed the truth. Barriss confessed, condemning the Jedi’s hypocrisy. She was imprisoned, her path forever changed. Barriss’s fall illustrated how war fractured the Jedi. Her actions sparked debate within the Order. She had once been a symbol of devotion. Now she stood as a cautionary tale. Her betrayal wounded those who trusted her. Yet her words echoed a truth others ignored. Barriss Offee was a product of a war that blurred the light and dark.','dark','blue','2014-12-20T16:46:40.440000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.457000Z',51),
	(66,'Dormé','unknown','brown','brown','165','unknown','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Dorm%C3%A9','/images/people/66-dorm-e.webp','[\"Royal House of Naboo\",\"Naboo Royal Handmaidens\",\"Galactic Republic\"]','Dormé was a loyal handmaiden of Padmé Amidala. She accompanied the senator during turbulent times. Dormé was graceful, intelligent, and brave. She protected Padmé from political threats. Her devotion was unwavering throughout their missions. Though often unseen, Dormé played a crucial protective role.','Dormé served as one of Padmé Amidala’s most trusted handmaidens during her senatorial career. Trained in security, etiquette, and politics, Dormé provided counsel and defense. She traveled with Padmé to Coruscant and other volatile environments. Dormé often posed as her mistress to thwart assassins. She maintained professionalism under pressure. When Padmé left for Naboo with Anakin Skywalker, Dormé stayed behind in Coruscant. She wept at their departure, sensing both danger and love. Dormé represented the strength of Naboo’s women. She acted with composure in diplomatic circles. Dormé\'s loyalty never wavered. Though not a soldier, she would have given her life for Padmé. She understood the stakes of galactic politics. Her silent courage often went unnoticed. Dormé remained vigilant against unseen threats. Her presence reassured Padmé during turbulent times. Though she appeared only briefly, her impact was lasting. Dormé embodied the grace and strength of Naboo’s royal tradition. Her legacy is one of humble service and quiet heroism.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T16:49:14.640000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.460000Z',8),
	(67,'Dooku','102BBY','brown','white','193','80','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Dooku','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/b/b8/Dooku_Headshot.jpg','[\"House of Dooku\",\"Lost Twenty\",\"Sith\",\"Independent Movement for Self-Determination\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\"]','Dooku was a former Jedi Master who turned to the dark side. Known as Count Dooku, he became Darth Tyranus under Darth Sidious. He led the Separatists during the Clone Wars. Elegant and philosophical, Dooku believed the Republic was corrupt. His betrayal marked a major turning point in galactic history. Dooku\'s ambition ultimately led to his own downfall.','Dooku was born into nobility on Serenno and brought to the Jedi Order at an early age. As a Jedi, he was wise, composed, and exceptionally powerful. He trained Qui-Gon Jinn and served the Republic with distinction. But disillusionment with the Jedi Council and Republic corruption led him to leave the Order. He became Count of Serenno, reclaiming his ancestral title. Secretly, he became Darth Tyranus, apprentice to Darth Sidious. Dooku orchestrated the rise of the Separatist movement, initiating the Clone Wars. His charisma drew many systems to his cause. Dooku helped commission the clone army through Jedi Master Sifo-Dyas’s vision. He led with precision, often confronting Jedi directly. He dueled Yoda, Obi-Wan, and Anakin, showcasing immense skill. Despite his calculated nature, Dooku was expendable to Sidious. In a shocking betrayal, Anakin killed him at Palpatine’s command. Dooku’s death cleared the path for Anakin’s fall and Palpatine’s rise. His legacy was one of manipulation, intellect, and tragedy. He believed himself a savior, not a villain. Yet his decisions plunged the galaxy into chaos. Count Dooku remains one of the most complex figures of the Clone Wars era.','dark','red','2014-12-20T16:52:14.726000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.462000Z',52),
	(68,'Bail Prestor Organa','67BBY','brown','black','191','unknown','tan','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Bail_Prestor_Organa','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/5/50/Bail_Organa_Mug.jpg','[\"House of Organa\",\"High Court of Alderaan\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Galactic Senate\",\"Loyalist Committee\",\"Security Committee\",\"Delegation of 2000\",\"Galactic Empire\",\"Imperial Senate\",\"Finance Committee\",\"Appropriations Committee\",\"Intelligence Oversight Committee\",\"Military Oversight Committee\",\"Alderaanian Resistance\",\"Kota\'s Militia\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\"]','Bail Organa was a senator of Alderaan and adoptive father to Leia. He opposed the Empire from within the Senate chambers. Brave and diplomatic, Bail secretly aided the Rebellion. He supported Jedi survivors, including Obi-Wan Kenobi and Yoda. His sacrifice helped preserve hope during dark times. Bail Organa stood as a beacon of resistance and honor.','Bail Prestor Organa served as a senator for Alderaan during the final days of the Republic. Known for his eloquence and resolve, he was a member of the Loyalist Committee. Bail remained a staunch ally of democracy and opposed the growing authoritarianism under Palpatine. Following the fall of the Jedi Order, Bail helped smuggle survivors to safety. He personally rescued Yoda and Obi-Wan after the Jedi Purge. Bail adopted Leia Organa, hiding her true heritage. As a member of the Rebellion’s founding leaders, he worked tirelessly in secret. His palace on Alderaan served as a sanctuary for dissidents. Bail was a diplomat who risked everything to stand for justice. He coordinated efforts with Mon Mothma and other resistance figures. Though he wore the robes of a senator, his heart beat for freedom. His commitment to peace was unshakable, even as war drew near. Bail never abandoned his values, even when the Empire targeted his homeworld. He died in the destruction of Alderaan, along with millions. His death was a devastating loss for the Rebellion. Bail Organa\'s courage lived on through Leia. He remains one of the most honorable figures of the Galactic Civil War era.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T16:53:08.575000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.463000Z',2),
	(69,'Jango Fett','66BBY','brown','black','183','79','tan','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Jango_Fett','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/5/56/JangoInfobox.png','[\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Tyranus\"]','Jango Fett was a feared Mandalorian bounty hunter. Known for his deadly precision and iconic armor. He served as the genetic template for the clone army. Jango raised his own clone son, Boba Fett. He worked for Count Dooku under secret contracts. Jango met his end at the hands of Mace Windu.','Jango Fett was born on Concord Dawn and trained as a Mandalorian warrior. Renowned for his lethality and discipline, he became one of the most feared bounty hunters in the galaxy. Count Dooku selected him as the genetic source for the Grand Army of the Republic. Jango agreed to the cloning under one condition: an unaltered clone to raise as a son—Boba Fett. He taught Boba survival, combat, and Mandalorian principles. Jango remained independent and cautious, avoiding political entanglements. Despite working with the Separatists, he maintained personal motives. He often operated from Kamino, overseeing the clone development. His reputation attracted rivals and allies alike. Jango wielded twin blasters and donned Mandalorian beskar armor. During the Battle of Geonosis, he confronted Jedi in open combat. He fought valiantly but was ultimately killed by Mace Windu. His death left Boba orphaned and seeking revenge. Jango’s DNA shaped the galaxy’s future, with millions of clones bearing his face. Despite his mercenary life, he cared deeply for his son. He remains a symbol of Mandalorian pride and professional honor. Jango Fett’s legacy lived on through both the Clone Wars and Boba Fett’s rise.','neutral',NULL,'2014-12-20T16:54:41.620000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.465000Z',53),
	(70,'Zam Wesell','unknown','yellow','blonde','168','55','fair, green, yellow','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Zam_Wesell','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/7d/Clawdite.jpg','[\"Mabari\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\"]','Zam Wesell was a Clawdite bounty hunter and shape-shifter. Known for her skill in disguise and assassination. She worked with Jango Fett on missions for the Separatists. Her attempt to kill Padmé Amidala failed. Captured by Obi-Wan, she was silenced before revealing her employer. Zam\'s legacy is one of shadows and secrets.','Zam Wesell hailed from Zolan and belonged to the Clawdite species, known for their shapeshifting ability. Her natural talents made her a formidable infiltrator. Zam specialized in stealth, poison, and disguise. She worked for various clients, including Jango Fett and the Confederacy of Independent Systems. Her most infamous mission involved the attempted assassination of Senator Padmé Amidala. Using a droid and poisonous insects, she infiltrated Padmé’s quarters. The attempt failed, prompting pursuit by Jedi Obi-Wan and Anakin. Zam led them on a dangerous chase through Coruscant’s underworld. Eventually cornered, she was shot with a toxic dart by Jango Fett. He silenced her before she could reveal his involvement. Zam’s brief appearance belied her significant role in the Clone Wars’ beginnings. Her death sparked the Jedi investigation into the clone conspiracy. She represents the hidden agents that shaped galactic events from the shadows. Zam’s skills and reputation earned her respect among bounty hunters. Yet her loyalty to clients proved fatal. She chose secrecy over honor and paid the price. Her shapeshifting ability gave her unmatched access. But her downfall was swift and final. Zam Wesell remains a shadowy figure in galactic history.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-20T16:57:44.471000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.468000Z',54),
	(71,'Dexter Jettster','unknown','yellow','none','198','102','brown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Dexter_Jettster','/images/people/71-dexter-jettster.webp','[\"Dex\'s Diner\"]','Dexter Jettster was a friendly Besalisk cook on Coruscant. He owned Dex’s Diner and had a colorful past. A former prospector and fighter, he knew many secrets. He helped Obi-Wan identify a Kaminoan saberdart. His knowledge spanned cultures, weapons, and galactic history. Dexter was a humble ally with hidden depths.','Dexter Jettster ran a bustling diner in the heart of Coruscant’s cityscape. Known for his warm smile and hearty meals, Dex was more than just a cook. He had once traveled the galaxy as a prospector and mercenary. His experience gave him knowledge that even Jedi lacked. When Obi-Wan Kenobi sought information about a mysterious dart, Dex identified it as Kaminoan. This clue helped uncover the clone army’s secret origin. Dexter’s diner became an unlikely hub for wisdom. He respected the Jedi and aided them when he could. Though not Force-sensitive, he showed insight and courage. He provided comfort to many during uncertain times. Dexter embraced a simple life but kept his adventurous spirit. He avoided conflict but knew how to defend himself. Dex’s diner was a haven of laughter and old stories. He valued friendship, honesty, and good food. His past was murky, but his present was meaningful. Dex taught that wisdom can come from anywhere. He never sought fame, only a good life. Dexter Jettster remains a beloved figure in Coruscant’s underworld. His impact on Obi-Wan’s journey was subtle but vital.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T17:28:27.248000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.470000Z',55),
	(72,'Lama Su','unknown','black','none','229','88','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Lama_Su','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/7/73/Lama_Su.jpg','[\"Galactic Republic\"]','Lama Su served as the Prime Minister of Kamino during the Clone Wars. Calm and calculating, he oversaw the creation of the Republic’s clone army. Lama Su maintained a distant professionalism in his dealings with Jedi emissaries. His belief in order and efficiency defined Kaminoan society. Despite his neutrality, Lama Su played a key role in galactic warfare. His actions indirectly shaped the fate of the Republic and the Jedi Order.','Lama Su was the Prime Minister of Kamino, a remote water-covered world known for its cloning expertise. He led the Kaminoan effort in creating the clone army for the Galactic Republic. Lama Su kept a composed and formal demeanor when welcoming Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi. He spoke openly of the army commissioned by Jedi Master Sifo-Dyas, though the true origins remained shadowed in mystery. His interactions with Kenobi revealed Kamino’s pivotal but hidden role in galactic affairs. Lama Su was focused on production and quality, emphasizing the loyalty and effectiveness of the clones. He never questioned the Republic’s motives, choosing to honor the arrangement. Under his leadership, Kamino became the backbone of the Grand Army. Lama Su took pride in his people’s scientific accomplishments. Yet, he remained detached from the moral implications of their creations. As the Clone Wars erupted, his facility continued to supply troops. Lama Su valued secrecy, working closely with Jedi generals but revealing little. He was not aligned with any faction beyond Kamino’s interests. When the Empire rose, Kamino’s autonomy was quietly suppressed. Lama Su attempted to maintain his authority during the Empire’s takeover. However, his fate was sealed when cloning programs were centralized under Imperial control. Lama Su’s legacy endures in the thousands of clone soldiers born from Kamino’s chambers. He was a quiet architect behind a massive military force. Lama Su represents the cold, clinical mindset behind the Republic’s war machine. Though rarely seen, his decisions left a deep imprint on the galaxy.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T17:30:50.416000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.473000Z',10),
	(73,'Taun We','unknown','black','none','213','unknown','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Taun_We','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/9/9c/TaunWe.jpg','[\"Galactic Republic\"]','Taun We was a Kaminoan aide who worked closely with Lama Su. She guided Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi through the cloning facilities. Soft-spoken and graceful, she offered insight into Kaminoan science. Taun We displayed unwavering loyalty to Kamino’s government. Her calm demeanor concealed the enormous consequences of her work. She played a small but vital role in the creation of the clone army.','Taun We was an administrative aide to Prime Minister Lama Su on Kamino. She greeted Obi-Wan Kenobi when he arrived to investigate the clone army. Her demeanor was polite and serene, in line with Kaminoan cultural norms. She provided Obi-Wan with a tour of the cloning facilities. Taun We spoke with pride about Kamino\'s achievements in genetic engineering. She detailed the accelerated growth and obedience of the clones. Her role was primarily diplomatic, easing the Jedi’s concerns with gentle explanation. Taun We appeared unaware of the darker forces behind the army\'s creation. She mentioned Jedi Master Sifo-Dyas as the one who placed the order. However, she never questioned the order’s secrecy or origins. During the Clone Wars, Taun We continued her work in support of Kamino’s cloning efforts. She showed compassion for the clones, viewing them as more than products. In the shifting political landscape, Taun We’s loyalty remained with Kamino’s leadership. Later Imperial suppression of Kamino\'s independence placed her in danger. She attempted to maintain Kamino’s scientific legacy. Her fate was uncertain as the Empire tightened its grip. Taun We\'s role was that of a quiet observer amid rising conflict. Though not a warrior, she influenced the war through science. Her presence was calm but significant. Taun We stands as a symbol of Kamino\'s quiet complicity in galactic war.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T17:31:21.195000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.474000Z',10),
	(74,'Jocasta Nu','unknown','blue','white','167','unknown','fair','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Jocasta_Nu','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/1/15/Jocasta_Nu_SWE.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\"]','Jocasta Nu was the Jedi Temple’s Chief Librarian and keeper of ancient knowledge. Wise and firm, she safeguarded the Jedi Archives with great pride. She guided young Jedi and answered their questions with authority. Jocasta believed in the sanctity of recorded knowledge. During the fall of the Jedi Order, she tried to preserve sacred texts. Her legacy lived on through the wisdom she protected.','Jocasta Nu served as the Chief Librarian of the Jedi Temple on Coruscant. She oversaw the Jedi Archives, one of the most comprehensive collections of knowledge in the galaxy. With a sharp memory and commanding presence, she offered guidance to Jedi seeking historical or tactical insight. She assisted Obi-Wan Kenobi during his search for Kamino, though her belief in the archive\'s completeness led her to dismiss the planet\'s absence. Jocasta was devoted to the Jedi Order and the preservation of its teachings. She believed deeply in the power of knowledge to bring peace. As the Clone Wars unfolded, she continued to maintain the archives amidst growing turmoil. After the fall of the Jedi, Jocasta became one of the few survivors of Order 66. She went into hiding, carrying Jedi teachings and secrets with her. Determined to restore the Order, she compiled a list of Force-sensitive children across the galaxy. Her goal was to pass Jedi knowledge to a future generation. She briefly returned to Coruscant to recover holocrons, risking capture. Despite her age, she proved to be resourceful and courageous. Jocasta was ultimately hunted down by Darth Vader and the Inquisitors. Her death marked another tragic loss for the Jedi Order. However, her efforts were not in vain. Some of the knowledge she safeguarded was recovered and used later by Luke Skywalker. Jocasta\'s life reflected the noblest ideals of the Jedi: wisdom, patience, and commitment to truth. Though not a warrior, she fought with the strength of her mind. Jocasta Nu will forever be remembered as the guardian of Jedi wisdom.','light','blue','2014-12-20T17:32:51.996000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.476000Z',9),
	(75,'R4-P17','unknown','red, blue','none','96','unknown','silver, red','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/R4-P17','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/6/6b/R4-P17.jpg','[\"Galactic Republic\"]','R4-P17 was a loyal astromech droid assigned to Obi-Wan Kenobi. Compact and efficient, she supported missions during the Clone Wars. R4 worked tirelessly to maintain starfighters and collect tactical data. Her resourcefulness saved Obi-Wan’s life more than once. Though she lacked speech, her programming made her a steadfast companion. R4’s journey ended in battle, but her contributions were vital to the Republic.','R4-P17 was a red-and-silver astromech droid who served Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi. She was instrumental in pre-flight checks, navigation, and repairs aboard his starfighter. R4 accompanied Obi-Wan during reconnaissance missions, including his visit to Kamino. She gathered data critical to exposing the clone army\'s existence. During the Clone Wars, R4 participated in space battles and scouting operations. Despite her small size, she displayed impressive adaptability. R4 had a brave personality and never hesitated to follow Obi-Wan into danger. While she lacked a humanoid voice, she communicated effectively through beeps and lights. Obi-Wan trusted her completely and considered her a partner in missions. She often worked with other droids, sharing data and coordinating logistics. R4-P17’s memory held sensitive information valuable to the Republic. She once helped disable enemy systems during a surprise attack. Her systems included advanced sensors and mapping protocols. R4 was known for her loyalty and quick diagnostics. In the Battle of Coruscant, she was destroyed by buzz droids while trying to assist Obi-Wan. Her destruction was mourned by her Jedi companion. Though her existence was brief, her actions made a lasting impact. R4-P17 represents the importance of support roles in galactic conflict. She stood by Obi-Wan with quiet bravery. R4 remains one of the Republic\'s unsung heroes. Her circuitry may be gone, but her loyalty endures in memory.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T17:43:36.409000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.478000Z',28),
	(76,'Wat Tambor','unknown','unknown','none','193','48','green, grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Wat_Tambor','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/a/a5/Wat_Tambor.png','[\"Techno Union\",\"Baktoid Armor Workshop\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Separatist Council\"]','Wat Tambor was a Techno Union foreman and Separatist leader. He played a major role in supplying weapons during the Clone Wars. Tambor used his position to advance war profiteering and influence politics. He rarely showed empathy, focusing on technological gain. His appearance was mechanical, mirroring his cold personality. Wat Tambor embodied the darker side of industry during war.','Wat Tambor was the Foreman of the Techno Union and a key member of the Separatist Council. He operated from the planet Skako and managed numerous factories and droid foundries. Tambor wore a pressurized suit that modulated his voice and kept his body stable in foreign environments. He allied with Count Dooku to supply the Separatists with battle droids and war technology. Tambor believed in profit and efficiency above all else. He showed little concern for the lives lost in the wars he fueled. His factories operated across the galaxy, arming the Confederacy of Independent Systems. On Ryloth, he occupied the planet and enslaved its people to harvest resources. His cruelty became a symbol of Separatist oppression. Tambor viewed organic life as secondary to production quotas. He remained calm in public but ruthless behind closed doors. His greed and loyalty to Dooku made him a threat to the Republic. During the Clone Wars, he attended council meetings and directed war efforts. Tambor rarely engaged in combat, instead using subordinates and machines. He underestimated the Republic\'s resolve and the strength of the Jedi. When Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi liberated Ryloth, Tambor was captured. He was later executed alongside other Separatist leaders by Darth Vader. His death marked the end of the Techno Union’s autonomy. Wat Tambor’s legacy is one of greed, innovation, and moral decay. He turned science into a tool of destruction. Wat Tambor represents how unchecked industry can become a force of oppression.','dark',NULL,'2014-12-20T17:53:52.607000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.481000Z',56),
	(77,'San Hill','unknown','gold','none','191','unknown','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/San_Hill','/images/people/77-san-hill.png','[\"InterGalactic Banking Clan\",\"Muunilinst Banking Clan\",\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Separatist Council\"]','San Hill was the Chairman of the InterGalactic Banking Clan. As a Separatist leader, he funded the Confederacy during the Clone Wars. He used financial power to influence galactic politics. Hill allied with Count Dooku to weaken the Republic. His motivations were rooted in greed and economic dominance. San Hill represents the corruption of power through wealth.','San Hill served as the Muun Chairman of the InterGalactic Banking Clan during the waning years of the Galactic Republic. Tall and gaunt, he belonged to the Muun species, known for their financial acumen. As tensions rose in the galaxy, San Hill allied his clan with Count Dooku and the Confederacy of Independent Systems. His goal was to destabilize the Republic and increase the Banking Clan’s power. Hill provided critical funding for the Separatist war effort. He financed the construction of droids and starships and ensured the flow of resources. His presence on the Separatist Council gave him influence over the galaxy’s fate. Though not a warrior, Hill was a key figure in the Clone Wars. He often used diplomacy and manipulation to pursue his agenda. Greed was his compass, and profit was his cause. As the war escalated, his fortunes rose and fell with the Separatist campaign. After the war, Hill was executed during Darth Sidious’s purge of the Separatist leadership. His death marked the end of Muunilinst’s dominance. San Hill’s legacy is one of betrayal, ambition, and downfall. He believed in numbers, not ideals. But numbers alone could not save him. His downfall was a warning about unchecked greed in a galaxy on fire.','dark','red','2014-12-20T17:58:17.049000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.484000Z',57),
	(78,'Shaak Ti','unknown','black','none','178','57','red, blue, white','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Shaak_Ti','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/2/20/Shaak_Ti_closeup-SWE.png','[\"Jedi Order\",\"Jedi High Council\",\"Jedi assault team\",\"Galactic Republic\",\"Grand Army of the Republic\"]','Shaak Ti was a Togruta Jedi Master known for her wisdom and grace. She served on the Jedi High Council during the Clone Wars. Shaak Ti led troops and protected the cloning facilities on Kamino. Her presence was calm, thoughtful, and deeply connected to the Force. She was dedicated to Jedi ideals even in the darkest times. Shaak Ti symbolizes endurance and quiet strength.','Shaak Ti was a Jedi Master from the planet Shili and a respected member of the Jedi High Council. As a Togruta, she was distinguished by her colorful skin and tall montrals. During the Clone Wars, she played a vital role in overseeing the training and development of clone troopers on Kamino. Shaak Ti believed in compassion, discipline, and harmony through the Force. She was a voice of calm reason among the Council, offering measured insights during moments of crisis. She led several missions and proved her combat prowess in battle. Despite the chaos of war, she remained committed to Jedi principles. Her presence on Kamino helped protect one of the Republic’s most important military assets. After Order 66, her fate became surrounded by conflicting accounts. Some say she died in the Jedi Temple, others that she perished on Felucia. What remained constant was her unwavering resolve. Shaak Ti mentored young Jedi and stood as a moral compass. Her connection to the Force was strong and steady. She embodied the best of the Jedi Order even as it crumbled. Shaak Ti’s legacy endured through those she guided. She remains a symbol of serene strength, duty, and the light side’s quiet wisdom.','light','blue','2014-12-20T18:44:01.103000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.486000Z',58),
	(79,'Grievous','unknown','green, yellow','none','216','159','brown, white','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Grievous','/images/people/79-grievous.jpg','[\"Confederacy of Independent Systems\",\"Separatist Droid Army\"]','General Grievous was a fearsome cyborg warlord and Supreme Commander of the Separatist droid armies. Originally a Kaleesh warrior, he was transformed into a weapon of war. Grievous wielded multiple lightsabers taken from fallen Jedi. He was ruthless, strategic, and feared across the galaxy. Though powerful, he was manipulated by Darth Sidious. Grievous embodied the brutal machine of war.','General Grievous began life as Qymaen jai Sheelal, a Kaleesh warlord known for his fierce tactics. Gravely injured in a shuttle explosion orchestrated by the Sith, his body was reconstructed into a cybernetic form. Reborn as General Grievous, he became the ruthless Supreme Commander of the Separatist droid army. Trained in lightsaber combat by Count Dooku, Grievous hunted Jedi and collected their weapons as trophies. His body housed mechanical limbs, a reinforced exoskeleton, and advanced targeting systems. He could wield four lightsabers at once, overwhelming opponents with sheer ferocity. Grievous\'s combat style relied on intimidation and aggression. He was feared on every battlefield he appeared. Despite his strength, he was driven by rage and a sense of vengeance against the Jedi. Grievous viewed himself as a victim molded into a conqueror. Behind the mask was a bitter warrior shaped by loss and manipulation. His presence spread terror among clones and Jedi alike. He was loyal only to his cause and cared little for alliances. In the final days of the Clone Wars, Grievous was defeated by Obi-Wan Kenobi on Utapau. His demise marked the beginning of the Republic\'s end. Grievous\'s legacy remains a twisted blend of honor lost and hatred reborn.','dark','red','2014-12-20T19:43:53.348000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.488000Z',59),
	(80,'Tarfful','unknown','blue','brown','234','136','brown','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Tarfful','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/3/37/Tarfful_RotS.png','[\"Galactic Republic\"]','Tarfful was a Wookiee chieftain from Kashyyyk and an ally of the Jedi. Strong and honorable, he fought to protect his people during the Clone Wars. Tarfful aided Yoda and the Republic during the Battle of Kashyyyk. He later helped Chewbacca survive Imperial purges. His loyalty and bravery were legendary among Wookiees. Tarfful symbolizes strength, honor, and resistance.','Tarfful was a towering Wookiee warrior and a respected chieftain of his people on the forested planet of Kashyyyk. As war came to his world, he forged an alliance with the Jedi and the Republic. Tarfful fought fiercely during the Battle of Kashyyyk, using his strength and tactical skill to repel Separatist invaders. He fought side by side with Master Yoda and other Jedi generals. Tarfful\'s leadership helped unify Wookiee resistance forces. Despite heavy losses, he remained determined to protect his homeland. Tarfful showed wisdom in warfare and compassion for his people. His roars were commands of defiance against oppression. When the Jedi were betrayed during Order 66, Tarfful helped Yoda escape the clone ambush. He also became a protector of Chewbacca, guiding him through the chaos that followed. Tarfful remained a symbol of honor in an age of tyranny. His resistance continued throughout the rise of the Empire. Though not seen on the galactic stage, his actions influenced key survivors. Tarfful embodied the Wookiee spirit—courageous, noble, and unyielding. He lives on in the stories passed among his people. Tarfful’s strength was not just in his size, but in his loyalty and courage.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T19:46:34.209000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.491000Z',14),
	(81,'Raymus Antilles','unknown','brown','brown','188','79','light','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Raymus_Antilles','https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/starwars/images/8/80/Raymus_card_trader.png','[\"House of Organa\",\"Alliance to Restore the Republic\",\"Alliance Military\"]','Raymus Antilles served as captain of the Tantive IV and was loyal to House Organa. He played a key role in transporting Leia and the stolen Death Star plans. Calm and dutiful, he upheld the ideals of the Rebellion. Raymus remained composed even under Imperial capture. He died protecting his mission from Darth Vader. His sacrifice marks the beginning of a galactic revolution.','Raymus Antilles was a starship captain in service to House Organa and the Rebel Alliance. He commanded the Tantive IV, the consular ship used by Princess Leia to transport crucial Rebel intelligence. Antilles was a seasoned officer, trusted by Bail Organa for his integrity and resolve. He carried out high-risk missions in secrecy, often traveling through dangerous Imperial zones. When the Death Star plans were transmitted aboard his ship, Antilles became a target of Imperial wrath. As the Tantive IV was captured above Tatooine, Antilles stood firm in the face of overwhelming force. Darth Vader interrogated and ultimately killed him in search of the plans. Raymus did not betray the Rebellion. His death marked the very opening of the Galactic Civil War. Raymus was more than a soldier—he was a loyal protector of hope. His quiet heroism gave Leia a chance to escape with the plans. His actions set the stage for the Rebel victory at Yavin. Though often overlooked, Antilles was a pillar of the Alliance. His legacy is carried in the spirit of those who fought on. Raymus Antilles died for the future of the galaxy.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T19:49:35.583000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.493000Z',2),
	(82,'Sly Moore','unknown','white','none','178','48','pale','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Sly_Moore','/images/people/82-sly-moore.webp','[\"Galactic Republic\",\"Office of the Chancellor\",\"Galactic Empire\"]','Sly Moore was a close advisor to Supreme Chancellor Palpatine. Pale, mysterious, and silent, she held deep secrets within the Senate. She was one of the few aware of Palpatine’s true identity as Darth Sidious. Moore manipulated political outcomes from the shadows. Her loyalty to the Sith made her a quiet force of darkness. Sly Moore embodied secrecy, control, and unseen influence.','Sly Moore was an Umbaran political figure who rose to prominence during the waning years of the Galactic Republic. With her piercing gaze and ghostly appearance, she stood apart in the Senate halls. Moore served as one of Chancellor Palpatine’s senior administrative aides, always near but rarely speaking. Her role extended far beyond protocol; she was a trusted confidante in Palpatine’s rise to power. Unlike many in the Senate, she knew his Sith identity and supported his hidden agenda. Using her species\' innate powers of persuasion and manipulation, Moore helped influence votes and silence opposition. She operated silently, often unnoticed yet never irrelevant. Her presence was unsettling, yet few dared question her authority. As the Republic fell and the Empire rose, Moore remained at Sidious\'s side. She was a rare non-Imperial officer with the Emperor’s full trust. Though she held no official military rank, her political influence was immense. She supervised the disbanding of the Jedi-led systems and shaped early Imperial policy. Despite her importance, little is known of her fate after the Clone Wars. Her legacy lies in the quiet orchestration of tyranny. Sly Moore represents the hidden architects of galactic downfall. She never lifted a weapon, but she helped destroy a galaxy. Her power lay in whispers, not war.','dark','red','2014-12-20T20:18:37.619000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.496000Z',60),
	(83,'Tion Medon','unknown','black','none','206','80','grey','https://starwars.wikia.com/wiki/Tion_Medon','/images/people/83-tion-medon.webp','[\"Galactic Republic\"]','Tion Medon was the administrative portmaster of Pau City on Utapau. Tall and skeletal, he welcomed Obi-Wan Kenobi during the Clone Wars. Though living under Separatist control, he secretly aided the Jedi. Medon provided critical intelligence about General Grievous’s location. His courage was veiled behind calm diplomacy. Tion Medon stood for quiet resistance and hidden bravery.','Tion Medon was a Pau’an native of Utapau and served as the port administrator of Pau City. With his elongated features and solemn presence, he was an imposing yet composed figure. During the Clone Wars, his city fell under Separatist occupation. Medon maintained a facade of neutrality while quietly resisting their rule. When Obi-Wan Kenobi arrived in search of General Grievous, Medon discreetly guided him to the Separatist leader’s hideout. His warning helped launch a vital Republic assault on Utapau. Tion Medon’s diplomacy masked a brave defiance. He risked his life to aid the Jedi without alerting the Separatists. Though not a warrior, his courage shaped the outcome of a key battle. He stayed behind as the conflict raged around him. Medon’s people depended on his careful judgment. His role was one of resilience and wisdom, balancing diplomacy with quiet rebellion. Tion Medon is remembered for the strength it takes to resist from within. He never sought glory, only justice. His legacy is etched in the silent acts of bravery that turn the tide of war.','light',NULL,'2014-12-20T20:35:04.260000Z','2014-12-20T21:17:50.498000Z',12);
