INSERT INTO `planets` (`id`, `name`, `rotation_period`, `orbital_period`, `diameter`, `climate`, `gravity`, `terrain`, `surface_water`, `population`, `created`, `edited`, `image_url`, `short_description`, `long_description`)
VALUES
	(1,'Tatooine','23','304','10465','arid','1 standard','desert','1','200000','2014-12-09T13:50:49.641000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.411000Z','/images/planets/1-tatooine.png','Tatooine is a desert world located in the Outer Rim Territories. It is known for its twin suns and harsh, arid climate. The planet is home to smugglers, moisture farmers, and dangerous creatures. Tatooine played a pivotal role in galactic history as the birthplace of Anakin and home of Luke Skywalker. Its remoteness made it a haven for outlaws and forgotten legends. Tatooine symbolizes hardship, destiny, and unexpected beginnings.','Tatooine is a remote desert planet orbiting twin suns in the Outer Rim Territories. Known for its blistering heat and endless dunes, it is a harsh place to live, but it has shaped some of the most significant figures in galactic history. Moisture farming is the main form of livelihood for its settlers, who live in isolated homesteads. Tatooine is home to various native species, including the Tusken Raiders and Jawas, as well as dangerous beasts like the krayt dragon. It gained galactic notoriety as the home of Anakin Skywalker, who would become Darth Vader, and later as the upbringing world of his son, Luke Skywalker. Despite its obscurity, the planet served as a key setting in several major events. It was the site of Jabba the Hutt\'s criminal empire and a pit stop for smugglers like Han Solo. Obi-Wan Kenobi also hid on Tatooine after Order 66, watching over Luke from afar. The planet has seen everything from podracing to slave trades to Jedi duels. Its remote nature gave it freedom from central control, yet it remained deeply entangled in the fate of the galaxy. Tatooine reflects the theme of unlikely origins and hidden greatness. It remains one of the most iconic and storied planets in galactic lore.'),
	(2,'Alderaan','24','364','12500','temperate','1 standard','grasslands, mountains','40','2000000000','2014-12-10T11:35:48.479000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.420000Z','/images/planets/2-alderaan.webp','Alderaan was a peaceful and beautiful world known for its rich culture and natural beauty. It stood as a beacon of diplomacy and education in the galaxy. The planet was ruled by the House of Organa, including Leia Organa’s adoptive family. Alderaan was destroyed by the Death Star as a show of Imperial force. Its destruction galvanized the Rebel Alliance. Alderaan symbolizes peace, sacrifice, and the cost of tyranny.','Alderaan was a Core Worlds planet known for its lush landscapes, snowy mountains, and commitment to pacifism. Governed by the noble House of Organa, it was a center of art, education, and culture. Under the leadership of Bail Organa, the planet maintained a strong stance against the authoritarian rise of the Galactic Empire. Alderaan offered sanctuary to those fleeing tyranny and played a covert role in the formation of the Rebel Alliance. Its people were known for their strong ethics and civic responsibility. The destruction of Alderaan came suddenly when Grand Moff Tarkin used the Death Star to annihilate it, targeting the planet as a demonstration of the Empire\'s might. This act of terror resulted in the deaths of billions and turned Leia Organa, its princess, into a central figure in the fight against the Empire. The tragedy shocked the galaxy and removed any illusion that the Empire could be reasoned with. The loss of Alderaan fueled rebellion across the stars. While the planet itself no longer exists, its memory endures in the ideals and resolve of its survivors. Alderaan became a symbol of what was lost and what the Rebellion sought to restore. It reminds the galaxy of the high price of oppression and the enduring power of hope.'),
	(3,'Yavin IV','24','4818','10200','temperate, tropical','1 standard','jungle, rainforests','8','1000','2014-12-10T11:37:19.144000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.421000Z','/images/planets/3-yavin-iv.png','Yavin IV is a jungle-covered moon in the Yavin system. It served as a secret base for the Rebel Alliance. Hidden among its ancient Massassi temples, the Rebellion launched its first major strike. It was from here the attack on the first Death Star was planned. Yavin IV became a symbol of underdog defiance. It represents secrecy, bravery, and pivotal beginnings.','Yavin IV, one of the moons orbiting the gas giant Yavin Prime, is blanketed in dense jungle and scattered with the ruins of the ancient Massassi civilization. These temples were repurposed by the Rebel Alliance as their main base of operations during a critical phase of the Galactic Civil War. The location\'s remoteness provided cover from the Empire’s surveillance, making it ideal for strategic planning. From this moon, the Rebellion launched the daring assault on the first Death Star. It was here that Princess Leia brought the stolen Death Star plans, and where Luke Skywalker received his briefing before the Battle of Yavin. The successful destruction of the Death Star marked a turning point in the war and was celebrated across the galaxy. Yavin IV\'s temples became sacred ground for the Rebel cause. Despite later evacuations, the site remained significant in galactic memory. The moon’s natural wilderness added to its mystique, with ancient secrets still hidden beneath the vegetation. Yavin IV is not only a military base, but a symbol of the Rebellion’s ingenuity and courage. It holds a legacy of unlikely victory and unwavering belief in a better future. The battle fought from this moon inspired generations to rise against oppression.'),
	(4,'Hoth','23','549','7200','frozen','1.1 standard','tundra, ice caves, mountain ranges','100','unknown','2014-12-10T11:39:13.934000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.423000Z','/images/planets/4-hoth.webp','Hoth is an icy, desolate planet located in the Outer Rim. It became the site of the Rebel Alliance’s Echo Base. Known for its extreme cold and deadly wildlife, survival there is a challenge. The Empire discovered and attacked the base in the Battle of Hoth. Despite defeat, the Rebellion’s spirit endured. Hoth reflects resilience in the harshest conditions.','Hoth is a frozen wasteland far from the core systems of the galaxy. Covered in snow and glaciers, it is nearly inhospitable to life, yet it became a vital location in the early days of the Galactic Civil War. The Rebel Alliance, on the run after Yavin, established Echo Base deep beneath the ice. Wampas and tauntauns are among the few native lifeforms that manage to survive the cold. The Battle of Hoth became one of the most famous confrontations in galactic history. Using ground speeders and makeshift defenses, the Rebels held off the Imperial onslaught led by Darth Vader and AT-AT walkers. Though ultimately forced to retreat, the Alliance demonstrated courage and unity in the face of overwhelming power. Hoth’s severe climate symbolized the hardship faced by the Rebellion. It was a place where the cause was tested and strengthened. The harsh winds and endless snow mirror the bleak odds the Rebels endured. Yet, even in defeat, their resolve was unbroken. Hoth became a frozen monument to persistence. The memory of Echo Base lingers as a testament to resistance in the cold shadows of tyranny.'),
	(5,'Dagobah','23','341','8900','murky','N/A','swamp, jungles','8','unknown','2014-12-10T11:42:22.590000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.425000Z','/images/planets/5-dagobah.webp','Dagobah is a remote, swamp-covered planet strong in the Force. It served as Yoda\'s exile and Luke Skywalker\'s place of training. The planet is teeming with life, yet devoid of civilization. Hidden in the murky fog, it offers quiet reflection and deep insight. Its isolation made it a sanctuary beyond the reach of the Empire. Dagobah symbolizes mysticism, wisdom, and personal transformation.','Dagobah is a remote world shrouded in dense swamps, tangled vines, and constant mist. It is one of the most obscure planets in the galaxy, unknown to most and deliberately chosen by Jedi Master Yoda as a place of hiding after Order 66. Despite its wild and primitive appearance, Dagobah is unusually strong in the Force, possibly due to the death of a powerful dark side entity in its past. Yoda made a modest home there, using the Force-rich environment to mask his presence from Sith detection. When Luke Skywalker arrived seeking guidance, the planet became a sacred place of Jedi training and revelation. The trials Luke faced were both physical and spiritual, forcing him to confront fear, failure, and his own nature. Dagobah contains a mysterious cave imbued with dark energy, where Luke experienced a chilling vision of Darth Vader and his future self. This planet, though devoid of technology or cities, became a turning point in Luke’s path to becoming a Jedi. Its constant rain, eerie calls of unseen creatures, and unyielding terrain represented the chaos and uncertainty Luke had to navigate within himself. Dagobah taught him the value of patience, humility, and inner strength. It is remembered not for battles or politics, but for deep introspection and growth. Even after Yoda’s death, the planet remains a sacred site of the Jedi legacy. Dagobah endures as a symbol of wisdom emerging from solitude.'),
	(6,'Bespin','12','5110','118000','temperate','1.5 (surface), 1 standard (Cloud City)','gas giant','0','6000000','2014-12-10T11:43:55.240000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.427000Z','/images/planets/6-bespin.webp','Bespin is a gas giant known for its floating Cloud City. It became the site of betrayal, loss, and critical turns in the Galactic Civil War. Lando Calrissian once ruled it with charm and profit. The Empire seized the city, using it to trap Han Solo and his friends. Bespin is remembered for tragedy and resilience. It represents beauty, deception, and unexpected courage.','Bespin is a massive gas giant located in the Anoat sector, with its inhabited Cloud City floating high above the planet’s surface. The city is a mining colony that harvests valuable tibanna gas used in starship weaponry. Operated under the supervision of Lando Calrissian, Cloud City thrived as a neutral, lightly regulated trade outpost. Despite its serene skies and luxurious settings, it became a pivotal setting in the Galactic Civil War. Darth Vader arrived at Cloud City before the Rebels, coercing Lando into betraying his friends. It was here that Han Solo was frozen in carbonite and taken by bounty hunter Boba Fett. The same city witnessed the fateful duel between Luke Skywalker and Darth Vader, culminating in the revelation of Luke’s parentage. The dramatic sequence of events deeply altered the course of the Rebellion. Bespin transformed from a quiet outpost into a symbol of trust broken and bravery awakened. Lando, guilt-ridden over his betrayal, joined the Rebel Alliance and sought redemption. Though not a traditional battleground, Bespin\'s events left scars on the hearts of the heroes. It stands out in memory as a place of suffering and survival. The planet’s layers of clouds mirror the hidden truths and emotional storms experienced there. Bespin remains one of the most visually striking and thematically complex locations in Star Wars lore.'),
	(7,'Endor','18','402','4900','temperate','0.85 standard','forests, mountains, lakes','8','30000000','2014-12-10T11:50:29.349000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.429000Z','/images/planets/7-endor.webp','Endor is a forest moon known for its lush greenery and brave Ewok inhabitants. It became the final battleground of the Galactic Civil War. The Rebel Alliance destroyed the second Death Star above its skies. Endor\'s natives played a crucial role in the Rebel victory. The moon represents unity, courage, and the fall of tyranny. Endor is a symbol of nature triumphing over machines.','Endor, often called the Forest Moon of Endor, orbits the gas giant of the same name and is covered in towering trees, dense underbrush, and a vibrant ecosystem. Despite its primitive appearance, Endor became the site of one of the most decisive battles in the galaxy. The second Death Star was constructed in its orbit, with a protective shield generator based on the moon\'s surface. The Rebel Alliance launched a desperate mission to destroy the generator and give their fleet a chance to end the war. Unexpectedly, the native Ewoks, small but courageous forest dwellers, allied with the Rebels. Their knowledge of the terrain and use of guerrilla tactics proved vital. Stormtroopers and Imperial walkers were overwhelmed by traps, logs, and unyielding resistance. Above the moon, Luke Skywalker confronted Darth Vader and Emperor Palpatine, culminating in Anakin Skywalker\'s return and the Emperor’s demise. The Death Star exploded in Endor’s sky, marking the end of the Empire\'s dominance. The moon itself became a symbol of hope and alliance between civilizations. Its serene nature contrasted with the ferocity of the conflict, highlighting the theme that strength lies not only in firepower but in unity and heart. Endor’s forests echoed with celebration, drums, and the dawn of peace. It remains a place where the smallest allies made the greatest difference.'),
	(8,'Naboo','26','312','12120','temperate','1 standard','grassy hills, swamps, forests, mountains','12','4500000000','2014-12-10T11:52:31.066000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.430000Z','/images/planets/8-naboo.webp','Naboo is a serene and elegant planet rich with culture and natural beauty. It is home to both human and Gungan civilizations. Known for its lakes and cities, Naboo shaped both Padmé Amidala and Emperor Palpatine. It has seen war and peace, royalty and revolution. Naboo symbolizes balance between nature and civilization. It reflects harmony, heritage, and hidden power.','Naboo is a lush, picturesque planet located in the Chommell sector of the Mid Rim. Known for its rolling plains, sparkling lakes, and classical architecture, it is home to two intelligent species—the surface-dwelling humans and the underwater Gungans. Despite their cultural differences, both societies are deeply rooted in tradition and nature. The capital, Theed, is renowned for its art and diplomacy. Naboo gave rise to influential figures such as Queen Padmé Amidala, a noble leader, and Sheev Palpatine, who would rise to become Emperor. During the Invasion of Naboo, the Trade Federation blockaded and invaded the planet, triggering the events that led to the fall of the Republic. It was on Naboo that Anakin Skywalker first displayed his abilities and met Padmé. The planet later became a romantic refuge for the pair. Naboo saw the beginnings of galactic conflict but also moments of peace and unity, especially when the humans and Gungans allied to repel invaders. Though outwardly peaceful, Naboo\'s political influence reached the galaxy\'s core. Its story is a reminder that greatness can come from places of grace. The planet remains a symbol of aesthetic beauty, wisdom in leadership, and the dual paths of light and dark that emerged from its soil.'),
	(9,'Coruscant','24','368','12240','temperate','1 standard','cityscape, mountains','unknown','1000000000000','2014-12-10T11:54:13.921000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.432000Z','/images/planets/9-coruscant.jpg','Coruscant is the galactic capital, a city-covered planet symbolizing civilization’s peak. It is home to the Senate, Jedi Temple, and political intrigue. Beneath its shining towers lie shadows of corruption. Many galactic events began or ended here. Coruscant is the heart of politics, culture, and power. It represents order, ambition, and perilous control.','Coruscant is a planet entirely covered by a sprawling cityscape, the political and cultural hub of the galaxy for millennia. Located in the Core Worlds, it hosted the Galactic Senate, Jedi Temple, and other major institutions of the Republic. Its surface consists of towering skyscrapers, speeder highways, and endless districts stacked upon one another. While the upper levels shine with privilege, the lower levels fall into darkness, crime, and poverty. Coruscant was the seat of Chancellor Palpatine\'s power, who secretly orchestrated the fall of the Republic and the rise of the Empire. It was here that Anakin Skywalker succumbed to the dark side and helped execute Order 66. The Jedi Temple was ransacked, and the Sith finally claimed control over the galaxy. Despite its corruption, Coruscant has also been a beacon of law, knowledge, and diplomacy. The planet serves as a complex symbol—where ideals were born and betrayed. Its ever-busy skyline reflects the constant tension between progress and decay. Coruscant is the center of influence, where every choice can shape the galaxy’s destiny. It is both magnificent and terrifying in its reach and depth.'),
	(10,'Kamino','27','463','19720','temperate','1 standard','ocean','100','1000000000','2014-12-10T12:45:06.577000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.434000Z','/images/planets/10-kamino.png','Kamino is an ocean world perpetually battered by storms. Hidden from many maps, it housed the Republic’s secret clone army. Its cities rise above endless waves. The Kaminoans mastered genetic science in sterile isolation. Kamino symbolizes control, creation, and ethical uncertainty. It reflects the calm before the clone wars\' storm.','Kamino is a remote planet located beyond the Outer Rim, surrounded by constant rain and violent seas. Its civilization resides in elegant, towering cities elevated above the endless ocean. The Kaminoans, tall and soft-spoken beings, are known for their advanced cloning technology. Discovered only through an erased archive entry, Kamino became the secret cradle of the Grand Army of the Republic. Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi traced an assassination plot to Kamino and found the clone army created from the bounty hunter Jango Fett. Though they claimed to serve the Republic, the clones were programmed with hidden orders that would later doom the Jedi. Kamino represents scientific mastery but also moral ambiguity. Its quiet halls and sterile labs contrast with the chaos its clones would unleash. The Kaminoans viewed their work with clinical detachment, never engaging in the wars their creations fought. Kamino embodies themes of artificial life, secrecy, and unintended consequences. The stormy backdrop mirrors the turmoil beneath its calm surface. It stands as the origin of a manipulated war, hidden behind polished glass and rain-soaked skies. Kamino is both marvel and warning, an example of how creation without conscience can change the fate of galaxies.'),
	(11,'Geonosis','30','256','11370','temperate, arid','0.9 standard','rock, desert, mountain, barren','5','100000000000','2014-12-10T12:47:22.350000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.437000Z','/images/planets/11-geonosis.webp','Geonosis is a rocky desert planet known for its towering spires and industrial hives. It was the site of the Clone Wars\' first battle. Home to the Geonosians, the planet was central to Death Star construction. It harbored separatist factories and dark secrets. The red dust of Geonosis witnessed Jedi sacrifice. It symbolizes war’s beginning and sinister engineering.','Geonosis is a harsh, arid world orbiting a red star in the Outer Rim. Its landscape is dominated by jagged rock formations and sprawling hive structures built by its insectoid native species, the Geonosians. Long isolated, Geonosis gained galactic infamy as the birthplace of the Separatist movement and the setting for the Clone Wars\' first large-scale battle. Count Dooku and the Confederacy of Independent Systems planned their war from this planet, and its foundries produced battle droids by the millions. It was here that Obi-Wan Kenobi uncovered the droid army, leading to the Jedi rescue mission and the arena battle that ended in full war. The planet’s catacombs also secretly housed early construction of the Death Star. Despite the loss of the war, the Geonosians remained deeply tied to the Empire’s darker ambitions. Over time, the population was decimated, their planet poisoned to protect imperial secrets. Geonosis became a silent graveyard of betrayal and blind industry. Its dusty fields and grim history serve as a cautionary tale about unchecked militarization. The world is remembered not only for battles, but for the secrets buried beneath its crimson soil.'),
	(12,'Utapau','27','351','12900','temperate, arid, windy','1 standard','scrublands, savanna, canyons, sinkholes','0.9','95000000','2014-12-10T12:49:01.491000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.439000Z','/images/planets/12-utapau.webp','Utapau is a sinkhole-filled planet hidden in the galaxy’s shadows. Known for its vertical cities and native Pau’ans, it played a role in the Clone Wars’ climax. General Grievous hid there before his final battle. Obi-Wan Kenobi\'s duel brought the war closer to its end. Utapau is a quiet world of depth and final confrontations.','Utapau is a remote planet marked by its massive sinkholes, each housing vertical cities and complex communities. The planet’s surface is barren and windswept, but deep underground lies Pau City and other settlements carved into the cliffs. Home to the tall, sunken-eyed Pau’ans and their shorter neighbors, the Utai, the world was long overlooked until the late Clone Wars. General Grievous chose Utapau as a secret refuge for the Separatist leadership. Obi-Wan Kenobi discovered his location and faced him in a decisive duel, riding the swift varactyl Boga through the vertical terrain. The battle ended with Grievous\' death, significantly weakening the Separatists. Though the Republic seemed victorious, this event marked the prelude to Emperor Palpatine’s ascension and the Jedi’s fall. Utapau is symbolic of hidden depths—both literal and political. Its people maintained neutrality and bore witness to galactic shifts they could not control. The quiet planet became a turning point in history. It remains etched in memory for its vertical spires, quiet dignity, and the calm before the galactic storm.'),
	(13,'Mustafar','36','412','4200','hot','1 standard','volcanoes, lava rivers, mountains, caves','0','20000','2014-12-10T12:50:16.526000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.440000Z','/images/planets/13-mustafar.webp','Mustafar is a volcanic planet where fire rules and fate is sealed. It became the battleground for Anakin and Obi-Wan’s final duel. Rivers of lava surround the ancient Sith ruins. Here, Anakin fell, and Darth Vader rose. Mustafar represents transformation through pain. It is fire, fury, and the ashes of brotherhood.','Mustafar is a hellish volcanic world located in the Outer Rim. The planet’s surface is riddled with lava flows, volcanic eruptions, and metal facilities that extract valuable minerals from its fiery crust. Once used by ancient Sith for dark rituals, Mustafar pulsed with dark side energy long before the Clone Wars. It gained tragic renown as the setting for Anakin Skywalker\'s final steps into darkness. Ordered by Emperor Palpatine to destroy the Separatist leadership, Anakin massacred them here, cementing his turn. Obi-Wan Kenobi followed him to Mustafar, confronting his former apprentice in one of the saga’s most iconic and devastating lightsaber duels. The battle left Anakin burned and broken, only to be rebuilt as Darth Vader. Mustafar thus became the birthplace of the Empire’s enforcer. Later, Vader made the planet his home, constructing a fortress atop ancient Sith grounds. The constant firestorm around the fortress mirrored the inner torment of its resident. Mustafar embodies rage, loss, and rebirth through pain. Its landscape burns as eternally as the wounds it carved into the galaxy’s fate.'),
	(14,'Kashyyyk','26','381','12765','tropical','1 standard','jungle, forests, lakes, rivers','60','45000000','2014-12-10T13:32:00.124000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.442000Z','/images/planets/14-kashyyyk.webp','Kashyyyk is a lush, tree-covered planet home to the Wookiees. Its tall wroshyr trees house cities in their canopies. During the Clone Wars, it saw fierce fighting. The Empire enslaved many of its natives. Kashyyyk represents strength, loyalty, and the bonds of family. It is the heart of Wookiee pride and resilience.','Kashyyyk is a verdant planet covered in towering wroshyr trees, the tallest of which rise kilometers above the forest floor. The Wookiees, a noble and fierce species, live in treetop cities that blend architecture with nature. Kashyyyk\'s landscape is rich in biodiversity, but also treacherous, as deadly creatures lurk in the underbrush. During the Clone Wars, the planet became a battleground when the Separatists invaded. Jedi Master Yoda led Republic forces in its defense alongside loyal Wookiees like Chewbacca and Tarfful. The celebration of victory was short-lived, as Order 66 turned the clone army against the Jedi. Later, the Empire enslaved many Wookiees, stripping Kashyyyk of its peace. The planet endured hardship but remained a symbol of unity and resistance. Wookiees continued to fight back, aiding the Rebellion and rebuilding what was lost. Kashyyyk embodies the strength of tradition and the tenacity of a people bound by honor. Its towering forests tell a story of valor, betrayal, and endurance rooted in the soil of home.'),
	(15,'Polis Massa','24','590','0','artificial temperate ','0.56 standard','airless asteroid','0','1000000','2014-12-10T13:33:46.405000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.444000Z','/images/planets/15-polis-massa.webp','Polis Massa is an asteroid colony hidden in deep space. It is known for its advanced medical facilities and secrecy. The Rebellion used it after the fall of the Jedi. Padmé Amidala gave birth here to Luke and Leia. Polis Massa represents refuge and the beginning of hope. It is quiet, sterile, and sacred.','Polis Massa is not a traditional planet, but an asteroid settlement carved into the remnants of a shattered world. Its original inhabitants were lost to history, and in their place, off-world miners and scientists built sterile research labs and medical centers. It was to this hidden colony that Bail Organa, Obi-Wan Kenobi, and Yoda fled after the fall of the Jedi Order. Here, Padmé Amidala gave birth to her twins, Luke and Leia, before passing away. The event marked both tragedy and hope—the end of one era and the quiet start of another. Polis Massa’s isolation provided safety from the Empire’s reach. Its silent halls, dim lighting, and austere design created an atmosphere of solemnity. Though it witnessed one of the galaxy’s most emotional moments, it remained impartial, a place of life and death beyond politics. Polis Massa is remembered as the cradle of the next generation. Its legacy is whispered, not shouted, yet its importance is undeniable. The cold rock in deep space holds the spark that would one day reignite the flame of the Jedi.'),
	(16,'Mygeeto','12','167','10088','frigid','1 standard','glaciers, mountains, ice canyons','unknown','19000000','2014-12-10T13:43:39.139000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.446000Z','/images/planets/16-mygeeto.webp','Mygeeto is a freezing, war-torn world filled with icy skyscrapers. Its wealth funded the Separatist cause. Jedi fought and died among its ruins. The planet is rich in kyber crystals hidden beneath frost. Mygeeto stands for loss, deception, and the hidden price of power. It echoes with betrayal beneath its chill surface.','Mygeeto is a crystalline, snow-covered planet that served as a financial center and strategic battleground during the Clone Wars. Dominated by frigid winds and glittering skyscrapers, the world is both beautiful and brutal. It was governed by the InterGalactic Banking Clan, which aligned itself with the Separatists. Jedi General Ki-Adi-Mundi led clone battalions into fierce combat amid its ice-blasted ruins. Unknown to most, kyber crystals mined here were used to secretly power the Death Star’s superlaser. Near the end of the war, Mygeeto became one of the many fronts where Jedi were slaughtered during Order 66. Ki-Adi-Mundi fell to his own troops in a moment of betrayal. The planet\'s surface became littered with wreckage and the cold memories of conflict. Mygeeto reflects the silent greed and sacrifice embedded in war. Its financial prestige masked sinister investments in destruction. Even now, its glittering facades hide buried scars. Mygeeto is a frozen stage where honor was traded for obedience, and power grew in shadow.'),
	(17,'Felucia','34','231','9100','hot, humid','0.75 standard','fungus forests','unknown','8500000','2014-12-10T13:44:50.397000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.447000Z','/images/planets/17-felucia.webp','Felucia is a vibrant jungle world bursting with bizarre plant life. Its beauty masks lethal danger. Jedi Aayla Secura died here during Order 66. The planet is both wild and haunting. It represents fragile harmony broken by violence. Felucia is life at its most vivid and its most tragic.','Felucia is one of the galaxy’s most visually striking planets, its surface covered in towering fungi, glowing spores, and alien plant life. The jungle world pulses with color and strangeness, but its beauty conceals a deadly ecosystem. Clone forces battled Separatists across Felucia’s shifting terrain during the Clone Wars. Jedi General Aayla Secura was stationed here and ultimately assassinated by her clone troopers during Order 66. Her sudden death among the luminous foliage is one of the war’s most tragic images. Felucia’s wildness made it nearly impossible to tame. It shifted allegiances and control as different factions tried to exploit or survive it. The planet also played a minor role during the Empire\'s reign, becoming a place of exile, conflict, and forgotten skirmishes. Felucia reflects the theme of life’s unpredictability—gorgeous and strange, nurturing and lethal. It reminds us that chaos and beauty often coexist. The glowing jungle remains untouched by civilization, echoing with the whispers of lost Jedi and the songs of alien life. Felucia is vivid, sacred, and sorrowful.'),
	(18,'Cato Neimoidia','25','278','0','temperate, moist','1 standard','mountains, fields, forests, rock arches','unknown','10000000','2014-12-10T13:46:28.704000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.449000Z','/images/planets/18-cato-neimoidia.webp','Cato Neimoidia is a wealthy, bridge-world known for its luxurious hanging cities. It served as a stronghold for the Trade Federation. The planet’s political ties were often suspect. Jedi were deployed there during the Clone Wars. Suspicion and secrecy mark its reputation. Cato Neimoidia symbolizes opulence mixed with treachery.','Cato Neimoidia is one of the wealthiest of the Neimoidian purse worlds, famous for its grand cities suspended by bridges between steep mountain ranges. Its landscape is breathtaking, with cloud-covered valleys and refined architecture reflecting the planet\'s elite culture. The planet was central to the Trade Federation’s operations, often caught between commerce and corruption. During the Clone Wars, Cato Neimoidia was occupied by Separatist forces and became the site of fierce engagements involving Jedi and Republic troops. One such confrontation led to the death of Jedi Master Plo Koon during Order 66. Though technologically advanced, the planet was always under scrutiny for its loyalties and hidden agendas. Its leaders were known for valuing profit over principle. Cato Neimoidia’s beauty masks a long history of manipulation and double-dealing. Even in times of peace, it operated in the gray zone of galactic politics. The planet is a monument to excess, shadow diplomacy, and the thin line between neutrality and betrayal.'),
	(19,'Saleucami','26','392','14920','hot','unknown','caves, desert, mountains, volcanoes','unknown','1400000000','2014-12-10T13:47:46.874000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.450000Z','/images/planets/19-saleucami.webp','Saleucami is a dry, crater-filled world once home to intense conflict. Its surface bears signs of heavy bombardment and military occupation. Jedi fought on its plains during the Clone Wars. The planet reflects hardship and sacrifice. Saleucami stands for forgotten battlefields and resilience in the face of devastation.','Saleucami is a harsh, semi-arid world characterized by massive craters, sparse vegetation, and underground lava flows. Despite its desolate appearance, it became a vital battleground during the Clone Wars due to its strategic location. The planet was fortified by Separatist forces and saw prolonged engagements with Republic armies. Jedi Master Stass Allie was stationed there and tragically killed during Order 66 while riding a speeder bike through the open plains. The world’s terrain offered little cover, making it a perilous front for both sides. Saleucami\'s surface is dotted with remnants of conflict—crashed ships, buried bunkers, and echoes of fallen warriors. It lacks the glory of better-known planets but bears the scars of sacrifice. For the clones and Jedi who served there, it was a place of duty and struggle. Saleucami reflects the often-overlooked costs of war and the forgotten valor of its participants. Its cracked soil holds the memories of courage under fire.'),
	(20,'Stewjon','unknown','unknown','0','temperate','1 standard','grass','unknown','unknown','2014-12-10T16:16:26.566000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.452000Z','/images/planets/20-stewjon.png','Stewjon is a quiet, lesser-known planet in the galaxy. It is famously the birthplace of Obi-Wan Kenobi. Little is known about its culture or landscape. Its mystery preserves a sense of sacredness. Stewjon symbolizes humble beginnings and Jedi destiny. It is the start of a legendary path.','Stewjon is a remote and scarcely documented world within the galaxy. It gained prominence solely due to its association with Jedi Master Obi-Wan Kenobi, who was born there before being taken to the Jedi Temple on Coruscant. The planet’s terrain, climate, and society remain largely a mystery, with no records of significant political or military involvement. In its anonymity lies symbolic power—it represents the modest roots from which greatness can arise. Obi-Wan’s journey from this forgotten planet to the heart of galactic history speaks to the Jedi’s practice of detachment and universal duty. Stewjon remains an enigmatic world, untouched by the wars and politics that shaped much of the galaxy. Its silence and mystery elevate its meaning, suggesting that not all origins require grandeur to leave an impact. It is a reminder that the Force flows even from the quietest places. Stewjon is stillness, simplicity, and the unspoken beginning of a legend.'),
	(21,'Eriadu','24','360','13490','polluted','1 standard','cityscape','unknown','22000000000','2014-12-10T16:26:54.384000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.454000Z','/images/planets/21-eriadu.webp','Eriadu is an industrial hub and a symbol of human ambition. Known for pollution and rapid growth, it mirrors Coruscant’s darker edges. It is the homeworld of Grand Moff Tarkin. The planet’s rise reflects order through control. Eriadu stands for authority, discipline, and ruthless progress.','Eriadu is located in the Outer Rim and is often seen as a harsh reflection of Coruscant. Once a modest world, its rapid industrialization transformed it into a smog-choked metropolis dominated by factories and starship production facilities. The Tarkin family rose to prominence here, embodying the planet’s rigid ideals of structure, power, and control. Wilhuff Tarkin, later Grand Moff Tarkin, championed the view that fear and order must reign supreme to maintain peace. Eriadu’s development mirrored this philosophy, valuing efficiency over compassion. Its citizens embraced discipline and militaristic pride, feeding directly into the future Imperial doctrine. The planet became a model for the Empire’s vision of enforced order. Though not inherently evil, Eriadu\'s trajectory shows the dangerous allure of control unchecked by empathy. It remains a world of achievement, but at a cost. Its factories fueled the war machine, and its doctrines echoed in the galaxy’s darkest policies. Eriadu is ambition hardened into command.'),
	(22,'Corellia','25','329','11000','temperate','1 standard','plains, urban, hills, forests','70','3000000000','2014-12-10T16:49:12.453000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.456000Z','/images/planets/22-corellia.webp','Corellia is a bustling world of shipyards, speed, and rebellious spirit. Famous for its pilots and starships, it values independence and skill. Han Solo was born here. The planet mixes crime, innovation, and pride. Corellia stands for daring, craftsmanship, and freedom. It thrives on motion and edge.','Corellia is a vital core world known throughout the galaxy for its top-tier shipyards and talented pilots. The world is home to sprawling cities, busy spaceports, and a culture of innovation and speed. Its people are fiercely independent, often valuing self-reliance and daring over law and order. Han Solo, one of the most iconic smugglers and heroes of the Rebellion, was born and raised on Corellia. The planet’s capital, Coronet City, bustles with trade, corruption, and ingenuity. Corellians built ships like the Millennium Falcon—fast, tough, and customizable. Though aligned with the Republic and later the Empire, many citizens were involved in black market activity and anti-authoritarian movements. Corellia’s soul lies in its resistance to control and its passion for freedom. It is a world where the line between hero and outlaw blurs. The planet symbolizes the balance between talent and risk, loyalty and rebellion. Corellia is speed, savvy, and stars.'),
	(23,'Rodia','29','305','7549','hot','1 standard','jungles, oceans, urban, swamps','60','1300000000','2014-12-10T17:03:28.110000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.458000Z','/images/planets/23-rodia.webp','Rodia is a swampy jungle planet home to the Rodians. Known for its hunter culture and vibrant wildlife, it is both beautiful and perilous. Greedo hailed from here. Rodia struggles with corruption and legacy. The planet represents ambition clashing with tradition. It is green, wild, and restless.','Rodia is a humid, lush world covered in thick swamps, dense jungles, and towering trees. The Rodians, its native species, developed a culture centered on hunting, survival, and competition. Over time, they became known as bounty hunters, driven by honor and desperation to earn prestige. Greedo, the ill-fated Rodian who confronted Han Solo, was a product of this environment. Rodia’s leadership often grappled with political instability, swinging between loyalty to larger galactic powers and internal corruption. Though it once suffered from isolation and resource scarcity, the planet eventually modernized, gaining representation in the Republic. Its cities are a contrast of tradition and expansion, where ancient customs meet galactic industry. Rodia remains proud and complex—a world of ambition, tangled alliances, and fierce independence. Its marshy terrain mirrors the challenges faced by its people: always navigating thick obstacles. Rodia is a planet of survivalists with dreams that sometimes outpace reality.'),
	(24,'Nal Hutta','87','413','12150','temperate','1 standard','urban, oceans, swamps, bogs','unknown','7000000000','2014-12-10T17:11:29.452000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.460000Z','/images/planets/24-nal-hutta.webp','Nal Hutta is the Hutt homeworld, a murky swamp of decadence and crime. It is the heart of Hutt space and underworld dealings. Slime-covered palaces line its bogs. The planet oozes greed and domination. Nal Hutta represents corruption, power, and self-indulgence. It is rot made empire.','Nal Hutta, literally \'Glorious Jewel\' in Huttese, is an ironic name for one of the galaxy’s most infamous cesspools. The planet is a humid swamp covered in bogs, mists, and fungal growth. It serves as the capital of Hutt Space and the political center of the Hutt Cartel. From its slime-coated cities, crime lords rule vast networks of smuggling, slavery, and vice. Jabba the Hutt and his kin hold feasts and decrees in palaces rising from murky marshes. The native Evocii were displaced by the Hutts centuries ago, their history buried beneath opulence and waste. Despite its decay, Nal Hutta is immensely influential, feared rather than respected. The planet attracts criminals, mercenaries, and those seeking deals outside the law. Its air is thick with corruption and entitlement. Nal Hutta is a grotesque monument to unchecked indulgence and dominion. Where others see ruin, the Hutts see profit. It is the throne world of sin, gluttony, and power wielded without shame.'),
	(25,'Dantooine','25','378','9830','temperate','1 standard','oceans, savannas, mountains, grasslands','unknown','1000','2014-12-10T17:23:29.896000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.461000Z','/images/planets/25-dantooine.webp','Dantooine is a quiet, grassy world once used by the Rebel Alliance. Its peaceful plains hide deep political echoes. Though remote, it played a part in galactic resistance. The planet holds ancient Jedi ruins and rebel memories. It symbolizes hidden strength and missed opportunity. Dantooine stands for calm amidst turbulence.','Dantooine is a remote planet known for its wide-open grasslands, gentle rivers, and rustic beauty. Though lacking in major industry or large cities, it was once home to a Rebel Alliance base. That base was abandoned prior to the destruction of Alderaan, but its existence became known when Princess Leia misled the Empire about the Rebels’ location. Despite being spared from destruction, Dantooine\'s quiet fields became associated with deception, sacrifice, and survival. Long before the Rebellion, the planet also housed ancient Jedi ruins, evidence of a once-thriving Force-sensitive presence. Its lack of strategic value kept it out of the main theaters of war, yet it remained symbolically important. Dantooine is a world where power operates in silence and solitude. It reflects the persistence of hope in unassuming places. Though often forgotten, its role in the galactic struggle endures through its stories. Dantooine represents the strength of the unseen and the cost of staying hidden.'),
	(26,'Bestine IV','26','680','6400','temperate','unknown','rocky islands, oceans','98','62000000','2014-12-12T11:16:55.078000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.463000Z','/images/planets/26-bestine-iv.webp','Bestine IV is an arid planet with Imperial significance. Known for its military outposts and strategic value, it served the Empire’s expansion. The planet’s dry lands see little comfort. Bestine IV symbolizes compliance through strength. It is a reminder of Imperial reach and localized control.','Bestine IV is a desert world located in the Outer Rim, known for its harsh climate and windswept terrain. Despite its environment, it became an important Imperial garrison world, hosting facilities and listening stations. The planet\'s population was kept under tight control, with loyalty to the Empire maintained through force and surveillance. Its main settlement served both as an industrial hub and a launching point for operations in nearby sectors. Bestine IV held no natural beauty or valuable resources but was prized for its strategic positioning. As such, it became a symbol of the Empire’s policy of domination by presence. For many of its residents, life meant obedience and endurance. Its quiet subjugation reflects the Empire’s reach into even the most mundane worlds. Bestine IV exemplifies how everyday places became gears in a galactic machine. It stands as a testament to occupation, order, and the cost of silence.'),
	(27,'Ord Mantell','26','334','14050','temperate','1 standard','plains, seas, mesas','10','4000000000','2014-12-15T12:23:41.661000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.464000Z','/images/planets/27-ord-mantell.webp','Ord Mantell is a rugged world marked by lawlessness and war. Known for bounty hunters and scrapyards, it plays host to conflict. Smugglers and outlaws roam freely. The planet represents the shadowed middle ground. Ord Mantell is risk, betrayal, and survival by wits.','Ord Mantell is a gritty, chaotic planet located in the Mid Rim, once known as a military depot and later overrun by criminals and mercenaries. Its terrain includes scrapyards, industrial zones, and abandoned war machines. Once a haven for smugglers and bounty hunters, the planet has a reputation for dirty deals and treacherous betrayals. Han Solo referenced a run-in with a bounty hunter there, a pivotal moment in his decision to leave the Rebellion. Ord Mantell has been a battleground for underworld rivalries and an unofficial marketplace for black-market goods. It is a world of blurred loyalties and shifting alliances. Despite its grime and corruption, the planet is alive with commerce and raw energy. People survive not by strength alone but through cunning and deal-making. Ord Mantell reflects the moral gray zone between galactic powers. It stands as a mirror to the galaxy’s underside, where choices are made in shadow.'),
	(28,'unknown','0','0','0','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-15T12:25:59.569000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.466000Z','/images/planets/28-unknown.png','A mysterious place. No maps. Probably full of lost socks and lightsabers.',NULL),
	(29,'Trandosha','25','371','0','arid','0.62 standard','mountains, seas, grasslands, deserts','unknown','42000000','2014-12-15T12:53:47.695000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.468000Z','/images/planets/29-trandosha.png','Trandosha is the fearsome homeworld of the Trandoshans. It is a jungle-filled planet devoted to the hunt. Wookiees are their traditional prey. The world is steeped in blood, honor, and pursuit. Trandosha represents savage strength and predatory pride. It is a planet of hunters.','Trandosha is a lush, hostile jungle planet in the same star system as Kashyyyk. It is home to the Trandoshans, a reptilian species known for their aggressive culture centered on hunting. The planet’s surface is dense with thick forests and wild beasts, all serving as arenas for proving one’s worth. The Trandoshans revere a goddess-like entity known as the Scorekeeper, who rewards hunts and tallies victories. Slavery and bounty hunting are central to their economy and identity. Wookiees are often captured and enslaved by Trandoshans, creating a historic enmity between the two races. Bossk, one of the galaxy’s most feared bounty hunters, hails from this world. Trandosha symbolizes relentless survival, dominance through conquest, and glory through violence. Its beauty masks a brutal way of life. To step foot on Trandosha is to enter a world where you’re either the hunter—or the hunted.'),
	(30,'Socorro','20','326','0','arid','1 standard','deserts, mountains','unknown','300000000','2014-12-15T12:56:31.121000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.469000Z','/images/planets/30-socorro.png','Socorro is a harsh desert world known for its outlaws and drifters. The planet thrives in shadow. Smugglers use its dust-choked surface for shelter. It is a place where stories vanish into sand. Socorro symbolizes freedom beyond law. It is rebellion, wind, and dust.','Socorro is a barren, unforgiving desert planet located in the Outer Rim Territories. Its surface is dominated by rocky canyons, dry riverbeds, and scattered settlements filled with rogues, nomads, and outcasts. Socorro’s inhospitable environment makes it the perfect haven for smugglers and exiles, especially those wishing to avoid Imperial scrutiny. Many criminal networks maintain hidden bases there, taking advantage of the planet’s remoteness. Socorro is also known for its wandering storyteller clans and oral traditions. The people live simply, but fiercely defend their independence. Tales of lost ships and forgotten rebels drift on the desert wind. The planet is often spoken of in hushed tones—a place where debts are buried and identities erased. Socorro embodies resistance to order, life at the margins, and the myths that grow in forgotten places. It thrives in obscurity, where freedom is earned rather than granted.'),
	(31,'Mon Cala','21','398','11030','temperate','1','oceans, reefs, islands','100','27000000000','2014-12-18T11:07:01.792000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.471000Z','/images/planets/31-mon-cala.webp','Mon Cala is an ocean planet ruled by the Mon Calamari. Its seas hold cities of coral and light. The planet resisted the Empire fiercely. Admiral Ackbar hailed from here. Mon Cala is honor, resistance, and unity. It is a beacon beneath the waves.','Mon Cala, also known as Mon Calamari, is a beautiful ocean world with no dry land. Its cities rise from beneath the sea in elegant, coral-inspired structures. The Mon Calamari and the Quarren are the two native species, each with distinct roles and traditions. The Mon Calamari were peaceful, artistic, and inventive—yet when the Empire arrived, they did not yield. They supported the Rebellion with their advanced starships and military leadership. Admiral Ackbar, one of the most respected figures in the Rebel Alliance, came from Mon Cala. The planet\'s defense of freedom was not without cost—its cities were bombarded and its people enslaved. But Mon Cala never stopped fighting. It became a symbol of coordinated resistance and moral clarity. Its watery depths hold stories of courage and sacrifice. Mon Cala stands for the strength of unity against oppression, even from the depths of the sea.'),
	(32,'Chandrila','20','368','13500','temperate','1','plains, forests','40','1200000000','2014-12-18T11:11:51.872000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.472000Z','/images/planets/32-chandrila.png','Chandrila is a peaceful, democratic Core World. It is home to leaders and visionaries. The planet values education, liberty, and open debate. Mon Mothma was born here. Chandrila represents hope and political courage. It is the Republic’s heart reborn.','Chandrila is a lush, temperate planet in the Core Worlds known for its strong democratic traditions and civic institutions. Its landscape includes rolling hills, rivers, and well-planned cities focused on harmony and sustainability. The planet has produced many influential leaders, including Mon Mothma, who helped found the Rebel Alliance. Chandrila was one of the few worlds that maintained its ideals through Republic, Empire, and New Republic eras. It became the first capital of the New Republic after the fall of the Empire. Chandrila’s people prize diplomacy, education, and personal freedom. The planet’s Senate chambers hosted critical debates that helped reshape galactic order. Even in times of war, Chandrila stood as a voice of reason and reform. It reflects the best of the Republic’s values: justice, peace, and accountability. Chandrila reminds the galaxy that leadership grounded in principle can endure and inspire across generations.'),
	(33,'Sullust','20','263','12780','superheated','1','mountains, volcanoes, rocky deserts','5','18500000000','2014-12-18T11:25:40.243000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.474000Z','/images/planets/33-sullust.webp','Sullust is a volcanic world of fire and stone. Its surface is uninhabitable, but vast cities thrive underground. The Sullustans are clever, loyal, and resourceful. The planet supported the Rebel Alliance with technology and industry. Sullust symbolizes endurance under pressure. It is lava, loyalty, and innovation.','Sullust is a fiery, volcanic planet located in the Outer Rim, known for its hostile surface covered in rivers of lava and toxic fumes. Due to these conditions, the native Sullustans developed advanced subterranean cities where they built a highly industrialized society. Despite its harsh environment, Sullust became a critical center for starship production and military logistics. The Sullustans are known for their technical skill, adaptability, and strong sense of community. During the Galactic Civil War, the planet’s people aligned themselves with the Rebel Alliance, contributing vital resources, ships, and intelligence. Admiral Raddus, a Mon Calamari commander, launched the assault on Scarif from Sullust. The planet’s strategic importance made it a target, yet it resisted Imperial control through resilience and clever defense. Sullust stands as a symbol of defiant productivity, building progress from beneath the surface of destruction. It is a world where ingenuity rises from the depths.'),
	(34,'Toydaria','21','184','7900','temperate','1','swamps, lakes','unknown','11000000','2014-12-19T17:47:54.403000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.476000Z','/images/planets/34-toydaria.png','Toydaria is a swampy planet ruled by shrewd merchants. Its native Toydarians are immune to Jedi mind tricks. The world is rich in trade but poor in sympathy. Toydaria once held neutrality but leaned toward the Republic. It symbolizes cunning and independence. Toydaria is commerce in the mire.','Toydaria is a humid, marsh-covered world inhabited by the winged Toydarians, a species known for their mental resilience and strong business acumen. The terrain is difficult to navigate, with dense swamps and floating settlements. Toydaria\'s society is hierarchical but based around negotiation and trade. Despite its rough exterior, the planet is strategically important due to its location near Hutt Space and trade routes. The most famous Toydarian is Watto, a junk dealer who owned Anakin and Shmi Skywalker during their enslavement. During the Clone Wars, Toydaria initially claimed neutrality but eventually supported the Republic by offering aid and diplomacy. Its leaders valued sovereignty and economic autonomy above all. The Toydarians’ resistance to Force persuasion made them formidable in negotiations. Toydaria represents a realm where power lies in words, trade, and the ability to resist manipulation. It is a world that trades mud for influence.'),
	(35,'Malastare','26','201','18880','arid, temperate, tropical','1.56','swamps, deserts, jungles, mountains','unknown','2000000000','2014-12-19T17:52:13.106000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.478000Z','/images/planets/35-malastare.webp','Malastare is a rocky world famous for podracing. It is the home of the Dug species. The planet blends brutal sport with industrial utility. It supported the Republic but flirted with the Separatists. Malastare reflects speed, danger, and shifting allegiances.','Malastare is a dry, cratered planet located in the Mid Rim. It is best known for its dangerous podracing tracks and harsh industrial zones. The native Dugs are agile and proud, often at odds with the ruling Gran settlers who dominate the political and economic systems. Malastare hosted podracing events that attracted racers from across the galaxy, including the famed Boonta Eve Classic. The world also held vast fuel reserves and production facilities, making it economically vital. During the Clone Wars, Malastare tried to remain loyal to the Republic but became a contested battleground. The deployment of experimental weapons like the electro-proton bomb during conflicts scarred its lands and people. Malastare is a world of friction—between native and settler, between excitement and exploitation. It represents the thrill of the edge and the cost of being used. The planet is a paradox: a home of sport and a victim of war.'),
	(36,'Dathomir','24','491','10480','temperate','0.9','forests, deserts, savannas','unknown','5200','2014-12-19T18:00:40.142000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.480000Z','/images/planets/36-dathomir.jpg','Dathomir is a shadowy world steeped in dark magic. It is home to the Nightsisters and fearsome beasts. The Force flows wildly here, especially through the dark side. Darth Maul was born on Dathomir. The planet symbolizes rage, ritual, and raw power.','Dathomir is a remote and eerie planet known for its crimson skies, thorny vegetation, and potent dark side energies. It is the ancestral home of the Nightsisters, a coven of Force-sensitive witches who harness magic in terrifying ways. They lived apart from the male Zabrak population, who served them in harsh subjugation. The planet is wild and untamed, home to rancors, deadly fogs, and other supernatural creatures. Dathomir was the birthplace of Darth Maul and his brother Savage Opress, who were both shaped by the planet\'s harsh traditions. The Nightsisters were destroyed by General Grievous during the Clone Wars, but their legend endured. Dathomir is a world where the Force bends unnaturally, ruled more by blood ritual than balance. It stands as a cradle of ancient darkness, where power is earned through pain. Dathomir is feared and respected in equal measure, and few leave it unchanged.'),
	(37,'Ryloth','30','305','10600','temperate, arid, subartic','1','mountains, valleys, deserts, tundra','5','1500000000','2014-12-20T09:46:25.740000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.481000Z','/images/planets/37-ryloth.webp','Ryloth is a harsh, rocky world split between light and darkness. It is the home of the Twi\'lek people. The planet suffered under Separatist and Imperial occupation. Ryloth symbolizes endurance, resistance, and cultural pride. It is twilight made flesh.','Ryloth is a tidally locked planet with one side scorched by eternal sunlight and the other frozen in darkness. Life exists along the narrow twilight band where temperatures are tolerable. The Twi\'leks, known for their resilience and grace, are native to Ryloth. Their history is one of repeated invasions, exploitation, and rebellion. During the Clone Wars, the planet was occupied by the Separatists, and later the Empire enforced harsh rule and slavery. Cham Syndulla, a major figure in Ryloth’s resistance, led freedom fighters against both regimes. His daughter Hera would later become a key member of the Rebel Alliance. Despite suffering greatly, Ryloth’s people never stopped fighting for autonomy. Its cities are carved into rock, and its culture celebrates both beauty and strength. Ryloth is a world of survivors, shaped by shadow and flame. It reflects the power of resistance forged in hardship.'),
	(38,'Aleen Minor','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T09:52:23.452000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.483000Z','/images/planets/38-aleen-minor.webp','Aleen Minor is a small, earthquake-prone planet. Its surface is home to the Aleena, a spirited and agile species. Beneath its crust lies a toxic underworld. Jedi once intervened to save its people. Aleen Minor represents hidden danger and humble strength.','Aleen Minor is a lesser-known, geologically unstable planet inhabited by the Aleena, a short and cheerful reptilian species. The planet\'s surface is bright and welcoming, but deep crevices lead to a dangerous subterranean realm filled with poisonous gas and ancient forces. In one notable incident during the Clone Wars, a seismic rift unleashed noxious fumes, endangering the population. Jedi Knights Obi-Wan Kenobi and Anakin Skywalker were dispatched to stabilize the situation and uncover the mysterious causes beneath the planet’s surface. Though small and rarely noticed in galactic affairs, Aleen Minor revealed how even the smallest worlds could hide secrets of cosmic significance. Its people rely on community, agility, and tradition to survive the unpredictability of their land. The contrast between surface peace and underworld threat makes Aleen Minor a metaphor for unseen struggles. It’s a world that reminds others never to overlook the small or seemingly quiet.'),
	(39,'Vulpter','22','391','14900','temperate, artic','1','urban, barren','unknown','421000000','2014-12-20T09:56:58.874000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.485000Z','/images/planets/39-vulpter.png','Vulpter is an industrial world blanketed in factories and urban waste. Its landscape is dominated by machinery and environmental degradation. The native Vulptereen species have adapted to harsh urban conditions. Vulpter played a role in supplying the Separatists during the Clone Wars. Despite its pollution, it remains a hub of mechanical expertise. The planet embodies industrial excess and technological resilience.','Vulpter is located in the Deep Core and is known for its industrial sprawl, filled with factories, toxic sludge pits, and unregulated development. Centuries of production have ravaged the surface, leaving little of its natural ecosystem intact. The Vulptereen inhabitants have evolved to navigate their heavily polluted world with hunched forms and tough skin. The planet became notorious for its environmental disregard and focus on heavy manufacturing. During the Clone Wars, Vulpter aligned with the Confederacy of Independent Systems, providing droid components and other machinery. Its citizens were skilled in mechanical work, often finding employment as technicians or scavengers. Vulpter’s cities are built in layers, with the wealthier inhabitants residing in cleaner upper zones. The lower zones are choked with pollution and home to scrapyards. The air is thick and acrid, and visitors often require breathing gear. Despite the bleak conditions, innovation thrives here. Vulpter represents a cautionary tale of unchecked industrial growth. It stands as a symbol of both progress and its cost. While not a major military power, its infrastructure made it strategically valuable. Vulpter highlights the tension between technological advancement and environmental sustainability. The resilience of its people ensures that life continues amid the decay. It is often overlooked in galactic affairs, yet plays a quiet role behind the scenes. Its machines keep parts of the galaxy running.'),
	(40,'Troiken','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','desert, tundra, rainforests, mountains','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:01:37.395000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.487000Z','/images/planets/40-troiken.png','Troiken is a mountainous planet with rugged terrain and deep canyons. It is home to the Xexto species and their evolved form, the Quermians. The world is known for its unpredictable climate and volcanic activity. Troiken remained neutral during major galactic conflicts. Despite its isolation, it is rich in natural resources. Troiken stands for mystery, evolution, and quiet endurance.','Troiken, nestled in the Inner Rim, is a planet defined by its jagged mountains, high plateaus, and geothermal volatility. Deep fissures and active volcanoes shape the terrain, creating stunning yet hazardous environments. The native Xexto, agile and four-armed, are suited to this environment and later gave rise to the Quermians, an evolved offshoot who settled elsewhere. Troiken maintained a policy of isolationism throughout much of its history, avoiding involvement in galactic wars. Its population lives in communities built along cliffsides and within protected caves. Trade is limited but valued, focusing on rare minerals and geothermal energy. The planet\'s tectonic instability makes large-scale infrastructure difficult, but its people have adapted with resilient engineering. Troiken was occasionally visited by scouts and adventurers due to rumors of ancient ruins and Force-sensitive artifacts. It remained largely undisturbed even during the Clone Wars. The planet’s serene night skies and violent geological shifts mirror its dichotomy of peace and chaos. Troiken is considered a spiritual site by some Force users. Its cultural traditions emphasize balance and internal strength. Despite its seclusion, it has earned respect for its perseverance. The rugged beauty of Troiken continues to inspire those who brave its wild terrain.'),
	(41,'Tund','48','1770','12190','unknown','unknown','barren, ash','unknown','0','2014-12-20T10:07:29.578000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.489000Z','/images/planets/41-tund.webp','Tund was once a vibrant center of arcane Force knowledge. It became infamous after a catastrophic purge wiped out its inhabitants. The planet is now desolate, cloaked in mystery and darkness. The Tund Sorcerers once wielded incredible power. Today, only ruins and secrets remain. Tund represents lost wisdom and the consequences of corrupted ambition.','Tund, located in the Expansion Region, was once home to the powerful and enigmatic Sorcerers of Tund. These Force-sensitive mystics developed their own esoteric philosophies and techniques, often misunderstood and feared by outsiders. Their knowledge blended science, mysticism, and the Force, making them both revered and mistrusted. Over time, internal strife and external suspicion led to their downfall. The final blow came when a rogue Sorcerer unleashed a destructive wave that annihilated all life on the planet, leaving it barren. Now, Tund is a wasteland of scorched plains and collapsed temples. Its atmosphere remains charged with residual Force energy, making it a haunting site for scholars and Force adepts. Few dare to explore its ruins, fearing both physical and spiritual peril. Legends speak of dark knowledge buried beneath its surface. The Galactic Empire once considered excavating Tund but ultimately abandoned the effort due to strange occurrences. Tund\'s legacy is one of immense potential undone by arrogance and secrecy. It serves as a grim warning to those who pursue power without restraint. Though lifeless, its echoes persist in dark corners of the galaxy’s history. Tund remains an enduring symbol of fallen greatness and forbidden knowledge.'),
	(42,'Haruun Kal','25','383','10120','temperate','0.98','toxic cloudsea, plateaus, volcanoes','unknown','705300','2014-12-20T10:12:28.980000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.491000Z','/images/planets/42-haruun-kal.webp','Haruun Kal is a jungle world with deadly terrain and fierce storms. It is the homeworld of Jedi Master Mace Windu. The Korunnai people live in close harmony with the Force. The planet was scarred by war and violent politics. Haruun Kal symbolizes spiritual strength and survival under extreme pressure.','Haruun Kal, located near the Mid Rim, is a hostile jungle planet known for its explosive weather patterns and dense flora. Its elevated terrain is the only habitable surface, as lower regions are choked with poisonous gases. The native Korunnai are Force-sensitive descendants of Jedi settlers and have developed a culture that reveres the Force and communal living. Haruun Kal was the birthplace of Mace Windu, one of the Jedi Order’s most respected members. The planet\'s harsh environment shaped his discipline and power. During the Clone Wars, Haruun Kal became a battleground for Republic and Separatist forces, further destabilizing an already fragile society. The planet\'s jungle is filled with dangerous creatures, and constant lightning storms make navigation perilous. Korunnai tribes, skilled in guerrilla warfare, resisted outside control fiercely. The planet\'s spiritual and political tensions were explored in Jedi missions and humanitarian efforts. Haruun Kal is often regarded as a place of transformation—where those who endure emerge stronger. Its unyielding nature taught resilience and harmony with the Force. Despite war and hardship, its people endure. The legacy of Haruun Kal lives on in the Jedi who drew strength from its wild power. It is a world of survival and soul-deep wisdom.'),
	(43,'Cerea','27','386','unknown','temperate','1','verdant','20','450000000','2014-12-20T10:14:48.178000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.493000Z','/images/planets/43-cerea.webp','Cerea is a tranquil planet known for its low-tech society and meditative culture. The Cereans value wisdom and live in harmony with nature. It remained largely neutral in galactic conflicts. Jedi Master Ki-Adi-Mundi hailed from Cerea. The planet stands for simplicity, reflection, and balance.','Cerea is an idyllic world in the Mid Rim, blessed with fertile plains, towering trees, and a peaceful people. The Cereans, recognized by their elongated craniums, lead lives centered on harmony, intellectual pursuits, and strict population control. The society values moderation, often rejecting advanced technology to preserve cultural purity and ecological balance. Cerea remained isolated from most galactic politics, maintaining its independence until the Clone Wars. Jedi Master Ki-Adi-Mundi was one of its few emissaries to the Jedi Order and the Galactic Republic. His training and philosophies reflected his world’s meditative traditions. During the Clone Wars, Cerea experienced limited conflict but became politically divided. Some factions advocated for technological advancement, while others resisted change. The planet avoided widespread destruction, preserving its way of life. Cerea’s contributions to Jedi philosophy are well-regarded, emphasizing patience and mindfulness. The planet’s serene landscape and traditionalism contrast with the galaxy’s chaos. It remains a place of sanctuary and spiritual alignment. Cerea symbolizes balance between nature and society. Its legacy endures in the wisdom of its people and the Jedi it shaped.'),
	(44,'Glee Anselm','33','206','15600','tropical, temperate','1','lakes, islands, swamps, seas','80','500000000','2014-12-20T10:18:26.110000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.495000Z','/images/planets/44-glee-anselm.webp','Glee Anselm is a water-covered planet with lush coral reefs and oceanic cities. It is home to the Nautolan species, including Jedi Kit Fisto. The planet\'s environment is rich in aquatic life and culture. It maintained peace but saw conflict during the Clone Wars. Glee Anselm represents fluid strength, depth, and adaptability.','Glee Anselm lies in the Mid Rim and is largely covered by vast oceans and coral-encrusted archipelagos. It is inhabited by the amphibious Nautolans, a species highly attuned to underwater environments. These beings are known for their agility, aquatic combat skills, and sensitivity to emotion through pheromones. Glee Anselm’s societies thrive beneath the waves, in domed cities and submerged temples. The planet experienced skirmishes during the Clone Wars, primarily as a result of Separatist incursions. Despite this, the Nautolans remained committed to peace and survival. Jedi Master Kit Fisto, one of the most charismatic and respected Jedi, was born on Glee Anselm. His calm demeanor and mastery of underwater combat were products of his homeworld. The planet’s environment is dynamic, with fierce storms and teeming marine ecosystems. Glee Anselm also maintains rich artistic and spiritual traditions rooted in the sea. Its people embody resilience and emotional insight. The oceanic world continues to contribute to galactic culture and diplomacy. Glee Anselm is a symbol of inner strength, flowing harmony, and deep understanding. Its beauty and complexity run as deep as its oceans.'),
	(45,'Iridonia','29','413','unknown','unknown','unknown','rocky canyons, acid pools','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:26:05.788000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.497000Z','/images/planets/45-iridonia.png','Iridonia is a rugged, mountainous planet known for its warrior culture. It is the homeworld of the Zabrak species, including Darth Maul. The harsh terrain forged a tough and independent people. Iridonia has a long tradition of martial honor. It symbolizes strength, discipline, and passionate intensity.','Iridonia lies in the Mid Rim and is characterized by jagged canyons, fierce winds, and a challenging climate. Its people, the Zabraks, are renowned across the galaxy for their resilience, discipline, and combat prowess. The Zabraks have a strong warrior heritage, with traditions centered on endurance, personal achievement, and cultural pride. Despite being spread throughout the galaxy, many Zabraks maintain deep ties to Iridonia. The planet has seen political instability and various invasions, yet always recovered through collective strength. Iridonia is also known for its unique rites of passage, often involving trials in the planet’s unforgiving wilderness. Darth Maul, one of the most feared Sith Lords, originated from this world and exemplified the darker potential of its intense culture. While some Zabraks aligned with the Sith or mercenary factions, many others fought for peace and justice. Iridonia’s legacy is multifaceted—honorable yet dangerous, isolated yet influential. The planet stands as a crucible of character, forging individuals through hardship. Its landscape and people reflect a harsh beauty and unyielding will. Iridonia’s presence in galactic history is marked by strength, pride, and enduring fire.'),
	(46,'Tholoth','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:28:31.117000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.498000Z','/images/planets/46-tholoth.webp','Tholoth is a serene and spiritual world located in the Inner Rim. Its inhabitants are known for their deep connection to the Force. Tholothans value wisdom, tradition, and introspection. The planet\'s architecture blends nature with sacred design. Tholoth produced several respected Jedi, including Jedi Master Adi Gallia. It represents peace, inner clarity, and disciplined power.','Tholoth is a peaceful planet whose people are distinguished by their reverence for spiritual discipline and harmony with the Force. The Tholothans developed a strong cultural identity centered on meditation, sacred rites, and mental training. The landscape is marked by rolling hills, quiet temples, and ancient stone sanctuaries. Nature is respected, and development occurs in balance with the land. The Tholothan headdress worn by its people reflects cultural pride and spiritual symbolism. The Jedi Temple on Coruscant counted many Tholothan Jedi among its ranks, including the wise and powerful Adi Gallia. Tholoth remained largely uninvolved in galactic conflicts, maintaining a neutral stance. Its people are calm, introspective, and governed by consensus. Pilgrims and scholars often travel there seeking guidance and peace. While not a military power, Tholoth\'s influence lies in its ideals and the Jedi it nurtured. During the Clone Wars, it maintained cultural independence. The planet\'s legacy survives through its traditions and the resilience of its peaceful philosophy. Tholoth teaches that strength lies in understanding, and leadership in stillness. It is a world of elegant thought and spiritual depth.'),
	(47,'Iktotch','22','481','unknown','arid, rocky, windy','1','rocky','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:31:32.413000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.500000Z','/images/planets/47-iktotch.webp','Iktotch is a storm-battered moon known for its extreme winds and high-altitude settlements. It is the homeworld of the Force-sensitive Iktochi species. The harsh environment fosters powerful precognition and mental discipline. Jedi Master Saesee Tiin hailed from this world. Iktotch stands for foresight, strength, and mental endurance.','Iktotch is a mountainous satellite orbiting the planet Iktotchon, with a climate defined by violent, near-constant windstorms. Life on Iktotch developed in response to these conditions, producing a hardy species known as the Iktochi. These beings possess natural precognitive abilities, possibly influenced by the planet’s intense electromagnetic fields. Cities are carved into cliff faces or built into sheltered caverns. The Iktochi people value silence, concentration, and deep mental focus, making them well-suited for disciplines like meditation and piloting. Saesee Tiin, one of the Republic\'s most skilled Jedi pilots, came from Iktotch. His formidable abilities were enhanced by his species’ unique sensitivity to future events. Iktotch did not involve itself heavily in politics, preferring to remain isolated. The environment cultivates personal strength, with residents enduring fierce conditions from a young age. Jedi recruiters found Iktotch to be a consistent source of candidates with strong mental faculties. While the planet lacks scenic beauty, its skies and landscapes possess a stark, windswept majesty. Iktotch is a world where survival requires clarity and focus. It symbolizes perseverance, foresight, and inner strength shaped by elemental forces.'),
	(48,'Quermia','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:34:08.249000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.502000Z','/images/planets/48-quermia.webp','Quermia is a distant and curious world known for its evolved and intellectual inhabitants. It is the homeworld of the tall and cerebral Quermians. The planet thrives on scientific research, philosophy, and diplomacy. Jedi Master Yarael Poof came from Quermia. It symbolizes logic, reason, and detached wisdom.','Quermia is a planet that exists on the fringe of known galactic space, notable for the advanced evolution of its species. The Quermians are tall, thin beings with elongated necks and dual brains—one in the head, another in the chest. This unique biology supports exceptional intellect and multitasking. The culture of Quermia revolves around academic institutions, laboratories, and philosophical forums. Physical conflict is rare; disputes are resolved through argumentation and reason. The planet’s terrain includes sprawling biodomes, glass spires, and air-purifying gardens, showcasing an advanced yet peaceful society. Jedi Master Yarael Poof, known for his diplomatic skills and deep insight, was born on Quermia. Though distant from the galaxy’s core, the planet’s influence reached the Jedi High Council through him. Quermia seldom participates in military conflicts, instead offering intellectual and medical aid. Its people prize education, clarity, and calm debate. The Quermians serve as mediators and healers across many systems. Despite its remoteness, Quermia is respected as a beacon of logical harmony. It remains a model of enlightened civilization and academic purity. Its legacy lies in shaping minds rather than armies.'),
	(49,'Dorin','22','409','13400','temperate','1','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T10:48:36.141000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.504000Z','/images/planets/49-dorin.webp','Dorin is a world located between two black holes, shrouded in mystery and lethal gases. The Kel Dor species evolved to survive its toxic atmosphere. Jedi Master Plo Koon hailed from this planet. Dorin is a symbol of justice, perseverance, and balance amid darkness.','Dorin is positioned in a hazardous part of the galaxy, flanked by gravitational anomalies and cloaked in dense clouds of volatile gas. Its native inhabitants, the Kel Dor, require breath masks and goggles when off-world due to their unique respiratory needs. Dorin’s atmosphere, though deadly to most species, is natural and life-sustaining for the Kel Dor. The planet’s surface consists of volcanic ridges, glowing vents, and rugged plains. Kel Dor society emphasizes justice, order, and communal responsibility. Jedi Master Plo Koon was one of the Order’s most principled members, known for his compassion and incorruptibility. Dorin hosts monasteries and law councils rather than cities, reflecting its devotion to ethics and service. The Jedi on Dorin often begin their training early, especially among Force-sensitive youth. Despite the perilous space routes, the planet has remained continuously inhabited. Dorin is frequently regarded as a spiritual place, with its elemental dangers reinforcing humility and strength. It cultivates guardians of peace. The world is a bastion of moral clarity and enduring willpower. It represents serenity within chaos and truth within danger.'),
	(50,'Champala','27','318','unknown','temperate','1','oceans, rainforests, plateaus','unknown','3500000000','2014-12-20T10:52:51.524000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.506000Z','/images/planets/50-champala.webp','Champala is an oceanic world of color-shifting amphibians and artistic elegance. It is the homeworld of the Chagrians, including Mas Amedda. Known for its art and ceremony, it favored Imperial rule during the Clone Wars. Champala symbolizes tradition, adaptability, and refined political influence.','Champala is covered in shallow seas, island chains, and vibrant aquatic ecosystems. The Chagrian people are amphibious and capable of adapting both physically and culturally to various environments. Their skin changes hue in response to emotional or environmental stimuli, and their society places great value on ritual and ceremony. Champala is renowned for its public performances, architectural grandeur, and philosophical gatherings. Mas Amedda, the Grand Vizier of the Galactic Empire, originated from this world and carried its traditions into the Senate. Though its surface seems serene, Champala played a subtle political role during the Republic’s decline. Its leaders favored centralization and order, aligning with Palpatine’s reforms. The planet became a source of bureaucratic talent and political aides. Champala\'s oceanic life and weather cycles inspired a poetic worldview among its inhabitants. Their culture values adaptability and strategic thinking. Champala remains both culturally rich and politically complex. It is remembered as a world of ceremonial power and graceful maneuvering.'),
	(51,'Mirial','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','deserts','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T16:44:46.318000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.508000Z','/images/planets/51-mirial.jpg','Mirial is a desert world of spiritual discipline and deep tradition. The Mirialans are known for their ritual tattoos and Jedi potential. The harsh environment shaped their strong communal bonds. Jedi such as Luminara Unduli and Barriss Offee hailed from here. Mirial represents faith, resilience, and the testing of beliefs.','Mirial lies in the Outer Rim and consists largely of windswept deserts, rocky outcroppings, and scattered nomadic settlements. Its native people, the Mirialans, have green or yellow skin and adorn their faces with symbolic tattoos marking personal growth and achievement. The culture emphasizes self-discipline, spirituality, and strong bonds of kinship. Mirial has long contributed Jedi to the Order, with Luminara Unduli and Barriss Offee among its most recognized figures. The Jedi from Mirial carry the teachings of patience, modesty, and meditation rooted in their homeland. Life on the planet is austere, with families living in close-knit, survival-focused communities. Temples and ruins dot the landscape, each tied to various rites of passage. Mirialans believe strongly in destiny and the will of the Force. Despite their remote location, they maintain ties with galactic institutions. During the Clone Wars, the planet tried to remain neutral but suffered under Separatist pressure. Mirial endures as a place of quiet strength and inward exploration. It teaches humility and endurance through both belief and environment.'),
	(52,'Serenno','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','rainforests, rivers, mountains','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T16:52:13.357000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.510000Z','/images/planets/52-serenno.webp','Serenno is a noble world of wealth, history, and power. It is the home of Count Dooku, who left the Jedi Order to become a Sith Lord. The planet is ruled by aristocrats and steeped in tradition. Serenno embodies pride, legacy, and the seductive pull of authority.','Serenno is located in the Outer Rim and is known for its green hills, palatial estates, and ancient fortresses. It is governed by noble houses, each with vast resources and long lineages. Count Dooku, once a Jedi Master, was born into the ruling family and later returned to claim his inheritance. The planet’s aristocracy wielded great influence and viewed Jedi detachment as a weakness. Dooku’s return signaled a shift in Serenno’s galactic stance, aligning it with the Confederacy of Independent Systems during the Clone Wars. Serenno became a political and financial backbone of the Separatist movement. While many of its citizens supported Dooku’s ideals, others feared the cost. The planet hosts elite academies, libraries, and private armies. It is a hub of strategy, refinement, and ideological strength. Its lush countryside conceals both beauty and menace. Serenno teaches that legacy is both burden and weapon. The fall of Dooku cast a long shadow over its proud people. Serenno remains a place of intrigue and dangerous elegance, a world shaped by ambition and the thin line between light and dark.'),
	(53,'Concord Dawn','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','jungles, forests, deserts','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T16:54:39.909000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.512000Z','/images/planets/53-concord-dawn.png','Concord Dawn is a rugged agricultural world in the Mandalore sector. It is known for producing skilled warriors and bounty hunters. The planet is the birthplace of Jango Fett. Life on Concord Dawn is harsh, shaped by tradition and survival. Its warrior culture values strength, loyalty, and independence. Concord Dawn represents endurance, defiance, and legacy.','Concord Dawn is a sparsely populated world with a harsh environment, including open plains, rocky terrain, and minimal infrastructure. It lies within the Mandalore sector and shares the proud warrior heritage of the Mandalorian people. Though not as industrialized as Mandalore, it remains culturally significant for its history of producing bounty hunters and fighters. Jango Fett, who later became the genetic template for the Republic’s clone army, was born on Concord Dawn. The planet was ravaged by internal strife during Mandalorian civil wars, leaving its people wary and self-reliant. Most inhabitants live in small farming communities fortified against danger. The society values martial skill, independence, and honor through battle. Concord Dawn operates under a strict code that favors order and strength. Despite its peripheral status, the planet has influenced galactic events through its offspring and traditions. Bounty hunter guilds and warrior training centers have roots in its soil. Concord Dawn symbolizes the raw resilience of Mandalorian culture, unyielding in the face of adversity. It is a land where loyalty is earned and survival is proof of worth.'),
	(54,'Zolan','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T16:56:37.250000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.514000Z','/images/planets/54-zolan.webp','Zolan is a misty and isolated world, home to shape-shifting Clawdites. Its culture prizes secrecy and adaptability. Clawdites are often used as spies and infiltrators. Zolan remains largely unknown to outsiders. Its people walk the line between camouflage and deception. Zolan represents transformation, concealment, and identity.','Zolan is a mysterious planet with a cool, foggy climate and rugged, forested terrain. The native Clawdite population possesses the rare ability to alter their physical appearance at will. This trait developed as an evolutionary response to Zolan’s competitive and hazardous environment. Society on Zolan is built around covert skills, stealth, and control of emotion. Outsiders rarely visit, and few understand its intricate caste systems and identity-based rituals. Many Clawdites seek employment as spies, body doubles, and intelligence agents across the galaxy. Zam Wesell, a well-known Clawdite assassin, hailed from Zolan and used her talents for infiltration and assassination. Due to fear and prejudice, Clawdites often live in the shadows even beyond their homeworld. On Zolan, youth are taught early to control their transformations and mask intent. The planet’s political influence is minimal, but its individuals often play large roles in galactic intrigue. Zolan itself remains elusive—hidden behind veils of mystery and cultural complexity. It stands as a world where the line between survival and subterfuge is paper thin.'),
	(55,'Ojom','unknown','unknown','unknown','frigid','unknown','oceans, glaciers','100','500000000','2014-12-20T17:27:41.286000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.516000Z','/images/planets/55-ojom.webp','Ojom is a freezing world of ice-covered oceans and glaciers. It is inhabited by the Besalisk species, known for their multiple arms and hearty strength. Life is adapted to harsh temperatures and slow-moving storms. The people are tough, industrious, and communal. Ojom represents endurance, teamwork, and survival through adaptation.','Ojom is an icy world consisting mostly of glacial oceans and frozen landmasses. The climate is brutal, with temperatures rarely rising above freezing and frequent whiteout storms. Native to Ojom are the Besalisks, large, multi-armed beings capable of extraordinary physical feats. They live in compact dome cities that use geothermal energy and communal heat-sharing for survival. Daily life revolves around cooperation and resilience. The Besalisk are known across the galaxy for their work ethic and fortitude. One of the most famous Besalisks is Dexter Jettster, who left Ojom and opened a diner on Coruscant. Ojom’s economic structure is modest, with emphasis on sustainable harvesting of oceanic and glacial resources. Despite the extreme conditions, the culture is rich in oral storytelling and community festivals. Besalisks from Ojom often possess a gruff yet warm demeanor, shaped by their environment. Ojom symbolizes the strength of unity in adversity. It is a place of quiet perseverance and the belief that every storm can be endured through solidarity.'),
	(56,'Skako','27','384','unknown','temperate','1','urban, vines','unknown','500000000000','2014-12-20T17:50:47.864000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.517000Z','/images/planets/56-skako.png','Skako is a high-pressure, industrial world located in the Core Worlds. Its native Skakoans require special suits to survive off-world. The planet is heavily urbanized and technologically advanced. It was home to Wat Tambor and the Techno Union. Skako represents mechanical precision, bureaucracy, and cold ambition.','Skako is a planet enveloped in an atmosphere so dense that native lifeforms evolved under extreme pressure. The Skakoans developed highly advanced technology and enclosed cities with towering megastructures. Most Skakoans wear pressure suits called enviro-suits when traveling off-world, which maintain their survival conditions. The society is rigid, hierarchical, and technocratic, focused on precision, efficiency, and control. Skako is the headquarters of the Techno Union, a powerful corporate entity that supplied weapons and droids during the Clone Wars. Wat Tambor, its Foreman, represented the planet’s commitment to progress at any cost. Skako remained neutral on the surface but was deeply involved with the Separatist Council. Life on the planet is dominated by industry and cybernetic innovation. Decisions are made through algorithmic deliberation and corporate governance. Skako embodies a worldview of dominance through data and machinery. It is a planet where emotion yields to protocol, and identity is tied to function.'),
	(57,'Muunilinst','28','412','13800','temperate','1','plains, forests, hills, mountains','25','5000000000','2014-12-20T17:57:47.420000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.519000Z','/images/planets/57-muunilinst.png','Muunilinst is a wealthy banking world known for its towering spires and vast vaults. It is the home of the Muun species and the InterGalactic Banking Clan. The planet influenced galactic politics through finance. San Hill, a Separatist leader, hailed from here. Muunilinst symbolizes control through credit and economic power.','Muunilinst is a Core Worlds planet dominated by elegant, vertical cities and massive banking complexes. It is the headquarters of the InterGalactic Banking Clan, a financial institution that held immense sway during the Republic and Clone Wars eras. The Muun people are tall, logical beings known for their cold negotiation skills and love of structure. Muunilinst’s culture revolves around accounting, investment, and legal minutiae. The Banking Clan used its wealth to influence both Republic and Separatist agendas, officially siding with Count Dooku’s Confederacy. San Hill, its chairman, played a major role in these developments. The cities of Muunilinst feature meticulous design, mirrored towers, and digitized commerce hubs. There is little tolerance for sentiment or risk. Education focuses on mathematics, law, and finance from an early age. Muunilinst doesn’t project military strength, but its financial networks have destabilized entire systems. It is a planet that embodies cold calculation and the invisible hand of monetary domination.'),
	(58,'Shili','unknown','unknown','unknown','temperate','1','cities, savannahs, seas, plains','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T18:43:14.049000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.521000Z','/images/planets/58-shili.webp','Shili is a vibrant, natural world covered in plains and forests. It is the home of the Togruta species, known for their colorful skin and head-tails. Shili’s people live in harmony with predators and land. Jedi Master Shaak Ti came from here. Shili stands for balance, instinct, and living in tune with nature.','Shili is a verdant world teeming with life, wide-open grasslands, and towering forests. Its native species, the Togruta, evolved to live among fierce predators, developing natural camouflage and pack-based social behaviors. Their lekku and montrals are sensory tools that enhance spatial awareness. The Togruta are spiritual, valuing community, nature, and the living Force. Shili’s tribes thrive through cooperative hunting and shared survival. Jedi Master Shaak Ti, known for her wisdom and calm strength, was born on Shili and embodied its values. The planet remained mostly untouched by galactic wars, preferring isolation and cultural preservation. Shili’s beauty lies in its harmony—a blend of survivalism and spiritual elegance. The people believe strength comes from natural rhythm, not dominance. Even Jedi from Shili maintain a primal instinct and deep intuition. Shili is a reminder of how life adapts without losing grace, and how nature can inspire both strength and serenity.'),
	(59,'Kalee','23','378','13850','arid, temperate, tropical','1','rainforests, cliffs, canyons, seas','unknown','4000000000','2014-12-20T19:43:51.278000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.523000Z','/images/planets/59-kalee.webp','Kalee is a war-torn and arid planet known for its warrior culture. It is the birthplace of General Grievous. The Kaleesh are proud, tribal fighters who value honor and vengeance. The planet suffered economic collapse after conflict with the Yam’rii. Kalee represents pain, survival, and fury molded into purpose.','Kalee is a desolate world marked by jagged mountains, dry plains, and the ruins of endless battles. Its native people, the Kaleesh, are fierce and noble warriors with a deep spiritual tradition involving ancestral masks and ceremonial hunting. The planet came into galactic awareness through conflict with the insectoid Yam’rii of the nearby planet Huk. After intervention by the Galactic Republic on behalf of the Yam’rii, Kalee fell into economic and humanitarian crisis. One of its greatest warriors, Qymaen jai Sheelal, was remade into General Grievous and joined the Separatists out of hatred for the Jedi and Republic. Kalee’s tribes remain distrustful of galactic powers, maintaining old customs and vendettas. Life is built on proving one’s strength and protecting one’s people. The planet’s history is carved into bone, stone, and myth. Kalee is a scarred world—violent, misunderstood, but full of raw passion and loyalty. It stands as a reminder of what happens when dignity is denied and power is twisted by loss.'),
	(60,'Umbara','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T20:18:36.256000Z','2014-12-20T20:58:18.525000Z','/images/planets/60-umbara.png','Umbara is a shadowy world shrouded in perpetual darkness. Its inhabitants are secretive and advanced in military technology. Known as the ‘Shadow World,’ it served the Separatists during the Clone Wars. The Umbarans are highly strategic and distrustful. Umbara symbolizes deception, manipulation, and ruthless precision.','Umbara lies deep in the Expansion Region, locked in a twilight zone where sunlight rarely penetrates. Its dense atmosphere and bioluminescent plant life create a haunting, surreal environment. The native Umbarans are pale-skinned, reclusive humanoids with keen minds for strategy and manipulation. Their society values control, secrecy, and military prowess. During the Clone Wars, Umbara allied with the Separatists and repelled Republic forces in a brutal campaign. Advanced weaponry and unique war tactics made the Umbarans formidable enemies. Jedi General Pong Krell later betrayed the Republic during the conflict, adding infamy to the world’s legacy. Umbara is technologically superior but morally ambiguous, with little trust for outsiders. The planet’s isolationism feeds into its paranoia and ambition. Umbara’s warriors are cold, calculating, and effective. It is a planet where light struggles to thrive, both literally and philosophically. Umbara represents a civilization where darkness is not feared but wielded as a weapon.');
INSERT INTO `species` (`id`, `name`, `classification`, `designation`, `average_height`, `average_lifespan`, `eye_colors`, `hair_colors`, `skin_colors`, `language`, `created`, `edited`, `image_url`, `short_description`, `long_description`, `homeworld_id`)
VALUES
	(1,'Human','mammal','sentient','180','120','brown, blue, green, hazel, grey, amber','blonde, brown, black, red','caucasian, black, asian, hispanic','Galactic Basic','2014-12-10T13:52:11.567000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.136000Z','/images/species/1-human.png','Humans are the most widespread and adaptable species in the galaxy. Found in every sector, they influence politics, culture, and war. Their societies vary from primitive to highly advanced. Notable humans include Luke Skywalker, Leia Organa, and Darth Vader. Their actions have shaped galactic history for millennia. Humans symbolize ambition, diversity, and resilience.','Humans originated on Coruscant but spread throughout the galaxy, forming the backbone of many governments, armies, and institutions. They are known for their adaptability and diverse cultures, making them dominant in both the Galactic Republic and the Empire. Humans vary widely in appearance and customs depending on planetary origin. Many iconic figures, such as Padmé Amidala, Emperor Palpatine, and Han Solo, were human. Their flexibility allowed them to thrive in politics, trade, war, and diplomacy. Human-led factions like the Jedi Order, the Sith, the Rebel Alliance, and the Galactic Empire have directed the galaxy’s fate. Despite internal divisions and ideological conflict, humans consistently reinvent themselves. Their homeworld, Coruscant, became the capital of galactic civilization. Across the galaxy, humans are known for their strong will, emotional range, and capacity for both greatness and destruction. Their presence touches every major conflict and resolution. Whether as liberators or tyrants, humans are central to galactic destiny. They reflect the spectrum of moral choices, from selflessness to domination.',9),
	(2,'Droid','artificial','sentient','n/a','indefinite','n/a','n/a','n/a','n/a','2014-12-10T15:16:16.259000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.139000Z','/images/species/2-droid.png','Droids are artificial beings programmed for various tasks across the galaxy. They serve in roles from labor to warfare to diplomacy. Some develop unique personalities over time. Iconic droids include R2-D2, C-3PO, and General Grievous. Droids are tools, companions, and even heroes. They represent precision, loyalty, and evolving identity.','Droids are mechanical entities created to assist organic beings with labor, service, or combat. They range from simple utility units to advanced protocol and battle models. The galaxy’s reliance on droids is vast, with nearly every sector using them for technical or military work. Despite their programming, many droids display unique personalities, quirks, and even emotions. R2-D2’s bravery, C-3PO’s anxiety, and K-2SO’s sarcasm reflect this evolution. Some droids have been reprogrammed or gone rogue, raising ethical questions about consciousness and autonomy. During the Clone Wars, entire armies of droids were deployed by the Separatists, while others like astromechs served Jedi and Rebels with unwavering loyalty. While often underestimated, droids have saved countless lives and altered the course of history. Their design reflects their purpose, but their legacy transcends function. Droids continue to challenge the boundary between tool and being. They represent the promise and peril of artificial intelligence in galactic society.',NULL),
	(3,'Wookie','mammal','sentient','210','400','blue, green, yellow, brown, golden, red','black, brown','gray','Shyriiwook','2014-12-10T16:44:31.486000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.142000Z','/images/species/3-wookie.webp','Wookiees are tall, fur-covered beings from the planet Kashyyyk. They are known for strength, loyalty, and bravery. Their language is a complex series of roars and growls. Chewbacca is the most famous Wookiee ally of the Rebellion. Wookiees value honor and community. They symbolize courage, kinship, and enduring friendship.','The Wookiees hail from Kashyyyk, a lush, forested world with towering wroshyr trees. They live in elevated cities connected by bridges and ruled by tribal councils. Wookiees possess immense physical strength, longevity, and technical aptitude. Despite their primal appearance, they are intelligent and skilled in engineering and combat. The Wookiee code of honor is central to their culture, emphasizing life-debts, family, and resistance to enslavement. During the Clone Wars and the rise of the Empire, many Wookiees were captured and forced into labor, especially in constructing the Death Star. Chewbacca’s partnership with Han Solo and his role in the Rebellion made the species legendary across the stars. Wookiees are fiercely loyal, and betrayal is nearly unthinkable within their communities. Their bond with nature and intuitive understanding of technology makes them unique allies. Wookiees rarely speak Basic, but their language, Shyriiwook, is understood by many. They represent the strength of tradition, resistance, and brotherhood in the face of oppression.',14),
	(4,'Rodian','sentient','reptilian','170','unknown','black','n/a','green, blue','Galatic Basic','2014-12-10T17:05:26.471000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.144000Z','/images/species/4-rodian.jpg','Rodians are reptilian humanoids from the planet Rodia. They are recognized by their green skin and multifaceted eyes. Many become bounty hunters due to their warrior culture. Greedo, who confronted Han Solo, was a Rodian. They balance aggression with loyalty. Rodians represent pursuit, tenacity, and survival instinct.','Rodians evolved on Rodia, a humid world filled with dense jungles and dangerous wildlife. This environment forged their hunting skills and combat reflexes. Rodian society traditionally honors warriors and survivalists, leading many to seek careers as bounty hunters. Over time, the planet shifted from internal tribal warfare to intergalactic involvement, often through mercenary work. Greedo, a Rodian bounty hunter, became infamous for his failed attempt to capture Han Solo. Rodians are often seen as aggressive, but many seek respect, recognition, and economic opportunity. Their language, Rodese, is filled with guttural tones and clicks. As they’ve entered galactic society, Rodians have diversified in their professions and politics. Some work with crime syndicates, while others support the Rebellion or Republic. Despite stereotypes, Rodians are capable of deep bonds and strong moral codes. Their history reflects both the hardships of their environment and the potential for adaptation. Rodians thrive by tracking, surviving, and evolving.',23),
	(5,'Hutt','gastropod','sentient','300','1000','yellow, red','n/a','green, brown, tan','Huttese','2014-12-10T17:12:50.410000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.146000Z','/images/species/5-hutt.jpg','Hutts are large, slug-like beings known for crime, influence, and wealth. They rule through fear, bribery, and ruthless deals. Jabba the Hutt was among the most infamous. Hutts dominate the Outer Rim’s underworld. Their power lies in manipulation and longevity. They represent corruption, control, and unrelenting greed.','Originating from Nal Hutta, Hutts are a powerful species known for their immense size, long lifespans, and complete lack of moral restraint. They lead a criminal empire called the Hutt Cartel, which spans spice trade, slavery, gambling, and assassination. Despite their slow appearance, Hutts are cunning and politically shrewd. They operate from dens filled with wealth, mercenaries, and captives. Jabba the Hutt controlled Tatooine and played a key role in smuggling and bounty hunting operations during the Galactic Civil War. Hutts enforce their will through intimidation, often hiring enforcers like bounty hunters or rancors. While not traditionally warriors, their influence is formidable and far-reaching. Hutt society prizes power above all else, with court intrigue and betrayal as common tools. Their neutrality in galactic conflicts masks deep investments in both sides. Hutts view laws as flexible and morality as weakness. Their legacy is one of persistent corruption woven into galactic history.',24),
	(6,'Yoda\'s species','mammal','sentient','66','900','brown, green, yellow','brown, white','green, yellow','Galactic basic','2014-12-15T12:27:22.877000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.148000Z','/images/species/6-yoda-s-species.png','The mysterious species of Yoda remains largely unnamed and secretive. Few members are known in galactic records. They are deeply attuned to the Force and often live long lives. Yoda and Grogu are the most prominent examples. Their rarity adds to their mystique. They symbolize wisdom, balance, and ancient power.','Yoda’s species is one of the most enigmatic in the galaxy, with almost nothing publicly known about their name, origin, or population. Only a few individuals—such as Yoda, Yaddle, and Grogu—have ever been seen. Each known member exhibits strong Force sensitivity, long lifespans, and exceptional wisdom. Yoda lived for over 900 years, serving as Grand Master of the Jedi Order during its height and through its downfall. Despite their size and unassuming stature, members of this species possess tremendous physical ability and insight. Their speech often follows a unique syntax, reflecting an ancient and thoughtful worldview. Grogu, found in the post-Empire era, drew the attention of both Jedi and Imperials. The species’ relationship to the Force is profound and possibly biological. Their long lives and scarcity make them revered and heavily protected. The few who exist are either Jedi Masters or powerful Force users. This mystery enhances their legendary status. The species represents humility, depth, and the unknowable.',28),
	(7,'Trandoshan','reptile','sentient','200','unknown','yellow, orange','none','brown, green','Dosh','2014-12-15T13:07:47.704000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.151000Z','/images/species/7-trandoshan.jpg','Trandoshans are reptilian hunters from the planet Trandosha. They prize strength, trophies, and conquest. Their society revolves around hunting and honoring the Scorekeeper deity. Bossk is a feared Trandoshan bounty hunter. They clash often with Wookiees. Trandoshans represent aggression, glory, and survivalist tradition.','Trandoshans hail from Trandosha, a world of hot jungles and sacred hunting grounds. Their culture revolves around the worship of the Scorekeeper, a goddess who rewards successful hunts and punishes failure. Trandoshans earn \'points\' for each trophy, whether animal or sentient prey. This belief system fuels their violent and competitive nature. Trandoshans view hunting not just as a tradition, but as a spiritual obligation. Many become bounty hunters, mercenaries, or slavers. Bossk, one of the most feared Trandoshans, regularly hunted Wookiees and rivaled other hunters like Boba Fett. Trandoshans are biologically resilient, capable of regenerating limbs. They possess sharp claws, infrared vision, and incredible physical power. Despite their hostility, they operate under strict social codes and clan loyalty. Their enmity with Wookiees is legendary, rooted in conflict over territory and ideology. Trandoshans rarely show mercy but respect worthy opponents. They stand as avatars of primal strength, danger, and ritualized violence.',29),
	(8,'Mon Calamari','amphibian','sentient','160','unknown','yellow','none','red, blue, brown, magenta','Mon Calamarian','2014-12-18T11:09:52.263000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.153000Z','/images/species/8-mon-calamari.png','The Mon Calamari are amphibious beings from the ocean world of Mon Cala. Known for intelligence and engineering, they helped build starships for the Rebellion. Admiral Ackbar is their most famous leader. They value honor, strategy, and alliance. Mon Calamari culture blends aesthetics with utility. They represent defiance, craftsmanship, and unity.','Originating from the watery planet of Mon Cala, the Mon Calamari are amphibious beings with domed heads and webbed hands. Their culture emphasizes art, technology, and communal responsibility. Living in massive underwater cities, they became master starship designers, creating iconic vessels like the Mon Calamari cruisers. When the Empire occupied their world, the Mon Calamari rebelled, aligning with the Rebel Alliance. Their strategic and engineering contributions were vital during major battles like Endor. Admiral Ackbar, a key tactician, led their forces and delivered the famous warning, \'It’s a trap!\' Their society prizes harmony, resistance to tyranny, and defense of their homeworld. Despite their aquatic nature, they adapted well to galactic roles in leadership, diplomacy, and warfare. The Mon Calamari show that intelligence and creativity are as important as firepower. They symbolize collective strength, sacrifice, and the belief that freedom is worth fighting for.',31),
	(9,'Ewok','mammal','sentient','100','unknown','orange, brown','white, brown, black','brown','Ewokese','2014-12-18T11:22:00.285000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.155000Z','/images/species/9-ewok.png','Ewoks are small, furry creatures native to the forest moon of Endor. Despite their primitive appearance, they are clever and resourceful. They live in tree villages and use nature-based tools. Ewoks helped defeat the Empire in the Battle of Endor. Wicket is one of the most recognized among them. They symbolize innocence, bravery, and unexpected heroism.','Ewoks inhabit the dense forests of Endor and live in elevated villages among the trees. Though technologically primitive, they are inventive and brave, using traps, gliders, and teamwork to defend their territory. Ewoks value storytelling, ritual, and community, celebrating victories with music and dance. Their key role in helping the Rebel Alliance defeat the Imperial forces during the Battle of Endor surprised many across the galaxy. Wicket, a curious and courageous Ewok, formed a bond with Princess Leia and helped initiate contact with the Rebels. Ewoks use nature to their advantage, setting ambushes and leveraging terrain knowledge. They are guided by tribal leaders and spiritual elders. Despite their size, they fight fiercely when threatened. Ewoks teach that courage doesn’t come from strength but from heart. Their victory over advanced military forces turned them into legends. They remind the galaxy that even the smallest voices can bring down great empires.',7),
	(10,'Sullustan','mammal','sentient','180','unknown','black','none','pale','Sullutese','2014-12-18T11:26:20.103000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.157000Z','/images/species/10-sullustan.jpeg','Sullustans are humanoid beings with large jowls and keen senses. They come from the volcanic planet Sullust. Skilled in navigation and piloting, many serve in the Rebellion. Nien Nunb co-piloted the Millennium Falcon at Endor. Sullustans are loyal, perceptive, and brave. They symbolize precision, camaraderie, and hope.','Hailing from the volcanic world of Sullust, Sullustans are known for their adaptability, sharp reflexes, and navigational talents. With large, black eyes and leathery skin, they are well-suited to harsh environments. Sullustans played a prominent role in the Rebellion, especially in logistics and fleet operations. Nien Nunb became a hero of the Battle of Endor, co-piloting the Millennium Falcon during the attack on the second Death Star. Their language is filled with high-pitched tones, but many also speak Galactic Basic. Sullustans value loyalty and clarity, making them effective allies in high-stress situations. Their homeworld became a key manufacturing and staging ground during the Galactic Civil War. Though often underestimated, their presence proved essential to the Rebel cause. Sullustans are community-oriented and courageous, often facing great odds without hesitation. Their legacy lives on through precise action and enduring bonds.',33),
	(11,'Neimodian','unknown','sentient','180','unknown','red, pink','none','grey, green','Neimoidia','2014-12-19T17:07:31.319000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.160000Z','/images/species/11-neimodian.png','Neimodians are calculating beings from Neimoidia, known for trade and politics. They led the Trade Federation during the Clone Wars. Their actions contributed to the rise of the Empire. Nute Gunray was a central figure in their political schemes. Neimodians symbolize greed, manipulation, and fear-driven control.','The Neimodians are a species originating from Neimoidia and its colony worlds. They are known throughout the galaxy for their business acumen and bureaucratic dominance. As leaders of the Trade Federation, they amassed vast influence and wealth. Their involvement in the Naboo blockade and alliance with Darth Sidious helped trigger the Clone Wars. Neimodians often wear elaborate clothing and use droids for personal protection. Nute Gunray, their viceroy, remained a puppet of the Sith, blindly pursuing profit and security. While not inherently evil, their culture emphasizes profit over morality. This worldview led them to support separatist causes and eventually the formation of the Empire. Neimodians are risk-averse and often cowardly when confronted directly. Still, their ability to control systems through trade and legal maneuvering made them powerful. They serve as a cautionary tale about the consequences of unchecked greed and fear.',18),
	(12,'Gungan','amphibian','sentient','190','unknown','orange','none','brown, green','Gungan basic','2014-12-19T17:30:37.341000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.163000Z','/images/species/12-gungan.png','Gungans are amphibious beings from the planet Naboo. They live in underwater cities and value honor and unity. Their technology is organic and energy-based. Jar Jar Binks is a well-known Gungan. They helped defend Naboo from the Trade Federation. Gungans represent cultural pride, adaptability, and unlikely heroism.','The Gungans inhabit the swamps and lakes of Naboo, building vast underwater cities like Otoh Gunga. They are a proud and independent species, historically isolated from the human Naboo. With long ears and strong legs, Gungans are skilled swimmers and agile warriors. Their technology blends biological materials with plasma energy, creating bubble shields and boomas for battle. Jar Jar Binks, though clumsy, bridged the divide between the Gungans and Naboo during the Battle of Naboo. Their Grand Army fought valiantly against the droid forces of the Trade Federation. Over time, Gungans became more integrated into galactic politics. Despite being misunderstood, they are deeply spiritual, valuing tradition and loyalty. Gungans embody the idea that unity between different peoples leads to strength. Their rise from isolation to heroism reflects the potential in underestimated cultures.',8),
	(13,'Toydarian','mammal','sentient','120','91','yellow','none','blue, green, grey','Toydarian','2014-12-19T17:48:56.893000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.165000Z','/images/species/13-toydarian.png','Toydarians are winged beings from Toydaria, immune to Jedi mind tricks. They are shrewd and often deal in trade. Watto was a well-known Toydarian on Tatooine. They prioritize profit but can show unexpected loyalty. Toydarians represent bargaining, resistance, and rugged individualism.','Native to the swampy world of Toydaria, Toydarians are small, blue, flying creatures with snouts and large ears. Known for their stubbornness and greed, they often work in trade, salvage, and commerce. Toydarians are unique in that they are naturally resistant to Force persuasion, making them difficult to manipulate. Watto, a junk dealer and owner of Anakin Skywalker during his childhood, exemplified their rough exterior and sharp tongue. While often self-serving, Toydarians are not inherently evil. They operate by strict business codes and expect fair exchanges. Their society values toughness, independence, and verbal wit. Though many look down on them as cheats, Toydarians see themselves as survivors. They highlight how cunning and grit can thrive even in a galaxy ruled by powers far greater than themselves.',34),
	(14,'Dug','mammal','sentient','100','unknown','yellow, blue','none','brown, purple, grey, red','Dugese','2014-12-19T17:53:11.214000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.167000Z','/images/species/14-dug.png','Dugs are aggressive beings from the planet Malastare. They walk on their arms and speak in a rough dialect. Sebulba, a podracer, is the most well-known Dug. Their culture values speed, strength, and dominance. Dugs are quick to anger and proud. They represent competitiveness and survival.','Dugs are native to the high-gravity world of Malastare, which shaped their powerful upper limbs and inverted walking style. They walk on their arms while using their legs for manipulation. Known for their fierce temperament and physical prowess, Dugs often participate in podracing and high-risk sports. Sebulba, a podracing champion, gained notoriety during Anakin Skywalker’s early years. Dugs value competition and self-reliance. Their society respects those who take what they want and fight to keep it. This aggressive worldview leads them to become mercenaries, racers, or bodyguards. Despite their arrogance, Dugs are capable of admiration for true skill and determination. They symbolize raw competitiveness, ego, and the fight to stay on top. Dugs thrive in environments where survival depends on speed, wit, and strength.',35),
	(15,'Twi\'lek','mammals','sentient','200','unknown','blue, brown, orange, pink','none','orange, yellow, blue, green, pink, purple, tan','Twi\'leki','2014-12-20T09:48:02.406000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.169000Z','/images/species/15-twi-lek.png','Twi\'leks are a graceful species from the planet Ryloth, known for their head-tails called lekku. They are culturally diverse and often skilled in diplomacy, dance, or trade. Twi\'leks have endured oppression and slavery across the galaxy. Despite hardships, many rose to positions of power and leadership. Aayla Secura is one of their most famous Jedi. Twi\'leks symbolize resilience, adaptability, and hidden strength.','Twi\'leks are humanoid beings characterized by their twin head-tails, known as lekku, which aid in communication and balance. Native to the harsh and varied environments of Ryloth, their culture is rich with tradition and artistry. Twi\'leks have often suffered under galactic systems, with many sold into slavery or exploited for entertainment. However, they are also known for political savvy and cultural endurance. Their society includes many clans and a strong sense of identity. Despite systemic oppression, Twi\'leks like Aayla Secura became prominent figures in the Jedi Order. Others have served in senatorial roles or as resistance fighters. Their ability to adapt to various roles—diplomats, merchants, spies, or warriors—has ensured their survival. Twi\'leks value loyalty, honor, and personal freedom. They are emblematic of cultures forced to evolve under pressure yet maintaining their dignity. Their story is one of survival, transformation, and quiet rebellion.',37),
	(16,'Aleena','reptile','sentient','80','79','unknown','none','blue, gray','Aleena','2014-12-20T09:53:16.481000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.171000Z','/images/species/16-aleena.png','Aleena are short, agile beings from the planet Aleen Minor. Known for their quick movements and cheerful demeanor, they live in tribal societies. Despite their small size, they are tough and energetic. Aleena have strong spiritual beliefs and live in harmony with nature. They are curious and open-hearted. Aleena represent joy, perseverance, and ancient wisdom.','Aleena are diminutive reptilian beings with strong limbs and wide-set eyes. Their homeworld, Aleen Minor, is a planet of deep chasms and surface wastelands. Aleena live in close-knit tribes and hold strong traditions tied to the land and its spirits. Their energetic nature allows them to survive in harsh terrain, often traveling rapidly on foot. The species is deeply spiritual, believing in balance between the surface and the underground. Though rarely seen in wider galactic affairs, some Aleena have ventured beyond their world, showcasing a fierce curiosity. Their speech is fast-paced, and their personalities often exude joy. Despite their size, they are fearless in defense of their home. Aleena societies prioritize harmony, oral history, and sacred rituals. They symbolize how the smallest cultures often hold the oldest truths. The Aleena spirit is light, wise, and enduring.',38),
	(17,'Vulptereen','unknown','sentient','100','unknown','yellow','none','grey','vulpterish','2014-12-20T09:57:33.128000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.173000Z','/images/species/17-vulptereen.webp','Vulptereens are short, stocky beings from the polluted world of Vulpter. They are known for their toughness and engineering skills. Their planet\'s decay shaped them into survivors. Vulptereens often work in maintenance, demolition, or industry. They are aggressive and pragmatic. Vulptereens represent raw utility, endurance, and grit.','Hailing from the industrial wasteland of Vulpter, Vulptereens have evolved in harsh, toxic environments. Their bodies are built low and solid, allowing them to maneuver through polluted ruins and factories. Life on Vulpter demands practical thinking, and Vulptereens excel in fields like mechanics and scavenging. Their society revolves around efficiency, with little tolerance for extravagance. This has made them valuable workers in the galaxy’s most dangerous sectors. Though their speech and demeanor can be blunt, they are deeply loyal once trust is earned. Vulptereens are often misjudged as crude or hostile, but underneath lies a tenacious spirit. They pride themselves on problem-solving, brute strength, and adaptability. The decay of their world taught them resilience and creativity. Vulptereens embody perseverance in a world that offers no comfort. Their presence in the galaxy is a reminder that survival often depends on function over form.',39),
	(18,'Xexto','unknown','sentient','125','unknown','black','none','grey, yellow, purple','Xextese','2014-12-20T10:02:13.915000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.175000Z','/images/species/18-xexto.png','Xexto are four-armed, agile beings from the planet Troiken. Their small size belies their incredible coordination. They excel in racing, engineering, and multitasking roles. Gasgano was a famous Xexto podracer. Xexto value competition and precision. They represent speed, cleverness, and ambition.','The Xexto are a nimble, four-armed species originating from the rocky world of Troiken. Their additional limbs and fast reflexes make them excellent pilots, mechanics, and athletes. Known for a sharp sense of balance and coordination, Xexto often engage in high-speed activities like podracing. Gasgano, one of their most notable members, became a star in the podracing circuits of the Outer Rim. Despite their small stature, Xexto are driven and competitive. Their culture rewards excellence, quick thinking, and relentless effort. With large eyes and small mouths, they are expressive and fast-talking. Xexto society is dynamic and inventive, with youth encouraged to explore technology and physical prowess. Their multitasking abilities also make them valuable in technical fields. Xexto reflect the values of agility, ambition, and determination to succeed against the odds.',40),
	(19,'Toong','unknown','sentient','200','unknown','orange','none','grey, green, yellow','Tundan','2014-12-20T10:08:36.795000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.177000Z','/images/species/19-toong.jpg','Toongs are lanky beings from the planet Toong’l, known for long limbs and nervous energy. They are awkward but clever, excelling in unusual trades. Ben Quadinaros is their most famous podracer. They often find themselves underestimated. Toongs reflect anxious courage, oddity, and persistence.','Toongs are tall, wiry beings with elongated faces and twitchy movements, hailing from the planet Toong’l. Known for their jumpy behavior and awkward mannerisms, they are often misjudged as incompetent. However, Toongs possess surprising cleverness and ingenuity. Ben Quadinaros, a podracer who faced setbacks but remained optimistic, represents their spirit. Toong culture is eccentric but focused, with an appreciation for creative problem-solving. They often gravitate toward niche professions or unconventional technologies. While not natural warriors, Toongs use their intellect and unpredictability to great effect. Their personalities range from timid to wildly expressive. Despite failures, they continue to pursue goals with stubborn persistence. Toongs remind the galaxy that even the awkward and anxious can be tenacious and brave. They represent humor, determination, and resilience through strangeness.',41),
	(20,'Cerean','mammal','sentient','200','unknown','hazel','red, blond, black, white','pale pink','Cerean','2014-12-20T10:15:33.765000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.179000Z','/images/species/20-cerean.png','Cereans are tall, intelligent beings from the planet Cerea. They have large, conical skulls housing binary brains. Cereans value tradition and mindfulness. Ki-Adi-Mundi was a Jedi Master from this species. They emphasize logic, calm, and balance. Cereans symbolize wisdom, patience, and duality.','Cereans are a thoughtful species known for their elongated craniums, which contain dual brains that process logic and emotion separately. Native to the peaceful world of Cerea, they lead contemplative lives and maintain strong communal values. Their culture prizes tradition, consensus, and harmony with nature. Ki-Adi-Mundi, a Jedi Master and member of the High Council, embodied their disciplined philosophy. Due to a low male birth rate, Cerean society structures marriage and family through unique social customs. Their ability to process conflicting thoughts makes them ideal mediators and philosophers. Though usually pacifist, Cereans defend their ideals when necessary. They are also skilled in telepathy and long-term strategic thinking. Their presence in the Jedi Order contributed to its diversity of thought. Cereans remind the galaxy that duality can be strength when balanced with wisdom.',43),
	(21,'Nautolan','amphibian','sentient','180','70','black','none','green, blue, brown, red','Nautila','2014-12-20T10:18:58.610000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.181000Z','/images/species/21-nautolan.jpg','Nautolans are amphibious beings from the oceanic planet Glee Anselm. They have head-tentacles sensitive to emotions. Nautolans are powerful swimmers and strong in the Force. Kit Fisto is their most famous Jedi. They value courage, connection, and fluidity. Nautolans represent intuition, bravery, and grace.','Nautolans are aquatic humanoids with large, black eyes and thirteen head-tentacles that detect pheromones and emotional states. Hailing from the water world Glee Anselm, they are natural swimmers and comfortable in both aquatic and terrestrial environments. Their society is peaceful but honors strength, clarity, and empathy. Kit Fisto, a Jedi Master known for his smile and courage, represented their values in the Clone Wars. Nautolans are deeply attuned to the Force and often express calm confidence. Their physiology gives them advantages in perception and reflexes, making them effective warriors and diplomats alike. Their culture values flow—whether in combat, conversation, or thought. They move with poise, speak with purpose, and fight with fluidity. Nautolans teach that understanding emotion can lead to peace. They stand as symbols of inner strength, clarity, and harmony with the world around them.',44),
	(22,'Zabrak','mammal','sentient','180','unknown','brown, orange','black','pale, brown, red, orange, yellow','Zabraki','2014-12-20T10:26:59.894000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.183000Z','/images/species/22-zabrak.jpg','Zabraks are fierce, horned humanoids from Iridonia. Known for their resilience and warrior culture, they are physically and mentally strong. Their signature facial tattoos mark personal achievements. Darth Maul, a deadly Sith Lord, is one of their kind. Zabraks thrive in hostile environments. They represent pride, endurance, and relentless will.','Zabraks are a determined and physically tough species native to the rugged world of Iridonia, though colonies exist on other planets. They are easily recognized by the crown of horns on their heads and often display intricate facial tattoos that signify personal trials or status. Zabraks are highly independent, with a culture that emphasizes self-reliance, pain endurance, and discipline. From a young age, many undergo rigorous training and survival challenges. Darth Maul, trained by Darth Sidious, is the most notorious Zabrak, embodying their fierce nature. However, not all Zabraks walk the path of darkness—many have served as Jedi or respected galactic citizens. Their dual hearts allow them enhanced stamina and resistance. Zabraks are deeply proud and have a strong sense of identity. Whether as warriors or scholars, they carry an inner fire that drives them forward. They represent survival, fierce independence, and mastery of one’s fate.',45),
	(23,'Tholothian','mammal','sentient','unknown','unknown','blue, indigo','unknown','dark','unknown','2014-12-20T10:29:13.798000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.186000Z','/images/species/23-tholothian.jpeg','Tholothians are a graceful species often associated with spiritual calm. Their elaborate headgear hides tendril-like features. Jedi Master Adi Gallia was one of their most respected members. Tholothians are wise and introspective. They are known for diplomacy and clarity of thought. They represent serenity, tradition, and deep insight.','Tholothians are a lesser-known but noble species recognized by their distinct head structures, often adorned with ornate wrappings. While much of their biology remains a mystery, their cultural traits are associated with wisdom, calm, and ritual. They are deeply spiritual and maintain ancient traditions that guide their behavior and ethics. Adi Gallia, a Tholothian Jedi Master and member of the Jedi High Council, exemplified their thoughtful and composed demeanor. Tholothians value balance and purpose, often drawn to roles of mediation, education, and leadership. Their society promotes peaceful resolution and internal harmony. Though not warlike, Tholothians are not passive; they stand firm when justice is threatened. Their contribution to the Jedi Order symbolizes their dedication to galactic peace. They reflect strength through wisdom and the power of insight over aggression.',46),
	(24,'Iktotchi','unknown','sentient','180','unknown','orange','none','pink','Iktotchese','2014-12-20T10:32:13.046000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.188000Z','/images/species/24-iktotchi.png','Iktotchi are horned humanoids from Iktotch with powerful precognitive abilities. Jedi Master Saesee Tiin was among them. Their society is isolated and disciplined. They are known for mental focus and piloting skills. Iktotchi embrace fate and inner strength. They symbolize foresight, stoicism, and control.','The Iktotchi hail from the storm-wracked moon of Iktotch. Known for their curved horns and somber appearance, they possess a rare natural ability for precognition—visions of the future. This ability is often limited but profound, guiding many in their life paths. Their culture is one of discipline, contemplation, and isolation, shaped by the harsh winds of their homeworld. Saesee Tiin, a Jedi Master and renowned starfighter pilot, embodied their strengths in the Jedi Council. Iktotchi are introverted by nature, often misunderstood as cold or detached. In truth, they value deep reflection and rarely speak without purpose. They are skilled navigators and spiritual thinkers, blending logic with instinct. The species is highly respected for its ability to remain calm in the face of uncertainty. Iktotchi represent trust in destiny, mental resilience, and silent strength.',47),
	(25,'Quermian','mammal','sentient','240','86','yellow','none','white','Quermian','2014-12-20T10:34:50.827000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.189000Z','/images/species/25-quermian.png','Quermians are tall, willowy beings with two brains and four arms. They hail from the planet Quermia. Quermians are curious, highly intelligent, and often involved in science or diplomacy. Jedi Master Yarael Poof was a notable member. Their calm demeanor belies a deep analytical mind. They symbolize intellect, empathy, and logic.','Quermians are elongated, graceful beings with slender necks, dual brains, and extra limbs hidden beneath their robes. Native to the planet Quermia, they are genetically related to the Xexto species and bred for heightened cognitive function. Their dual-brain structure allows for parallel processing and nuanced empathy, making them ideal negotiators and thinkers. Yarael Poof, a Quermian Jedi Master, served on the Jedi High Council with distinction. Their society is based on philosophical inquiry and mental discipline. Despite their seemingly frail appearance, Quermians possess strong mental defenses and a deep understanding of sentient behavior. They are often found in roles of education, science, or galactic policy. Their unique physiology supports calm, careful analysis of any situation. Quermians remind the galaxy of the power of reflection, clarity, and harmonious thinking.',48),
	(26,'Kel Dor','unknown','sentient','180','70','black, silver','none','peach, orange, red','Kel Dor','2014-12-20T10:49:21.692000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.191000Z','/images/species/26-kel-dor.png','Kel Dor are Force-sensitive beings from Dorin, known for wearing masks due to their unique atmosphere. Jedi Master Plo Koon was one of their greatest heroes. They value justice, clarity, and the Force. Kel Dor are calm and spiritually attuned. They represent justice, discipline, and balance.','The Kel Dor hail from Dorin, a planet with a gas atmosphere toxic to most species. As a result, Kel Dor wear protective masks and eye shields when off-world. They possess sharp reflexes and are often born with Force sensitivity. Plo Koon, one of the Jedi Order\'s most respected Masters, was a Kel Dor known for his compassion and strength. Kel Dor society emphasizes moral clarity, discipline, and responsibility. They have their own Force tradition—the Baran Do Sages—who study perception, energy, and justice. Kel Dor are known for decisive thinking and unshakable calm. Despite their outwardly stern appearance, they harbor deep empathy. Their voices, filtered through breathing devices, carry quiet authority. In battle or meditation, they act with precision. Kel Dor reflect harmony between mind, spirit, and action. Their presence reminds the galaxy of balance through purpose and peace through strength.',49),
	(27,'Chagrian','amphibian','sentient','190','unknown','blue','none','blue','Chagria','2014-12-20T10:53:28.795000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.193000Z','/images/species/27-chagrian.png','Chagrians are blue-skinned beings with large cranial horns. They come from the water-rich world of Champala. Mas Amedda, a prominent political figure, was one of their kind. Chagrians value formality, tradition, and order. They are calm and authoritative. Chagrians represent discipline, hierarchy, and loyalty.','Native to the aquatic world of Champala, Chagrians are a regal species marked by their tall frames, blue skin, and two prominent horns. They evolved in coastal environments, which influenced their serene demeanor and composed nature. Chagrians do not eat solid food as adults, absorbing nutrients from liquids. Their culture prizes political structure, public service, and ceremonial tradition. Mas Amedda, Vice Chair of the Galactic Senate and later Grand Vizier of the Empire, is a well-known Chagrian who served in both Republic and Imperial governments. Though some Chagrians remained neutral in galactic conflicts, others became symbols of bureaucratic control. Their voices are deep, and their tone formal. Chagrians are often seen in leadership, administration, or religious roles. They embody governance, order, and the burden of duty. Whether seen as noble or complicit, Chagrians are figures of influence and resolve.',50),
	(28,'Geonosian','insectoid','sentient','178','unknown','green, hazel','none','green, brown','Geonosian','2014-12-20T16:40:45.618000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.195000Z','/images/species/28-geonosian.png','Geonosians are insectoid beings from the harsh desert world of Geonosis. They are hive-minded and skilled in engineering and weapons design. Their society is rigid and built on obedience. The Death Star’s early designs began on Geonosis. They represent industrial might, loyalty, and calculated power.','Geonosians are tall, winged insectoids native to the arid planet Geonosis. They live in hive-like colonies led by aristocratic figures such as Archduke Poggle the Lesser. Geonosians are industrious and efficient, excelling in the design of mechanical systems and battle droids. It was their foundries that first constructed the early plans for the Death Star, aligning them briefly with the Separatists during the Clone Wars. Their society is highly stratified, with warriors, workers, and nobility functioning under strict control. Communication among them involves clicks and gestures, enhanced by technological translators. Though often seen as menacing, Geonosians are deeply loyal to their queens and colonies. They are survivors of a brutal environment and possess a natural cunning. Their role in galactic history is complex—part engineers, part pawns in greater schemes. Geonosians symbolize mechanical ingenuity, hive loyalty, and the sharp edge of obedience.',11),
	(29,'Mirialan','mammal','sentient','180','unknown','blue, green, red, yellow, brown, orange','black, brown','yellow, green','Mirialan','2014-12-20T16:46:48.290000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.197000Z','/images/species/29-mirialan.png','Mirialans are green- or yellow-skinned humanoids with facial tattoos symbolizing personal achievements. They are deeply spiritual and value tradition. Many serve as Jedi or diplomats. Luminara Unduli and Barriss Offee were prominent Mirialan Jedi. They are agile, composed, and introspective. Mirialans represent discipline, faith, and balance.','Mirialans are a humanoid species native to the planet Mirial, characterized by their olive or greenish skin tones and geometric facial tattoos. These tattoos are not merely decorative—they reflect a person’s accomplishments and spiritual journey. Mirialan culture places strong emphasis on discipline, tradition, and devotion to a greater moral or spiritual path. Many Mirialans are Force-sensitive and have served the Jedi Order with distinction. Jedi Master Luminara Unduli and her Padawan Barriss Offee are two of the most well-known examples. Mirialans possess great agility and composure, often preferring thoughtful, measured approaches to conflict. They are highly respected for their restraint and clarity of mind. Even in moments of crisis, they maintain inner calm. Mirialan society values personal growth and accountability. Their philosophies shape a culture rich in ritual and respect. They embody wisdom, serenity, and duty.',51),
	(30,'Clawdite','reptilian','sentient','180','70','yellow','none','green, yellow','Clawdite','2014-12-20T16:57:46.171000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.199000Z','/images/species/30-clawdite.png','Clawdites are shapeshifters from the planet Zolan. They can alter their appearance to mimic other humanoid forms. This ability makes them ideal spies and assassins. Zam Wesell, a Clawdite, worked with Jango Fett. Their society is secretive and misunderstood. Clawdites symbolize adaptability, secrecy, and moral ambiguity.','Clawdites are a reptilian humanoid species native to Zolan, best known for their remarkable ability to alter their appearance at will. This genetic trait evolved as a response to environmental pressures and later became a defining aspect of their identity. Shapeshifting allows Clawdites to blend into various populations, making them valuable as infiltrators, bounty hunters, or undercover agents. Zam Wesell, a bounty hunter allied with Jango Fett, brought notoriety to her species through her actions during the Clone Wars. Despite their abilities, Clawdites often face discrimination and suspicion across the galaxy, leading many to live in secrecy. Their homeworld experienced societal rifts due to the genetic divergence between Clawdites and baseline Zolanders. Clawdites navigate a complicated moral world, where identity is fluid and trust is hard-won. Their society values survival, cunning, and independence. Though feared by some, they are highly intelligent and capable beings. Clawdites remind the galaxy of the complexity of appearances and the shades of truth behind every mask.',54),
	(31,'Besalisk','amphibian','sentient','178','75','yellow','none','brown','besalisk','2014-12-20T17:28:28.821000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.200000Z','/images/species/31-besalisk.png','Besalisks are multi-armed, large-bodied beings known for their strength and appetites. They hail from the planet Ojom. Dexter Jettster, a diner owner and informant, was a famous Besalisk. They are sociable, blunt, and resourceful. Besalisks value loyalty and grit. They embody brawn, warmth, and streetwise savvy.','Besalisks are a robust species from the icy world of Ojom, identifiable by their large frame and four arms. They are known for their hearty appetite, physical resilience, and boisterous personalities. Many Besalisks are skilled mechanics, cooks, or laborers, finding pride in practical, hands-on work. Dexter Jettster, a diner owner on Coruscant and a trusted source of information for Obi-Wan Kenobi, exemplified the Besalisk way of life—street-smart, warm-hearted, and direct. Their society values hard work, good food, and honesty. Though not often found in politics or warfare, Besalisks are reliable allies and fierce defenders of their communities. Their multiple arms grant them enhanced multitasking and dexterity. While not known for subtlety, Besalisks are wise in their own way. They thrive in social environments and often build close-knit networks of trust. Besalisks represent tenacity, resilience, and no-nonsense wisdom.',55),
	(32,'Kaminoan','amphibian','sentient','220','80','black','none','grey, blue','Kaminoan','2014-12-20T17:31:24.838000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.202000Z','/images/species/32-kaminoan.png','Kaminoans are tall, elegant beings from the stormy ocean world of Kamino. They are master cloners and geneticists. Their culture is coldly efficient and highly secretive. The Grand Army of the Republic was created under their guidance. Kaminoans represent science, control, and moral detachment.','Kaminoans are a slender, long-necked species native to Kamino, a remote ocean planet plagued by constant storms. Adapted to aquatic and dim environments, they developed advanced scientific technologies—especially in cloning. The Kaminoans played a pivotal role in galactic history when they created the Grand Army of the Republic under the contract of Jedi Master Sifo-Dyas, later manipulated by Darth Sidious. Lama Su and Taun We were key figures in the clone program. Kaminoan society values precision, secrecy, and order. Their cold and detached approach to life and ethics often unsettles outsiders. While brilliant, they are emotionally distant and view most matters through a clinical lens. Their architecture is pristine and sterile, mirroring their mindset. Kaminoans represent the dangers and power of scientific advancement without ethical grounding. They embody genetic mastery, bureaucratic loyalty, and eerie calm.',10),
	(33,'Skakoan','mammal','sentient','unknown','unknown','unknown','none','grey, green','Skakoan','2014-12-20T17:53:54.515000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.204000Z','/images/species/33-skakoan.png','Skakoans are technologically reliant beings from the high-pressure world of Skako. They require suits to survive off-world. Wat Tambor, of the Techno Union, was a Skakoan. They value innovation and power. Skakoans represent industry, control, and insulated ambition.','Skakoans originate from the planet Skako, a world with intense atmospheric pressure and toxic gases by galactic standards. Off-world, they wear pressurized suits to survive, giving them a mechanical and mysterious appearance. Skakoan culture revolves around engineering, corporate hierarchy, and technological control. Wat Tambor, a member of the Separatist Council and leader of the Techno Union, was the most prominent Skakoan seen in galactic affairs. Their speech is filtered through vocal synthesizers, and their actions are calculated and goal-driven. Skakoans are often involved in cybernetics, weaponry, and industrial commerce. They prioritize innovation over morality and logic over emotion. Despite their detachment, they are capable of loyalty to their interests and allies. Their isolationist tendencies come from their biological vulnerability and cultural pride. Skakoans reflect the double-edged nature of progress: great power, but with a cost. They symbolize the cold pursuit of advancement.',56),
	(34,'Muun','mammal','sentient','190','100','black','none','grey, white','Muun','2014-12-20T17:58:19.088000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.207000Z','/images/species/34-muun.webp','Muuns are tall, thin beings with calculating minds and a gift for economics. They control the InterGalactic Banking Clan. Darth Sidious’s apprentice, Darth Plagueis, was a Muun. They are precise, strategic, and value order. Muuns symbolize greed, intellect, and systemic influence.','Muuns are a cerebral species native to Muunilinst, recognized for their elongated heads, thin bodies, and economic acumen. They are known throughout the galaxy as financiers, bankers, and economic planners, often serving as the architects behind major institutions. The InterGalactic Banking Clan, which financed much of the Clone Wars, was controlled by Muuns. They are cool, reserved, and highly rational beings, preferring to exert influence through currency and credit rather than brute force. Darth Plagueis the Wise, a Sith Lord obsessed with immortality, was a Muun who trained Darth Sidious. Muuns favor stability, contracts, and long-term thinking. Their societies are governed by balance sheets, legalism, and financial power. While they may not fight on battlefields, their reach can topple worlds. Muuns represent the invisible levers of control—systemic, patient, and dangerous. They embody intellect weaponized through commerce.',57),
	(35,'Togruta','mammal','sentient','180','94','red, orange, yellow, green, blue, black','none','red, white, orange, yellow, green, blue','Togruti','2014-12-20T18:44:03.246000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.209000Z','/images/species/35-togruta.jpg','Togrutas are colorful, montral-bearing beings from Shili. They value community, nature, and harmony. Ahsoka Tano and Shaak Ti are among their most famous. Togrutas rely on teamwork and situational awareness. Their culture embraces intuition and belonging. They represent cooperation, grace, and resilience.','Togrutas are a striking species from the grassy plains of Shili, known for their colorful skin, striped lekku, and sensory montrals. The montrals grant them passive echolocation, enhancing their awareness of surroundings. Togruta culture places great value on community and unity over individualism. Members are taught from an early age to function as part of a group, respecting nature and the balance of life. Jedi like Ahsoka Tano and Shaak Ti embodied the Togruta ideals of grace, empathy, and strength. Togrutas often move fluidly in combat and are especially attuned to the living Force. Their society is harmonious, yet they are fierce when defending others. They prefer diplomacy but do not shy from danger. Togrutas symbolize balance with the environment, the power of intuition, and the strength of collective purpose. Their resilience and independence shine brightest when tested by adversity.',58),
	(36,'Kaleesh','reptile','sentient','170','80','yellow','none','brown, orange, tan','Kaleesh','2014-12-20T19:45:42.537000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.210000Z','/images/species/36-kaleesh.png','The Kaleesh are a warlike reptilian species from the planet Kalee. Known for their honor and martial prowess, they wear bone masks to honor fallen ancestors. General Grievous was once a Kaleesh warlord named Qymaen jai Sheelal. Their society reveres warriors and despises foreign domination. The Kaleesh symbolize pride, vengeance, and resilience. They are fierce and driven by legacy.','The Kaleesh are native to the war-torn world of Kalee, a harsh planet that forged them into proud and skilled warriors. With leathery skin, sharp claws, and fierce eyes, they often adorn themselves with traditional bone masks that honor their dead and symbolize their enduring spirit. The Kaleesh lived in near-constant conflict with neighboring species and colonial powers, leading to a deep-rooted mistrust of outsiders. One of their most famous members, Qymaen jai Sheelal, later known as General Grievous, became a symbol of their warrior heritage. Grievous\'s transformation into a cyborg was orchestrated by the Sith, using his hatred and military genius to serve their cause. Despite this, his Kaleesh roots remained central to his identity. The Kaleesh religion is based on ancestor veneration and a spiritual understanding of battle. They craft masks and weapons with deep symbolic meaning, passing them through generations. Their society values bravery, strategy, and honor in combat. Though often seen as brutal by outsiders, the Kaleesh hold a complex and proud culture. Their resilience in the face of oppression has become legendary. The galaxy remembers them as fierce combatants who never surrender. The Kaleesh spirit remains indomitable even in defeat. They represent cultural pride, remembrance, and the dark cost of war.',59),
	(37,'Pau\'an','mammal','sentient','190','700','black','none','grey','Utapese','2014-12-20T20:35:06.777000Z','2014-12-20T21:36:42.212000Z','/images/species/37-pau-an.png','Pau’ans are tall, gaunt beings with sunken features and long lifespans. They hail from the sinkhole world of Utapau. Known for their solemn speech and regal presence, they serve as administrators and diplomats. The Grand Inquisitor was a former Pau’an Jedi Temple Guard. Pau’ans embody patience, formality, and veiled authority. Their presence is both eerie and commanding.','Pau’ans, also known as the Utai’s surface counterparts, are the tall, narrow-faced inhabitants of Utapau. Distinguished by their pallid skin, deep-set eyes, and elongated skulls, Pau’ans have an average lifespan of over two centuries. They speak in slow, deliberate tones and often adopt a formal manner that reflects their governance traditions. Pau’ans serve as the ruling class of Utapau, overseeing relations with outsiders and managing subterranean cities carved into the planet’s immense sinkholes. One notable Pau’an, the Grand Inquisitor, was once a Jedi Temple Guard before turning to the dark side and leading the Inquisitorius under Darth Vader. This transformation marked a departure from Pau’an norms, as most of their kind value balance and structure. Pau’ans are viewed with curiosity and wariness due to their haunting appearance and enigmatic demeanor. Their leadership style is measured and strategic, often preferring diplomacy over conflict. They value hierarchy, tradition, and control. Despite their eerie look, they are not inherently malicious. Pau’ans reflect a species shaped by environmental extremes and long cultural memory. They serve as reminders that still waters can run deep and powerful. Their presence in galactic affairs, though subtle, carries lasting weight.',12);
INSERT INTO `starships` (`id`, `name`, `model`, `starship_class`, `manufacturer`, `cost_in_credits`, `length`, `crew`, `passengers`, `max_atmosphering_speed`, `hyperdrive_rating`, `MGLT`, `cargo_capacity`, `consumables`, `created`, `edited`, `image_url`, `short_description`, `long_description`)
VALUES
	(2,'CR90 corvette','CR90 corvette','corvette','Corellian Engineering Corporation','3500000','150','30-165','600','950','2.0','60','3000000','1 year','2014-12-10T14:20:33.369000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.867000Z','/images/starships/2-cr90-corvette.png','The CR90 corvette is a fast and versatile vessel used primarily by the Rebel Alliance. Also known as the Corellian Corvette, it was designed for diplomatic missions and blockade running. Its most famous variant is the Tantive IV. The ship balances speed, firepower, and endurance. It often served as a flagship for small fleets. The CR90 symbolizes defiance, mobility, and resilience.','The CR90 corvette, often called the Corellian Corvette, is a multi-purpose starship designed by Corellian Engineering Corporation. Measuring 150 meters in length, it became iconic for its long cylindrical shape and massive rear engine bank. Originally intended for diplomatic transport and patrol duties, the ship gained prominence during the Galactic Civil War as a favored vessel of the Rebel Alliance. The Tantive IV, used by Princess Leia, famously attempted to escape the Empire with stolen Death Star plans. Its speed allowed it to outrun larger warships, making it ideal for hit-and-run tactics and evasive maneuvers. Equipped with multiple turbolaser turrets and reinforced shielding, it was capable of standing its ground in skirmishes. Modular design allowed customization for medical, cargo, or combat roles. The CR90’s reliability made it popular among smugglers and resistance groups. Its presence in key battles underscored its role in the struggle for freedom. The ship’s compact size allowed it to operate in tight star systems. The CR90 served as a lifeline, a command center, and a symbol of hope. Its silhouette became a familiar sight in Rebel fleets. Despite advances in technology, its legacy endured. Veterans revered it, and its story lived on in historical archives. The CR90 remains a testament to ingenuity, perseverance, and rebellion.'),
	(3,'Star Destroyer','Imperial I-class Star Destroyer','Star Destroyer','Kuat Drive Yards','150000000','1,600','47,060','n/a','975','2.0','60','36000000','2 years','2014-12-10T15:08:19.848000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.870000Z','/images/starships/3-star-destroyer.png','The Star Destroyer is a massive warship used by the Galactic Empire. Its dagger-shaped design and immense firepower make it a symbol of fear and control. These capital ships dominate space battles and enforce imperial authority. Star Destroyers can carry thousands of troops, fighters, and vehicles. Their presence often signals occupation or destruction. They represent tyranny, dominance, and technological might.','Star Destroyers are colossal capital ships built by Kuat Drive Yards, forming the backbone of the Imperial Navy. Measuring over 1,600 meters long, they possess a wedge-shaped design optimized for frontal firepower and intimidation. Equipped with hundreds of turbolasers, ion cannons, and tractor beams, these ships project immense destructive power. Star Destroyers serve not only as weapons but also as mobile command centers capable of planetary subjugation. They can carry stormtroopers, TIE fighters, ground vehicles, and even entire regiments. The most iconic model, the Imperial-class Star Destroyer, enforced the Emperor’s will across countless systems. Their appearance instills terror and represents imperial dominance. The sheer scale of these vessels overshadows most enemy fleets. Some models, like the Super Star Destroyer, dwarf even the standard variants. These ships patrol hyperlanes, blockade planets, and hunt rebel forces. Their hyperdrive systems enable swift deployment across the galaxy. Despite their might, they are vulnerable to coordinated assaults, as seen in key Rebel victories. The loss of a Star Destroyer is both rare and symbolically significant. Their ominous presence looms in the history of galactic warfare. Star Destroyers are icons of oppression and power, towering over the stars they seek to control.'),
	(5,'Sentinel-class landing craft','Sentinel-class landing craft','landing craft','Sienar Fleet Systems, Cyngus Spaceworks','240000','38','5','75','1000','1.0','70','180000','1 month','2014-12-10T15:48:00.586000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.873000Z','/images/starships/5-sentinel-class-landing-craft.png','The Sentinel-class landing craft is an armored Imperial shuttle used for troop transport. Designed for atmospheric entry, it carries soldiers and vehicles directly into battle. Its wings and dorsal fin give it a distinct silhouette. Armed with laser cannons, it can defend itself during landings. These craft are used in planetary invasions. The Sentinel-class reflects order, control, and military efficiency.','The Sentinel-class landing craft, manufactured by Sienar Fleet Systems, is a heavy-duty transport designed to move Imperial forces from orbit to battlefield. Unlike the more familiar Lambda-class shuttle, the Sentinel is built for combat landings. It features reinforced hull plating, a central boarding ramp, and multiple gun placements, including wing-mounted blasters. Its large wings fold vertically during descent and flare out for stabilization upon entry. These ships carry stormtroopers, speeder bikes, and support gear, often launching ahead of ground operations. Their role is critical in planetary subjugations and surprise attacks. The dorsal fin contains sensor arrays for navigation and communication. Pilots undergo specialized training due to the ship\'s high-mass atmospheric handling. The Sentinel’s intimidating shape projects the Empire’s dominance. These shuttles operate alongside Star Destroyers and Gozanti cruisers in fleet actions. Deployed rapidly and efficiently, they enable the swift establishment of Imperial control. Rebel forces often target them due to their vital strategic function. Despite not being flashy, the Sentinel-class embodies the Empire\'s doctrine of strength and order. Its reliability in countless invasions makes it a fixture in the machinery of galactic conquest.'),
	(9,'Death Star','DS-1 Orbital Battle Station','Deep Space Mobile Battlestation','Imperial Department of Military Research, Sienar Fleet Systems','1000000000000','120000','342,953','843,342','n/a','4.0','10','1000000000000','3 years','2014-12-10T16:36:50.509000Z','2014-12-20T21:26:24.783000Z','/images/starships/9-death-star.png','The Death Star is a moon-sized battle station capable of destroying entire planets. Built by the Galactic Empire, it is the ultimate weapon of fear and control. Its superlaser can annihilate worlds in seconds. The station houses vast Imperial forces and weaponry. It was destroyed twice by the Rebel Alliance. The Death Star represents tyranny, terror, and overreach.','The Death Star is the most fearsome weapon ever created in the galaxy, designed to enforce the Emperor\'s rule through fear. Measuring over 160 kilometers in diameter, it houses countless stormtroopers, starfighters, and command staff. Its core feature is a planet-destroying superlaser capable of reducing entire worlds to rubble. The first Death Star was revealed when it destroyed Alderaan as a show of strength. However, a weakness in its reactor core allowed Luke Skywalker to destroy it during the Battle of Yavin. A second, even larger Death Star was built but destroyed during the Battle of Endor before completion. Both versions represent the Empire\'s reliance on fear and brute force. Construction of these stations drained massive resources, reflecting the arrogance of the Imperial regime. They were technological marvels but moral abominations. Inside, the stations featured military barracks, hangars, detention blocks, and command centers. Tarkin and Palpatine used the Death Stars as political tools of suppression. The Rebel victories against them became rallying cries across the galaxy. The destruction of the Death Stars marked turning points in the Galactic Civil War. Their legacy endures as cautionary tales of unchecked power and hubris.'),
	(10,'Millennium Falcon','YT-1300 light freighter','Light freighter','Corellian Engineering Corporation','100000','34.37','4','6','1050','0.5','75','100000','2 months','2014-12-10T16:59:45.094000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.880000Z','/images/starships/10-millennium-falcon.png','The Millennium Falcon is a legendary Corellian freighter modified for speed and firepower. Piloted by Han Solo and Chewbacca, it played vital roles in Rebel and Resistance victories. Its unassuming look hides advanced systems. The ship is fast, tough, and iconic. It represents defiance, freedom, and heart. The Falcon is more than a ship—it\'s a symbol of rebellion.','The Millennium Falcon, a YT-1300 Corellian freighter, is one of the most famous ships in the galaxy. Despite its battered exterior, it boasts unmatched speed and agility thanks to heavy modifications by owner-pilot Han Solo. Assisted by Chewbacca, the Falcon completed the Kessel Run in less than twelve parsecs. It features hidden compartments, enhanced shields, and a powerful hyperdrive. The ship played crucial roles in major battles, from the destruction of both Death Stars to assaults during the Resistance era. Often dismissed as a \'piece of junk,\' its performance consistently proves otherwise. The Falcon has carried royalty, Jedi, smugglers, and heroes alike. Its design allows both cargo hauling and heavy combat. The ship’s interior is a chaotic blend of upgrades and worn parts. After Solo\'s death, Rey inherited it, continuing its storied journey. The Falcon has evaded fleets, rescued allies, and changed history. Its rugged charm and resilience mirror the spirit of those who fly it. The ship is known across star systems, often followed by legend. It\'s a beacon of hope and rebellion. Every scorch mark tells a tale. The Millennium Falcon endures as a symbol of courage and freedom.'),
	(11,'Y-wing','BTL Y-wing','assault starfighter','Koensayr Manufacturing','134999','14','2','0','1000km','1.0','80','110','1 week','2014-12-12T11:00:39.817000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.883000Z','/images/starships/11-y-wing.png','The Y-wing is a durable Rebel bomber designed for long-range assaults. Known for its exposed mechanics and heavy payloads, it excels in precision strikes. It served in key battles like Scarif and Endor. Y-wings deliver torpedoes and ion blasts with devastating effect. Though slow, they are incredibly resilient. The Y-wing reflects endurance, reliability, and heavy firepower.','The BTL-A4 Y-wing starfighter is a powerful attack craft used by the Rebel Alliance for bombing runs and precision strikes. Originally developed by Koensayr Manufacturing, Y-wings were repurposed from Clone Wars service into vital assets in the Rebellion. Their stripped-down exteriors reveal rugged mechanics, making them easier to repair under duress. Y-wings carry heavy ordnance, including proton torpedoes and ion cannons capable of disabling capital ships. Despite being slower than other starfighters, they can withstand immense damage. Pilots appreciate their survivability in high-risk missions. During the Battle of Yavin, Gold Squadron flew Y-wings in the first attack run on the Death Star. They also saw action during the battles of Scarif and Endor. While visually outdated, their performance is reliable. These ships often operate in squadrons with X-wings for coordinated strikes. Their two-seater design supports both a pilot and astromech droid for tactical support. The Y-wing’s presence signals strategic bombing power. Though newer models replaced them, many remained in service due to dependability. The Y-wing represents the Rebellion’s resourceful use of aging tech. It is a workhorse of war. Where precision and power are needed, the Y-wing soars into battle.'),
	(12,'X-wing','T-65 X-wing','Starfighter','Incom Corporation','149999','12.5','1','0','1050','1.0','100','110','1 week','2014-12-12T11:19:05.340000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.886000Z','/images/starships/12-x-wing.png','The X-wing is the Rebel Alliance’s primary starfighter, famed for its versatility and balance. It features s-foils that open into an X-shape during combat. Fast, agile, and deadly, it excels in both dogfighting and bombing runs. X-wings were vital in battles like Yavin and Endor. Pilots admire their power and flexibility. The X-wing stands for resistance, freedom, and heroism.','The T-65B X-wing starfighter, manufactured by Incom Corporation, is a multirole fighter and the backbone of the Rebel Alliance’s fleet. It is equipped with four laser cannons and proton torpedo launchers. Its iconic s-foils spread into an X-shape in attack mode, giving the ship its name. X-wings balance speed, durability, and firepower, making them ideal for space superiority and escort missions. Pilots love their responsive controls and rugged survivability. X-wings played key roles in major galactic conflicts, including the Battle of Yavin where Luke Skywalker used one to destroy the first Death Star. Each X-wing has an astromech droid, often an R2 unit, to assist with navigation and repairs. Their hyperdrives allow for independent travel, unlike TIE fighters. During the Galactic Civil War and into the Resistance era, X-wings remained trusted combat platforms. Poe Dameron flew a specialized black and orange T-70 variant in the sequel era. X-wings symbolize courage and unity among rebel forces. Their success stories inspired hope across star systems. Easy to modify, they saw many upgrades. Whether flying solo or in formation, X-wings are symbols of tactical brilliance. They remain legendary across generations.'),
	(13,'TIE Advanced x1','Twin Ion Engine Advanced x1','Starfighter','Sienar Fleet Systems','unknown','9.2','1','0','1200','1.0','105','150','5 days','2014-12-12T11:21:32.991000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.889000Z','/images/starships/13-tie-advanced-x1.png','The TIE Advanced x1 was a prototype starfighter flown by Darth Vader. It featured advanced shields and a hyperdrive, unlike standard TIE fighters. With bent wings and a sleek design, it stood out in combat. The ship was agile, deadly, and personally customized. It pursued the Millennium Falcon and faced Luke at Yavin. The TIE Advanced x1 represents power, precision, and Sith supremacy.','The TIE Advanced x1 was a specialized starfighter developed by Sienar Fleet Systems as a prototype for advanced Imperial starships. This model combined the signature TIE fighter design with technological upgrades, including deflector shields, a hyperdrive, and enhanced targeting systems. Its wings curved outward in a distinctive shape, reducing its profile and giving it a unique aerodynamic silhouette. Most famously, the TIE Advanced x1 was flown by Darth Vader during the Battle of Yavin. The ship featured increased speed, armor, and maneuverability, making it formidable in dogfights. Unlike standard TIEs, it could operate independently over long distances. Its onboard systems allowed Vader to track and engage the Rebel forces with ruthless efficiency. Despite its limited production, the TIE Advanced x1 was a benchmark for future developments in Imperial fighter design. It embodied the Empire’s ambition to dominate space with elite technology. The fighter’s escape from Yavin after the Death Star’s destruction symbolized the Sith’s survival and ongoing threat. Vader’s personal modifications made it more lethal than any TIE in service. Its legacy continues as one of the deadliest starfighters ever built for the dark side.'),
	(15,'Executor','Executor-class star dreadnought','Star dreadnought','Kuat Drive Yards, Fondor Shipyards','1143350000','19000','279,144','38000','n/a','2.0','40','250000000','6 years','2014-12-15T12:31:42.547000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.893000Z','/images/starships/15-executor.png','The Executor was Darth Vader’s massive Super Star Destroyer. Over 19 kilometers long, it served as the command ship of the Imperial fleet. Its overwhelming firepower and size struck fear into enemies. The Executor led the assault on Hoth and pursued the Millennium Falcon. It was destroyed at Endor during the Death Star battle. The ship represents overwhelming might and authoritarian terror.','The Executor was the lead ship of the Executor-class Super Star Destroyers and served as Darth Vader’s personal flagship. Commissioned by Emperor Palpatine and constructed at Kuat Drive Yards, it spanned over 19 kilometers in length. With thousands of turbolasers, ion cannons, and a crew of over 280,000, it dwarfed all other ships in the Imperial Navy. The Executor’s intimidating silhouette loomed across battlefields, acting as a mobile fortress and command hub. It played major roles in key operations, including the pursuit of the Rebel fleet after the Battle of Hoth. Vader personally directed missions from its bridge, exerting fear and control over the galaxy. Its sheer size allowed it to carry multiple legions, walkers, and starfighters. The ship’s presence alone could quell uprisings or force planetary surrender. During the Battle of Endor, it became the centerpiece of the Imperial fleet but was ultimately destroyed when a Rebel A-wing crashed into its bridge. Plunging into the Death Star’s surface, it exploded in a fiery blaze. The Executor symbolized imperial dominance and the Sith\'s grip on the galaxy, and its loss marked the crumbling of that power.'),
	(17,'Rebel transport','GR-75 medium transport','Medium transport','Gallofree Yards, Inc.','unknown','90','6','90','650','4.0','20','19000000','6 months','2014-12-15T12:34:52.264000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.895000Z','/images/starships/17-rebel-transport.png','The Rebel transport was a vital support ship used by the Rebel Alliance. It carried troops, equipment, and refugees across the galaxy. Though lightly armed, it was key during evacuations like Hoth. These ships were modified freighters turned lifelines. Often escorted by starfighters, they symbolized hope in retreat. Rebel transports represent survival, sacrifice, and resistance.','The GR-75 medium transport, commonly referred to as the Rebel transport, was a cargo freighter repurposed by the Rebel Alliance for war efforts. Manufactured by Gallofree Yards, Inc., the ship featured a modular hull and large cargo holds. Its most famous role came during the evacuation of Echo Base on Hoth, where it carried personnel and materials to safety under heavy Imperial fire. Although it lacked heavy armament, it was equipped with shield generators and minimal laser defenses. Its design prioritized function over form, allowing for quick loading and adaptable cargo configurations. The ships were often escorted by X-wings or Y-wings during critical operations. Many were converted into medical ships, command posts, or even makeshift barracks. These vessels carried refugees and supplies, bridging systems across the Outer Rim. Despite their fragility, Rebel transports demonstrated the Alliance\'s ability to repurpose what little they had. Every successful mission meant lives saved and battles endured. The ships became emblems of perseverance in a war of attrition. In times of retreat, the Rebel transport meant survival and the will to continue the fight.'),
	(21,'Slave 1','Firespray-31-class patrol and attack','Patrol craft','Kuat Systems Engineering','unknown','21.5','1','6','1000','3.0','70','70000','1 month','2014-12-15T13:00:56.332000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.897000Z','/images/starships/21-slave-1.png','Slave I is the personal starship of bounty hunter Boba Fett. Originally owned by Jango Fett, it has a unique vertical flight mode and heavy weaponry. The ship is equipped with blasters, seismic charges, and tracking systems. Slave I has pursued fugitives across the galaxy. Its silhouette is feared by those who break the law. It represents danger, skill, and relentless pursuit.','Slave I is a modified Firespray-31-class patrol and attack craft, best known as the personal ship of Boba Fett and his father, Jango Fett. Built by Kuat Systems Engineering, the ship has a unique design that positions it vertically during flight. Its rugged frame is enhanced with powerful weaponry, including twin blaster cannons, ion cannons, seismic charges, and missile launchers. Jango used the ship during the Clone Wars before passing it down to Boba, who maintained and upgraded it further. Slave I was used in the capture of Han Solo and other high-value bounties. Its sensor systems and stealth capabilities made it ideal for bounty hunting. The ship could hold prisoners in carbonite and featured multiple hidden compartments. Its armored hull allowed it to withstand direct assaults and hyperspace travel. Though small in size, Slave I could take on larger vessels with strategic strikes. Its silhouette became synonymous with Fett\'s deadly reputation. The ship saw action during several galactic conflicts and continued to fly long after the fall of the Empire. Slave I is not just a vessel—it is a hunter\'s lair and an icon of fear.'),
	(22,'Imperial shuttle','Lambda-class T-4a shuttle','Armed government transport','Sienar Fleet Systems','240000','20','6','20','850','1.0','50','80000','2 months','2014-12-15T13:04:47.235000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.900000Z','/images/starships/22-imperial-shuttle.png','The Imperial shuttle, or Lambda-class shuttle, is a transport used by the Galactic Empire. It features folding wings and strong shielding. The shuttle carries troops, officers, or high-value cargo. Darth Vader and Emperor Palpatine often traveled in it. Despite its utilitarian look, it became a symbol of Imperial authority. The shuttle reflects control, precision, and dark elegance.','The Lambda-class T-4a shuttle is a transport and utility ship built by Sienar Fleet Systems for the Galactic Empire. With its tri-wing configuration and central dorsal fin, the shuttle stands out in both design and purpose. Primarily used for ferrying officers, stormtroopers, and dignitaries, it was equipped with deflector shields and twin laser cannons. The folding wings enable tight landings and atmospheric reentry. The shuttle’s rugged design allowed operations across space and planetary surfaces. It gained notoriety as the transport of choice for Darth Vader and Emperor Palpatine. Though not built for combat, it could hold its own with adequate escort. During the Battle of Endor, the stolen Imperial shuttle Tydirium was used by the Rebels to infiltrate the forest moon. Its versatility made it a staple in the Imperial fleet. Inside, the ship had space for troops, cargo, or command modules. The Lambda shuttle became a recognizable silhouette of the Empire’s presence, especially on occupied worlds. It symbolized discipline and dominance, descending like a blade wherever authority was needed.'),
	(23,'EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate','EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate','Escort ship','Kuat Drive Yards','8500000','300','854','75','800','2.0','40','6000000','2 years','2014-12-15T13:06:30.813000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.902000Z','/images/starships/23-ef76-nebulon-b-escort-frigate.png','The EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate is a mid-sized Rebel warship used for defense and support. Originally an Imperial design, many were captured or defected. The frigate is long and narrow, with a fragile spine structure. It served as a medical and command vessel. These ships were vital in protecting fleets and evacuating wounded. They represent support, strategy, and adaptive warfare.','The EF76 Nebulon-B escort frigate was developed by Kuat Drive Yards for the Galactic Empire but became more commonly associated with the Rebel Alliance. Designed as an anti-starfighter escort ship, it features a distinct two-section build joined by a thin midsection, making it vulnerable but agile. The Nebulon-B was quickly adopted by the Rebellion due to its balance of firepower and utility. Many were stolen, purchased on the black market, or salvaged from skirmishes. The frigate housed medical bays, making it essential for treating wounded personnel, as seen with Luke Skywalker after the events of Cloud City. It also served as a mobile command post in several battles. Its weapons included turbolasers and point-defense cannons, giving it the ability to protect larger ships or hold ground in small fleets. The ship’s silhouette became symbolic of the Rebellion’s resourcefulness. Though not as powerful as Star Destroyers, it held its own through maneuverability and crew coordination. The EF76 reflected the spirit of survival and adaptation. Its value wasn’t in might but in service, resilience, and community.'),
	(27,'Calamari Cruiser','MC80 Liberty type Star Cruiser','Star Cruiser','Mon Calamari shipyards','104000000','1200','5400','1200','n/a','1.0','60','unknown','2 years','2014-12-18T10:54:57.804000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.904000Z','/images/starships/27-calamari-cruiser.png','The Calamari Cruiser is a large capital ship designed by the Mon Calamari. Unique in appearance, each cruiser was handcrafted. These vessels led many Rebel assaults, including at Endor. With powerful shields and heavy turbolasers, they balanced strength with elegance. They carried fighters, troops, and hope. The Calamari Cruiser stands for craftsmanship, unity, and liberation.','The Calamari Cruiser, often referred to as the Mon Calamari star cruiser, is a class of capital ship created by the Mon Calamari species. Unlike mass-produced Imperial ships, each cruiser was individually crafted, giving it a unique aesthetic with organic, flowing lines. Outfitted with advanced shields, heavy turbolasers, and ion cannons, these ships became the backbone of the Rebel fleet. Their adaptability allowed for multi-role use—command, combat, transport, and support. The MC80 Liberty-type and Home One-type were among the most famous, with Admiral Ackbar commanding from Home One during the Battle of Endor. These cruisers were originally passenger liners repurposed into warships, reflecting the Mon Calamari’s commitment to the Rebellion. Their large hangars supported starfighters like X-wings and B-wings. Strong armor and shield generators gave them high survivability in prolonged engagements. Calamari Cruisers carried leaders, warriors, and the ideals of a free galaxy. Their sleek hulls shone with hope in battles where the odds were grim. More than war machines, they were floating cities of resistance. The Mon Calamari used their culture and art to resist tyranny, turning their vessels into icons of liberty.'),
	(28,'A-wing','RZ-1 A-wing Interceptor','Starfighter','Alliance Underground Engineering, Incom Corporation','175000','9.6','1','0','1300','1.0','120','40','1 week','2014-12-18T11:16:34.542000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.907000Z','/images/starships/28-a-wing.png','The A-wing is a fast, agile interceptor used by the Rebel Alliance. It was designed for speed and hit-and-run tactics. Its small frame and powerful engines make it ideal for outrunning enemies. A-wings were instrumental in the Battle of Endor. Despite their light armor, they packed strong firepower. The A-wing stands for precision, speed, and daring rebellion.','The RZ-1 A-wing interceptor is one of the fastest starfighters used by the Rebel Alliance. Originally developed by the Alliance’s engineers, its sleek, wedge-shaped frame and dual engines allow for extreme maneuverability. It was created to counter the Empire’s superior TIE Interceptors, giving Rebels the upper hand in dogfights. Equipped with laser cannons and concussion missiles, the A-wing excels in quick strikes and evasive attacks. Its small size and speed make it difficult for enemy systems to lock on. The fighter\'s cockpit was notoriously cramped and required skilled pilots. Despite lacking heavy shielding or armor, it delivered devastating hit-and-run tactics against larger ships. A notable moment in A-wing history came during the Battle of Endor, when pilot Arvel Crynyd crashed his A-wing into the bridge of the Executor, leading to the destruction of Darth Vader’s flagship. A-wings became a symbol of the Rebel fleet’s audacity and adaptability. Their appearance was distinct, often customized by pilots. The ship\'s speed allowed it to be used for reconnaissance and deep-strike missions. Though high-risk to fly, they offered unmatched performance for experienced aces. The A-wing represents the fast, fearless heart of the Rebellion.'),
	(29,'B-wing','A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter','Assault Starfighter','Slayn & Korpil','220000','16.9','1','0','950','2.0','91','45','1 week','2014-12-18T11:18:04.763000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.909000Z','/images/starships/29-b-wing.png','The B-wing is a heavy assault starfighter designed to destroy capital ships. It has a unique rotating cockpit and powerful weapons. Created by the Mon Calamari, it was part of the Rebel fleet’s evolution. Though hard to fly, it delivered massive damage in key battles. The B-wing was essential at Endor. It symbolizes innovation, risk, and firepower.','The B-wing, or the A/SF-01 B-wing starfighter, was developed by the Mon Calamari with the goal of combating Imperial capital ships. With a distinctive cross-shaped profile and gyroscopic rotating cockpit, the B-wing was a marvel of unconventional design. It featured multiple laser cannons, ion cannons, and proton torpedo launchers, making it one of the most heavily armed starfighters in the Rebel fleet. Its folding wings allowed it to switch configurations between storage, flight, and combat modes. Though its control systems were complex, experienced pilots could unleash devastating firepower. B-wings played a critical role during the Battle of Endor, targeting and disabling Star Destroyers. The ship’s ability to deliver sustained damage made it a threat to larger Imperial vessels. Though slower than other fighters, its strength lay in brute force and advanced targeting. It was also equipped with deflector shields for protection during direct assaults. Many B-wing squadrons were led by ace pilots willing to brave the chaos of large fleet engagements. The ship became a testament to Rebel ingenuity and the contributions of the Mon Calamari. Despite its complexity, it was embraced as a symbol of destructive capability and tactical edge.'),
	(31,'Republic Cruiser','Consular-class cruiser','Space cruiser','Corellian Engineering Corporation','unknown','115','9','16','900','2.0','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-19T17:01:31.488000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.912000Z','/images/starships/31-republic-cruiser.png','The Republic Cruiser was a diplomatic and transport vessel used by the Galactic Republic. Known for its red hull and sleek profile, it carried Jedi and officials. The ship was designed for quick travel and secure communication. It often preceded negotiations and conflict resolutions. A cruiser was sent to Naboo at the start of the Clone Wars. It represents diplomacy, order, and the Republic’s reach.','The Consular-class Republic Cruiser was a starship used primarily for diplomatic missions by the Galactic Republic. Easily recognizable by its crimson hull, the ship signified neutrality and peaceful intent in diplomatic zones. It was lightly armed but fast and equipped with advanced communication arrays. These cruisers were commonly used to ferry Jedi Knights, senators, and ambassadors across the galaxy. The vessel’s modular design allowed for rapid conversion to other roles, including command posts and medevac units. Its role in the blockade of Naboo was historic, as Jedi Master Qui-Gon Jinn and Obi-Wan Kenobi arrived aboard such a ship. The cruiser was destroyed by a Trade Federation ambush, marking a key moment that ignited galactic conflict. Though vulnerable in hostile situations, its primary role was to maintain peace and project the Republic’s presence. The cruiser reflected the Republic’s values—diplomacy over violence, dialogue before war. During the Clone Wars, some were retrofitted for military logistics. In its original purpose, however, it stood as a flying embassy and a beacon of interstellar cooperation. The Republic Cruiser was a symbol of peace amid growing unrest.'),
	(32,'Droid control ship','Lucrehulk-class Droid Control Ship','Droid control ship','Hoersch-Kessel Drive, Inc.','unknown','3170','175','139000','n/a','2.0','unknown','4000000000','500 days','2014-12-19T17:04:06.323000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.915000Z','/images/starships/32-droid-control-ship.png','The Droid Control Ship was the core of the Trade Federation’s battle droid armies. Shaped like a massive donut with a central sphere, it directed droids remotely. Destroying it could disable an entire army. It was heavily protected during planetary invasions. One was destroyed during the Battle of Naboo. The ship reflects mechanized warfare, control, and central vulnerability.','The Droid Control Ship was a specialized Lucrehulk-class battleship used by the Trade Federation to command and coordinate vast numbers of battle droids. These enormous vessels were originally cargo freighters, repurposed and retrofitted with hangars, control hubs, and defenses. Their spherical command center, located in the middle of the ring-like hull, served as the main processor for droid communication. Without it, most Trade Federation droids would become inoperative. During the invasion of Naboo, one such ship served as the nerve center of the entire occupation force. Anakin Skywalker destroyed that ship from the inside, leading to the shutdown of all droid forces on the planet. The vessel’s design prioritized command capability over speed or agility, relying on fighter escorts and immense shields for protection. It carried vulture droids and tanks, deploying them rapidly to planetary surfaces. These ships were symbols of economic and mechanical dominance, used more to control and intimidate than inspire. Their weakness was their centralized system—if the hub failed, the army failed. As symbols of the Separatist movement, they represented the cold precision of droid-led warfare and the perils of centralized automation.'),
	(39,'Naboo fighter','N-1 starfighter','Starfighter','Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps','200000','11','1','0','1100','1.0','unknown','65','7 days','2014-12-19T17:39:17.582000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.917000Z','/images/starships/39-naboo-fighter.png','The Naboo fighter was a sleek, yellow starfighter used by the Royal Naboo Security Forces. It combined aesthetics with performance. These nimble ships defended Naboo against the Trade Federation. Young Anakin flew one in battle during the invasion. Their elegant design hid powerful systems. Naboo fighters represent peace, beauty, and unexpected courage.','The N-1 Starfighter, more commonly known as the Naboo fighter, was a single-pilot craft developed by Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps for the defense of the peaceful planet Naboo. Characterized by its elegant yellow finish and long, chrome tail, the N-1 was a blend of art and engineering. While designed primarily for escort and patrol missions, it was equipped with twin laser cannons and proton torpedo launchers. During the Battle of Naboo, young Anakin Skywalker accidentally piloted one of these fighters into the Droid Control Ship, playing a decisive role in the battle’s outcome. Naboo’s commitment to aesthetics was present in the fighter’s smooth lines and polished look. Its engines offered impressive agility and speed, allowing it to perform in atmospheric and space combat. Although not a war machine by design, it was more than capable when called upon. The fighter included advanced navigation and communication systems for royal escort duties. Naboo pilots were known for their skill and poise, reflecting the planet’s values. The N-1 served not just as a defender but as a symbol of how beauty and strength could coexist.'),
	(40,'Naboo Royal Starship','J-type 327 Nubian royal starship','yacht','Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps, Nubia Star Drives','unknown','76','8','unknown','920','1.8','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-19T17:45:03.506000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.919000Z','/images/starships/40-naboo-royal-starship.png','The Naboo Royal Starship was a silver, elegant vessel used by Queen Amidala. Crafted for diplomacy and speed, it had no weapons. The ship fled Naboo and traveled to Tatooine and Coruscant. Its reflective hull and sleek design made it iconic. It embodied Naboo’s values of peace and refinement. The ship represents diplomacy, grace, and leadership.','The Naboo Royal Starship, also known as the J-type 327 Nubian, was the official vessel of Queen Padmé Amidala and the Naboo monarchy. Built by Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps, it featured a chrome finish and smooth, art-deco lines. It was unarmed, emphasizing its peaceful purpose. Despite lacking weapons, it had strong shields, advanced navigation, and speed, enabling it to escape dangerous situations. During the invasion of Naboo, it was used to flee the planet and carry Amidala to Tatooine and then Coruscant. The ship relied on an astromech team, including R2-D2, for repairs during battle damage. The Royal Starship symbolized diplomacy, culture, and unity. Its interior was luxurious yet functional, providing space for royal chambers and advisors. It reflected Naboo’s belief in elegance over aggression. Though peaceful, the ship was a vessel of action in critical moments. It served not just a monarch, but a cause. The silver hull became synonymous with the early efforts to restore peace to the Republic. The ship’s story is one of grace under pressure.'),
	(41,'Scimitar','Star Courier','Space Transport','Republic Sienar Systems','55000000','26.5','1','6','1180','1.5','unknown','2500000','30 days','2014-12-20T09:39:56.116000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.922000Z','/images/starships/41-scimitar.png','The Scimitar was Darth Maul’s personal stealth starship. Sleek and ominous, it featured a cloaking device and tracking systems. Built for infiltration and assassination, it carried Maul to Tatooine. It was a deadly shadow in space. Its design reflected the menace of the Sith. The Scimitar represents secrecy, threat, and lethal intent.','The Scimitar, officially named the Sith Infiltrator, was a heavily modified starship used by Darth Maul under orders from Darth Sidious. It was equipped with a rare stygium cloaking device, allowing it to become invisible to sensors and visual tracking. Sleek, blade-like, and silent, the ship embodied Sith design—functionally deadly and visually intimidating. The Scimitar carried Maul across the galaxy, including missions to Tatooine and Naboo. It was equipped with probe droids, encrypted communication, and advanced stealth technologies. Though lightly armed, it relied on surprise and speed. The ship featured a deployable speeder bike, which Maul used to close in on targets. The interior was stark and dark, matching its user’s grim purpose. The Scimitar\'s cloaking abilities made it ideal for espionage and covert assassination. It rarely entered open combat, instead functioning in the shadows. The ship marked a shift in Sith tactics—subtle, precise, and overwhelming when revealed. Its presence often preceded violence. The Scimitar remains one of the most enigmatic and dangerous craft of its era. It reflects the cold efficiency of Darth Maul and the resurgence of the Sith threat.'),
	(43,'J-type diplomatic barge','J-type diplomatic barge','Diplomatic barge','Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps, Nubia Star Drives','2000000','39','5','10','2000','0.7','unknown','unknown','1 year','2014-12-20T11:05:51.237000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.925000Z','/images/starships/43-j-type-diplomatic-barge.png','The J-type diplomatic barge was a sleek and silver starship used by Naboo royalty. Built for official galactic travel, it carried Queen Amidala on missions of diplomacy. Its shimmering surface reflected Naboo’s elegance. Though lightly armed, it relied on escort fighters. The barge symbolized neutrality and prestige. It represents peace, beauty, and political presence.','The J-type diplomatic barge was designed by the Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps for the royal house of Naboo. Intended for peaceful missions and state visits, it featured a flowing silver hull and minimalist aesthetic. Its luxurious interior accommodated royal delegations, diplomats, and staff, emphasizing grace and ceremony over aggression. During the Clone Wars era, the diplomatic barge carried Queen Amidala and other senators on missions to Coruscant and other galactic centers. Though mostly unarmed, it had minor shielding and was usually accompanied by armed escort fighters for protection. The ship was powered by twin Nubian drives and included advanced communication systems. Its design mirrored Naboo’s values of refinement, diplomacy, and nonviolence. With its elongated nose and broad body, it cut a striking figure in space. Its peaceful appearance belied its crucial political function, enabling quiet negotiations and interplanetary travel for officials. The barge remains a lasting image of the Republic’s fading elegance in the twilight before war. It embodied how form and purpose could align in the pursuit of peace.'),
	(47,'AA-9 Coruscant freighter','Botajef AA-9 Freighter-Liner','freighter','Botajef Shipyards','unknown','390','unknown','30000','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T17:24:23.509000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.928000Z','/images/starships/47-aa-9-coruscant-freighter.png','The AA-9 Coruscant freighter was a massive civilian transport vessel. Commonly used for moving people and cargo across the galaxy, it had minimal defenses. Padmé Amidala traveled on one in disguise. Its bulky frame concealed hidden journeys. The AA-9 represents anonymity, everyday travel, and humble rebellion.','The AA-9 Coruscant freighter was a large, utilitarian starship built for transporting cargo and passengers across the galaxy. With its elongated shape and tiered body, it was commonly seen in and around the urban sprawl of Coruscant. Built for efficiency, it had limited shielding and no weapons, relying on crowded space lanes and the Republic’s general security for protection. One of the most notable uses of an AA-9 was when Padmé Amidala disguised herself as a refugee to escape Coruscant with Anakin Skywalker. The ship served as a backdrop for pivotal personal and political developments in the Star Wars saga. Despite its plain appearance, the freighter was capable of hyperspace travel and could carry thousands of passengers or tons of goods. It featured rudimentary sleeping quarters and communal spaces. It was a ship of the people, ordinary in every way but vital to the functioning of galactic society. The AA-9 symbolizes movement in secrecy, hidden agendas, and the quiet motion of destiny among the stars.'),
	(48,'Jedi starfighter','Delta-7 Aethersprite-class interceptor','Starfighter','Kuat Systems Engineering','180000','8','1','0','1150','1.0','unknown','60','7 days','2014-12-20T17:35:23.906000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.930000Z','/images/starships/48-jedi-starfighter.png','The Jedi starfighter was the personal spacecraft used by Jedi Knights during the Clone Wars. Sleek and sharp, it lacked hyperdrive, relying on ring transports. Obi-Wan Kenobi famously piloted one to Kamino. Agile but vulnerable, it reflected the Jedi’s minimalist style. The starfighter symbolizes duty, swiftness, and individual heroism.','The Delta-7 Aethersprite-class light interceptor, commonly known as the Jedi starfighter, was designed for use by Jedi during the final years of the Galactic Republic. Compact and precise, it was lightly armed but incredibly fast and maneuverable, matching the Jedi’s reflexes and combat style. Unlike most ships, it had no built-in hyperdrive and instead docked into an external hyperdrive ring. Obi-Wan Kenobi piloted one to Kamino and Geonosis during the events leading up to the Clone Wars. The cockpit was cramped, with space for a single pilot and an astromech droid socket. Its triangular profile made it distinct and efficient for aerial acrobatics and space pursuit. Jedi starfighters were symbols of the Jedi Order’s lone, precise interventions. While elegant, they also signaled the Republic’s growing militarization. The ship’s design reflected the Jedi’s austere lifestyle and their emphasis on agility and awareness. These starfighters were eventually modified into more militarized variants as the war escalated. Yet, the original Delta-7 remains iconic as a Jedi vessel—focused, restrained, and swift.'),
	(49,'H-type Nubian yacht','H-type Nubian yacht','yacht','Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps','unknown','47.9','4','unknown','8000','0.9','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T17:46:46.847000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.932000Z','/images/starships/49-h-type-nubian-yacht.png','The H-type Nubian yacht was a royal cruiser used by Padmé Amidala. Sleek and luxurious, it combined Naboo elegance with speed. The ship carried her to Mustafar during a tragic turning point. Its chrome design reflected high culture and status. The yacht stands for beauty, sorrow, and devotion. It represents grace in moments of despair.','The H-type Nubian yacht was a personal transport vessel of Naboo design, known for its refined curves and silver chrome plating. Crafted by the Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps, it was smaller than other royal ships but highly advanced. It carried Queen Amidala and later Senator Padmé Amidala on important personal missions. One of its most notable journeys was to Mustafar, where Padmé confronted Anakin Skywalker after his turn to the dark side. The ship was equipped with advanced sensors, navigation, and a modest defense system, though it was not built for combat. Its smooth surface and flowing lines epitomized Naboo’s preference for form and beauty over aggression. The yacht provided comfort and autonomy for high-ranking passengers. It moved through space like a whisper, emphasizing quiet purpose and sovereign grace. Despite its luxury, it was witness to heartbreak and betrayal. The ship became a vehicle for tragic confrontation, carrying love and loss through the stars. It embodies both elegance and sorrow, and remains a symbol of doomed peace and personal courage.'),
	(52,'Republic Assault ship','Acclamator I-class assault ship','assault ship','Rothana Heavy Engineering','unknown','752','700','16000','unknown','0.6','unknown','11250000','2 years','2014-12-20T18:08:42.926000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.935000Z','/images/starships/52-republic-assault-ship.png','The Republic Assault Ship was a massive warship used during the Clone Wars. Built for planetary invasions, it deployed thousands of clones and walkers. These ships signaled the Republic’s transformation into a military force. They were seen over Geonosis and beyond. They reflect militarization, scale, and organized might.','Known officially as the Acclamator-class assault ship, this vessel was the Republic’s primary transport and landing ship at the onset of the Clone Wars. With the capacity to carry up to 16,000 clone troopers, dozens of walkers, and support vehicles, it served as the backbone of the Grand Army of the Republic. The Acclamator was first deployed during the Battle of Geonosis, marking the Republic’s entry into all-out war. The ship’s massive hangar bays could release waves of forces onto planetary surfaces, supported by heavy turbolasers and shields. Though originally designed as a troop ship, it doubled as a space combat vessel when needed. Its introduction represented the rapid militarization of the Republic under Chancellor Palpatine’s emergency powers. These ships were not elegant or subtle, but practical and overwhelming. They became symbols of the Jedi’s transition from peacekeepers to generals. Despite their effectiveness, they also foreshadowed the rise of the Empire. The Republic Assault Ship was the harbinger of galactic change—efficient, powerful, and deeply political.'),
	(58,'Solar Sailer','Punworcca 116-class interstellar sloop','yacht','Huppla Pasa Tisc Shipwrights Collective','35700','15.2','3','11','1600','1.5','unknown','240','7 days','2014-12-20T18:37:56.969000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.937000Z','/images/starships/58-solar-sailer.png','The Solar Sailer was Count Dooku’s personal transport. With a large energy sail, it glided through hyperspace in eerie silence. The ship was elegant and minimalistic, echoing Separatist secrecy. Dooku used it for stealth and personal missions. It reflected his calm, sinister authority. The Sailer stands for finesse, mystery, and hidden danger.','The Punworcca 116-class interstellar sloop, more commonly known as the Solar Sailer, was an exotic starship employed by Count Dooku during the early years of the Clone Wars. Its most striking feature was a large, semi-transparent energy sail that allowed it to travel silently through hyperspace. Built by the Geonosians, the craft was sleek and lightweight, prioritizing elegance and stealth over firepower. Dooku used the ship to travel between covert locations and meetings with his master, Darth Sidious. The ship’s design reflected Dooku’s refined taste and noble heritage while also serving his dark objectives. Its energy sail was unique, making it stand out in contrast to typical Separatist machinery. The interior was sparse and meditative, much like Dooku himself. It had no weapons but relied on secrecy and speed. The Solar Sailer was an ideal ship for dark dealings and hidden movements, bridging the gap between aristocracy and treachery. It became a flying symbol of Dooku’s dual identity—public noble, secret Sith.'),
	(59,'Trade Federation cruiser','Providence-class carrier/destroyer','capital ship','Rendili StarDrive, Free Dac Volunteers Engineering corps.','125000000','1088','600','48247','1050','1.5','unknown','50000000','4 years','2014-12-20T19:40:21.902000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.941000Z','/images/starships/59-trade-federation-cruiser.png','The Trade Federation cruiser was a modified Lucrehulk-class battleship. Originally cargo haulers, they were converted into command ships. These massive rings encircled a central sphere. They controlled vast droid armies. One such ship was the Droid Control Ship over Naboo. They represent commerce, dominance, and mechanized rule.','The Lucrehulk-class core ship, often referred to as the Trade Federation cruiser, was an enormous vessel originally designed for commercial cargo but later militarized. Its design consisted of a giant ring with a detachable central core, allowing modular functions. The Trade Federation repurposed these ships to act as command centers for droid armies and planetary invasions. With immense hangar bays, they could carry thousands of droids, tanks, and vulture starfighters. During the invasion of Naboo, one such ship served as the Droid Control Ship destroyed by Anakin Skywalker. The ship’s scale and functionality made it a symbol of the Federation’s blend of economic power and militarized bureaucracy. Despite their sluggish speed, they were heavily shielded and well-defended. The cruiser’s imposing shape and function reflected the growing threat of corporate influence in galactic affairs. These vessels signified the Republic’s declining control over commerce and conflict. The Trade Federation cruiser stands as an icon of strategic might wrapped in greed and mechanization.'),
	(61,'Theta-class T-2c shuttle','Theta-class T-2c shuttle','transport','Cygnus Spaceworks','1000000','18.5','5','16','2000','1.0','unknown','50000','56 days','2014-12-20T19:48:40.409000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.944000Z','/images/starships/61-theta-class-t-2c-shuttle.png','The Theta-class T-2c shuttle was used during the final days of the Republic. It served as a high-ranking transport vehicle, often seen carrying Darth Sidious. The ship had an elegant, folding wing design and advanced shielding. Its usage marked the shift from Republic elegance to Imperial function. It appeared during crucial turning points in the Clone Wars. The shuttle symbolizes transition and the rise of the Empire.','The Theta-class T-2c shuttle was a sleek and sophisticated transport used primarily during the final days of the Galactic Republic. Its most notable passenger was Chancellor Palpatine, later revealed as Darth Sidious, who used the shuttle to return from critical missions. It featured vertical folding wings, an aerodynamic frame, and enhanced shielding systems for protection. The shuttle combined elegance with efficiency, suitable for VIP missions and medical transport. After the Battle of Coruscant, the Theta-class famously delivered the severely injured Anakin Skywalker to receive cybernetic enhancements, transforming him into Darth Vader. The ship\'s sleek appearance masked the darkness of its purpose. Its association with the rise of the Sith made it an enduring symbol of transformation and loss. Though not produced in large quantities, the Theta-class influenced future Imperial designs. Its black and red interior reflected the sinister undertone of its users. It was fast, secure, and respected by Republic and Separatist forces alike. The shuttle carried key figures in their moments of transition, from Jedi to Sith, Republic to Empire. It reflected a galaxy in flux. With time, it became a rare sight, overshadowed by more militarized ships. However, its legacy endures in holorecords and tales of power lost and gained. The Theta-class was more than a transport—it was a harbinger of change.'),
	(63,'Republic attack cruiser','Senator-class Star Destroyer','star destroyer','Kuat Drive Yards, Allanteen Six shipyards','59000000','1137','7400','2000','975','1.0','unknown','20000000','2 years','2014-12-20T19:52:56.232000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.946000Z','/images/starships/63-republic-attack-cruiser.png','The Republic attack cruiser was the primary battleship of the Clone Wars. It carried troops, starfighters, and supplies into battle zones. Commanded by Jedi generals, it served as a mobile base for the Republic. Its red and white hull became iconic across warfronts. These cruisers laid the groundwork for future Star Destroyers. They represent the might of the Republic’s military machine.','The Republic attack cruiser, also known as the Venator-class Star Destroyer, was a capital ship used extensively during the Clone Wars. Built by Kuat Drive Yards, the cruiser served as the backbone of the Galactic Republic’s fleet. It was designed to transport clone troopers, AT-TE walkers, and starfighters, including the V-wing and ARC-170. Each ship was often commanded by a Jedi General and a clone captain, forming the nerve centers of Republic campaigns. The red stripes and imposing silhouette of the ship made it instantly recognizable across the galaxy. The Venator-class could operate in both atmospheric and space-based combat, allowing it to perform planetary invasions. Its hangar bay doors opened along the dorsal spine, allowing fast deployment of fighters. These cruisers participated in nearly every major battle of the Clone Wars. Their design later inspired the Imperial Star Destroyers that dominated the galaxy under the Empire. The ships marked a time of unity and war, before the Jedi Purge. Many were repurposed or destroyed after Order 66. The Republic attack cruiser represents both the heroism of the Clone Wars and the fall that followed. It remains a symbol of strength and transition.'),
	(64,'Naboo star skiff','J-type star skiff','yacht','Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps/Nubia Star Drives, Incorporated','unknown','29.2','3','3','1050','0.5','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T19:55:15.396000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.948000Z','/images/starships/64-naboo-star-skiff.png','The Naboo star skiff was a sleek and elegant transport ship. It was used by Padmé Amidala during the Clone Wars. With a thin frame and reflective hull, it was built for diplomacy and speed. The star skiff symbolized the style and grace of Naboo. It was later used in Padmé’s final mission to Mustafar. The ship embodies elegance in a time of war.','The Naboo star skiff, also known as the J-type star skiff, was a personal transport vessel from the peaceful planet of Naboo. Built by Theed Palace Space Vessel Engineering Corps, it combined function and luxury. The ship featured a long, narrow profile with retractable wings and polished chrome plating. Unlike most military ships of the era, the skiff had no weapons, prioritizing speed and stealth instead. Senator Padmé Amidala used this ship to travel across the galaxy during critical missions. Most notably, she used it to visit Anakin Skywalker on Mustafar before the fall of the Republic. The ship’s light frame allowed it to navigate tight landing zones and evade detection. It housed limited crew but offered high comfort for its passengers. The star skiff marked the transition of Naboo vessels toward more practical wartime applications. Though small, it played a role in moments of great personal and galactic consequence. Its final mission marked the end of Padmé’s journey and the beginning of the Empire. Today, the Naboo star skiff is remembered as a piece of beautiful design, tragic memory, and noble intent.'),
	(65,'Jedi Interceptor','Eta-2 Actis-class light interceptor','starfighter','Kuat Systems Engineering','320000','5.47','1','0','1500','1.0','unknown','60','2 days','2014-12-20T19:56:57.468000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.951000Z','/images/starships/65-jedi-interceptor.png','The Jedi Interceptor was a fast and nimble starfighter. It was used by Jedi Knights during the Clone Wars. With s-foils and advanced agility, it offered superior space maneuvering. Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi piloted these ships in major battles. The ship bridged the era between Jedi and Empire. It represents precision, speed, and shifting tides.','The Jedi Interceptor, formally known as the Eta-2 Actis-class light interceptor, was a compact and highly maneuverable starfighter used near the end of the Clone Wars. Developed as an evolution of the Jedi starfighter, it was faster and more combat-ready. The ship featured folding s-foils and wingtip laser cannons. It lacked hyperdrives, relying on docking with hyperspace rings. Jedi pilots, including Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi, used these ships in battles such as Coruscant and Utapau. Its cockpit was designed for Jedi reflexes, demanding acute awareness and control. R2 units often accompanied the pilot, enhancing navigation and repairs. The Interceptor could evade tight enemy formations and execute complex maneuvers. It was a favorite among elite Jedi for its responsiveness. The ship was a direct precursor to TIE fighter design, showing the Empire’s adaptation of Jedi-era tech. After Order 66, few remained, as Jedi were purged and their ships destroyed. The Jedi Interceptor is remembered as a vessel of both glory and doom. It soared through the final victories and final defeats of the Jedi Order. Sleek and deadly, it defined the twilight of the Republic’s protectors.'),
	(66,'arc-170','Aggressive Reconnaissance-170 starfighte','starfighter','Incom Corporation, Subpro Corporation','155000','14.5','3','0','1000','1.0','100','110','5 days','2014-12-20T20:03:48.603000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.953000Z','/images/starships/66-arc-170.png','The ARC-170 was a heavy starfighter used during the Clone Wars. Piloted by clones, it carried three crew members and an astromech. It was durable, long-range, and capable of hyperspace travel. The ship played a major role in the Republic’s space battles. Its wings inspired the later X-wing design. The ARC-170 represents unity, strength, and sacrifice.','The Aggressive Reconnaissance-170 starfighter, or ARC-170, was a long-range combat ship used by the Republic during the Clone Wars. Developed by Incom and Subpro, it was flown by elite clone trooper pilots. The ship featured s-foils, heavy blasters, and rear-facing gunners for full coverage. With a crew of three and an astromech droid, it balanced power and coordination. ARC-170s participated in major space battles like Coruscant and Kashyyyk. Their rugged design made them suitable for deep-space patrol and escort missions. Jedi often flew alongside ARC squadrons in coordinated strikes. The ship’s profile and function later inspired the iconic X-wing design of the Rebel Alliance. Pilots who manned ARC-170s were respected for their skill and bravery. During Order 66, ARC ships turned on Jedi targets in tragic betrayals. Despite that, the ship is remembered for its role in noble missions and brotherhood among clones. Its legacy spans both honor and heartbreak. The ARC-170 remains a testament to the valor of the Grand Army of the Republic.'),
	(68,'Banking clan frigte','Munificent-class star frigate','cruiser','Hoersch-Kessel Drive, Inc, Gwori Revolutionary Industries','57000000','825','200','unknown','unknown','1.0','unknown','40000000','2 years','2014-12-20T20:07:11.538000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.956000Z','/images/starships/68-banking-clan-frigte.png','The Banking Clan frigate was used by the Separatists during the Clone Wars. It served as a support ship and heavy cruiser. Designed by the InterGalactic Banking Clan, it combined firepower with defense. These frigates often escorted larger capital ships. The design was modular and adaptable. The ship represents economic power turned militarized.','The Banking Clan frigate, officially known as the Munificent-class star frigate, was a long, narrow warship used by the Confederacy of Independent Systems. Developed by the InterGalactic Banking Clan, it combined financial interests with heavy firepower. It measured over 800 meters and featured powerful turbolasers and communication arrays. The ship’s role was to disrupt Republic fleets and protect Separatist command ships. It was often deployed in groups, providing support to droid fighters and bombers. The vessel\'s slender frame made it harder to target, but it lacked the durability of larger warships. The design reflected the dual nature of the Banking Clan—corporate neutrality paired with military aggression. These ships were crewed mostly by droids and AI systems. Though not as iconic as battleships, they played vital roles in blockades and siege warfare. Many were destroyed or repurposed after the war. The Munificent-class frigate shows how economic entities shaped the Clone Wars. It was a weapon of commerce and conflict, serving the ambitions of the Separatists and the hidden plans of Darth Sidious.'),
	(74,'Belbullab-22 starfighter','Belbullab-22 starfighter','starfighter','Feethan Ottraw Scalable Assemblies','168000','6.71','1','0','1100','6','unknown','140','7 days','2014-12-20T20:38:05.031000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.959000Z','/images/starships/74-belbullab-22-starfighter.png','The Belbullab-22 was a compact, deadly starfighter used by Separatists. General Grievous piloted this model during key missions. It featured heavy armament and superior speed. The ship had sharp, aggressive lines and twin engines. Its design reflected Grievous’s brutal efficiency. The Belbullab-22 symbolizes calculated aggression and command.','The Belbullab-22 starfighter was a high-performance combat ship used by the Confederacy of Independent Systems. Produced by Feethan Ottraw Scalable Assemblies, it was primarily flown by General Grievous. The fighter was sleek and compact, with twin ion engines and a powerful front-facing arsenal. Its frame allowed quick acceleration and evasive maneuvers, making it suitable for elite droid pilots or exceptional organic ones. Unlike droid-only fighters, it was manually piloted, reflecting its strategic importance. Grievous used it to escape after the Battle of Coruscant, highlighting its reliability. The fighter had a closed cockpit, hyperdrive, and independent targeting systems. It was rarely seen in large numbers but feared when it appeared. The Belbullab-22 was symbolic of Separatist leadership—deadly, precise, and unrelenting. Its design influenced later starfighter models. Though mostly retired after the Clone Wars, it remained a mark of Grievous’s presence. Its name and silhouette inspire tales of elite Separatist victories. The ship was not just fast—it was ruthless.'),
	(75,'V-wing','Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter','starfighter','Kuat Systems Engineering','102500','7.9','1','0','1050','1.0','unknown','60','15 hours','2014-12-20T20:43:04.349000Z','2014-12-20T21:23:49.961000Z','/images/starships/75-v-wing.png','The V-wing starfighter marked the transition from Republic to Empire. It was used during the final battles of the Clone Wars. Fast and compact, it resembled early TIE fighter prototypes. The V-wing had foldable wings and twin ion engines. It symbolized the fall of the Jedi and rise of the Empire. The ship represents change and continuity in design.','The Alpha-3 Nimbus-class V-wing starfighter was a short-range, fast-response combat ship used by the Galactic Republic. Developed by Kuat Systems Engineering, it saw heavy use during the final days of the Clone Wars. Its distinctive folding wings and high-speed ion engines made it ideal for pursuit missions. The V-wing lacked a hyperdrive, requiring carrier deployment. It was flown primarily by clone pilots in planetary defense and escort missions. Its cockpit and control layout closely resembled the designs later seen in TIE fighters. After the rise of the Galactic Empire, many V-wings were transitioned into Imperial service. Their sound, performance, and aesthetics became blueprints for the next generation of Imperial craft. The V-wing symbolized the transition from Republic freedom to Imperial control. It represented the evolution of war technology and military philosophy. Fast, fierce, and stripped of unnecessary components, the V-wing foretold the era to come. Though overshadowed by later ships, it played a vital role in securing early Imperial dominance.');
