INSERT INTO `vehicles` (`id`, `name`, `model`, `vehicle_class`, `manufacturer`, `length`, `cost_in_credits`, `crew`, `passengers`, `max_atmosphering_speed`, `cargo_capacity`, `consumables`, `created`, `edited`, `image_url`, `short_description`, `long_description`)
VALUES
	(4,'Sand Crawler','Digger Crawler','wheeled','Corellia Mining Corporation','36.8 ','150000','46','30','30','50000','2 months','2014-12-10T15:36:25.724000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.661000Z','/images/vehicles/4-sand-crawler.png','The Sand Crawler is a massive, treaded transport used by Jawas. It roams the deserts of Tatooine in search of scrap and salvage. With its towering structure and rusted hull, it is both iconic and mysterious. Inside, Jawas live and trade droids and machinery. These vehicles are remnants of a forgotten industrial age. The Sand Crawler symbolizes scavenging survival and hidden opportunity.','The Sand Crawler is a colossal, slow-moving vehicle used primarily by the Jawas of Tatooine. Originally mining transports left behind by offworld corporations, they were repurposed into mobile homes and workshops. Constructed with thick armor plating and supported by massive treads, they can traverse the planet’s harsh desert terrain. The interior of a Sand Crawler includes storage for droids, scrap parts, and living quarters for entire Jawa clans. With a large frontal ramp, Jawas can load newly acquired salvage or display items for trade. Their presence is often preceded by the shrill chatter of Jawas negotiating sales. These vehicles serve as roaming marketplaces and homes, representing the Jawa way of life. Sand Crawlers are relics of a time before Tatooine’s isolation. Now, they move slowly through endless dunes, each one a creaking monument to the past. Despite their size, they are rarely attacked due to their non-aggressive nature. They’ve become a cultural symbol, appearing in many stories of Tatooine’s inhabitants. From Luke Skywalker’s first encounters with droids to Rebel reconnaissance, the Sand Crawler leaves its mark. It stands as a fusion of utility, heritage, and resilience in the unforgiving sands.'),
	(6,'T-16 skyhopper','T-16 skyhopper','repulsorcraft','Incom Corporation','10.4 ','14500','1','1','1200','50','0','2014-12-10T16:01:52.434000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.665000Z','/images/vehicles/6-t-16-skyhopper.png','The T-16 Skyhopper is a nimble repulsorlift vehicle used for atmospheric flight. It’s commonly seen on Tatooine and owned by moisture farmers. Luke Skywalker used one in his youth, practicing flying and targeting womp rats. Its design foreshadowed his later skills as a pilot. The Skyhopper represents dreams of escape and a pilot’s journey. It is a training ground for future heroes.','The T-16 Skyhopper is a civilian atmospheric craft favored by young adventurers and rural settlers, particularly on desert planets like Tatooine. It features a sleek body, vertical stabilizer, and dual control surfaces for tight maneuvering. Capable of high-speed travel and aerobatics, the T-16 is often used for recreation and training. Luke Skywalker famously used his T-16 to fly through Beggar’s Canyon and target womp rats, developing skills that would later help him pilot an X-wing. Its targeting system and flight controls mimic those of military fighters, making it an ideal trainer. The craft is often stored in simple garages and used to travel between distant homesteads. It became symbolic of youthful ambition and a yearning for more beyond the homestead. Though not weaponized, it provides a stepping stone toward piloting combat starfighters. In the lore of the Rebellion, many skilled pilots credit their early Skyhopper experience. Sleek and agile, the T-16 embodies the restless spirit of young rebels across the galaxy. It connects dreams to destiny through dust, wind, and flight.'),
	(7,'X-34 landspeeder','X-34 landspeeder','repulsorcraft','SoroSuub Corporation','3.4 ','10550','1','1','250','5','unknown','2014-12-10T16:13:52.586000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.668000Z','/images/vehicles/7-x-34-landspeeder.webp','The X-34 landspeeder is a civilian hover vehicle used for ground travel. It was popular on arid planets like Tatooine. Luke Skywalker used one for transportation and errands. It glides smoothly over terrain using repulsorlift technology. Often dusty and battered, it reflects life in the Outer Rim. The X-34 symbolizes modest freedom and daily survival.','The X-34 landspeeder is a common civilian vehicle designed for short-range travel on dry, rugged worlds. Powered by repulsorlift engines, it hovers just above the ground and reaches moderate speeds. Its open cockpit, weathered finish, and utilitarian frame make it ideal for the rough life of Tatooine settlers. Luke Skywalker used an X-34 for transportation across the desert, traveling from his uncle’s moisture farm to Tosche Station and beyond. With no weapons or armor, it served only for transit and exploration. These landspeeders often showed signs of heavy wear, patched parts, and improvisational maintenance. Despite its simplicity, the vehicle played a central role in Luke’s early journey, including his meeting with Obi-Wan Kenobi and sale of R2-D2 and C-3PO. The landspeeder reflects the harsh, practical reality of Outer Rim life. It’s a tool of necessity, not luxury. Yet, within its rusted hull and humming engine lies the spirit of movement, curiosity, and quiet independence. It remains one of the most iconic civilian vehicles in the Star Wars universe.'),
	(8,'TIE/LN starfighter','Twin Ion Engine/Ln Starfighter','starfighter','Sienar Fleet Systems','6.4','unknown','1','0','1200','65','2 days','2014-12-10T16:33:52.860000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.670000Z','/images/vehicles/8-tie-ln-starfighter.png','The TIE/LN starfighter is the backbone of the Imperial fleet. Fast, agile, and mass-produced, it lacks shields and hyperdrives. Its twin ion engines emit a distinctive scream in flight. Pilots are trained for loyalty over survival. TIEs represent the ruthless efficiency of the Empire. They are symbols of fear, speed, and obedience.','The TIE/LN starfighter, commonly known as the standard TIE fighter, is the most recognizable vessel of the Galactic Empire. Developed by Sienar Fleet Systems, it features twin ion engines and a spherical cockpit flanked by solar array panels. It lacks deflector shields and hyperdrives, emphasizing speed, quantity, and expendability. Pilots are trained under strict Imperial doctrine and regarded as assets to be replaced. The TIE fighter’s iconic screeching engine has become synonymous with approaching Imperial might. These ships serve as patrol, escort, and assault units in nearly every space battle. Their rapid deployment capabilities make them ideal for swarming enemies. The design reflects the Empire’s philosophy: functional, menacing, and cost-effective. Despite their weaknesses, TIEs overwhelmed enemies through sheer numbers. Pilots flew with honor or fear, knowing escape was rarely an option. The TIE/LN starfighter embodies control through power and uniformity. Its silhouette, sound, and tactics define the Empire’s aerial dominance. It remains a symbol of totalitarian strength.'),
	(14,'Snowspeeder','t-47 airspeeder','airspeeder','Incom corporation','4.5','unknown','2','0','650','10','none','2014-12-15T12:22:12Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.672000Z','/images/vehicles/14-snowspeeder.webp','The Snowspeeder is a modified airspeeder used by the Rebel Alliance. Adapted for cold environments like Hoth, it played a key role in the Battle of Hoth. It features tow cables, blasters, and open cockpits. Pilots fly low and fast to avoid detection. It became iconic for its role in toppling AT-ATs. The Snowspeeder symbolizes resilience and ingenuity.','The T-47 Snowspeeder is a lightly armed, high-speed airspeeder originally used for cargo towing. Rebel engineers modified the design for combat during the Galactic Civil War. On Hoth, these vehicles were outfitted with laser cannons and harpoon tow cables to fight the Empire’s walkers. Two crew members—a pilot and a gunner—sit in tandem within an open canopy. Their strategy involves low-altitude flight to exploit terrain and AT-AT blind spots. In the iconic Battle of Hoth, Snowspeeders performed daring maneuvers, entangling walkers and slowing the Imperial advance. The ship’s simplicity and adaptability made it vital for Rebel tactics. Though vulnerable to enemy fire, they exemplified the Rebellion’s courage. Their nimbleness contrasted with the Empire’s heavy machinery. Snowspeeders have become a cultural image of rebellion and clever resistance. Despite limited shielding and range, they represent grit and resourcefulness. The Snowspeeder is proof that speed and strategy can challenge even the mightiest of machines.'),
	(16,'TIE bomber','TIE/sa bomber','space/planetary bomber','Sienar Fleet Systems','7.8','unknown','1','0','850','none','2 days','2014-12-15T12:33:15.838000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.675000Z','/images/vehicles/16-tie-bomber.png','The TIE bomber is a heavy assault craft used by the Galactic Empire. It features twin hulls and carries a variety of ordnance. Slower than standard TIEs, it excels at destroying ground targets and capital ships. Its design prioritizes firepower over agility. The TIE bomber reflects the Empire’s destructive capability. It is a symbol of targeted force and terror.','The TIE/sa bomber is a dual-hull starfighter designed by Sienar Fleet Systems for heavy payload delivery. One hull contains the cockpit, while the other holds bombs, torpedoes, or mines. Unlike the nimble TIE fighter, the bomber is slower but far more devastating. It serves in both space and atmospheric operations. TIE bombers were used extensively during the Galactic Civil War to eliminate enemy bases, destroy convoys, and suppress resistance. Their bombing runs brought destruction with chilling precision. In the Battle of Hoth, they targeted Rebel positions during the Imperial assault. The design’s simplicity allows for mass production, consistent with Imperial doctrine. Its sound and shape evoke dread on battlefields. Often operating with fighter escorts, TIE bombers are vulnerable to interception but lethal when left unchecked. They show the Empire’s willingness to overwhelm rather than outmaneuver. Each bombing run reinforces the image of dominance and devastation. TIE bombers remain a feared tool in the Empire’s arsenal.'),
	(18,'AT-AT','All Terrain Armored Transport','assault walker','Kuat Drive Yards, Imperial Department of Military Research','20','unknown','5','40','60','1000','unknown','2014-12-15T12:38:25.937000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.677000Z','/images/vehicles/18-at-at.jpeg','The All Terrain Armored Transport, or AT-AT, is a massive Imperial walker. Towering over battlefields, it delivers troops and devastates targets with heavy firepower. Its armor is nearly impenetrable to small arms. AT-ATs represent Imperial intimidation and control. They were famously used on Hoth. The walker symbolizes fear, might, and authoritarian precision.','The AT-AT, or All Terrain Armored Transport, is a four-legged, heavily armored walker developed by the Galactic Empire. Standing over 20 meters tall, it was designed to dominate ground warfare through fear and sheer power. Each AT-AT carries stormtroopers, speeder bikes, and heavy artillery. Their slow but relentless pace terrifies enemies and crushes defenses. The most famous deployment occurred during the Battle of Hoth, where AT-ATs assaulted Echo Base. Rebels struggled to bring them down, resorting to harpoon cables and strategic targeting of weaker joints. Their presence in battle zones sends a message of total control. The walker’s towering profile is both symbolic and functional—visible authority and battlefield supremacy. Inside, commanders direct invasions with brutal efficiency. Though vulnerable to concentrated attacks, their psychological impact outweighs their flaws. AT-ATs are synonymous with Imperial doctrine: unyielding, methodical, and dominant. They remain one of the most recognizable weapons of oppression in the galaxy.'),
	(19,'AT-ST','All Terrain Scout Transport','walker','Kuat Drive Yards, Imperial Department of Military Research','2','unknown','2','0','90','200','none','2014-12-15T12:46:42.384000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.679000Z','/images/vehicles/19-at-st.png','The AT-ST is a bipedal scout walker used by the Empire. Smaller and faster than the AT-AT, it serves in reconnaissance and support roles. It is armed with blasters and grenade launchers. Despite its size, it is formidable in battle. It was seen in action during the Battle of Endor. The AT-ST represents mobility and tactical presence.','The All Terrain Scout Transport, or AT-ST, is a two-legged walker built by the Galactic Empire for reconnaissance, flanking, and close support. Standing at approximately 8.6 meters tall, it carries a pilot and gunner in a heavily armored cockpit. The AT-ST is equipped with blaster cannons, grenade launchers, and moderate armor plating. Its agility allows it to maneuver through forests, cityscapes, and battle zones. The walker was notably deployed during the Battle of Endor, where it supported AT-ATs and fought against Ewok resistance. Despite being top-heavy and vulnerable to terrain traps, its firepower gave it a major advantage over infantry. AT-STs are commonly used to patrol occupied worlds and enforce Imperial presence. They offer quick deployment and psychological deterrence. In the Empire\'s arsenal, they represent speed, adaptability, and authority. Their angular design and stilted walk make them instantly recognizable. Though not as indestructible as larger walkers, they embody the constant reach of Imperial enforcement.'),
	(20,'Storm IV Twin-Pod cloud car','Storm IV Twin-Pod','repulsorcraft','Bespin Motors','7','75000','2','0','1500','10','1 day','2014-12-15T12:58:50.530000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.681000Z','/images/vehicles/20-storm-iv-twin-pod-cloud-car.png','The Storm IV Twin-Pod cloud car patrols the skies of Bespin’s Cloud City. It is operated by the city’s security forces. With dual cockpits and moderate firepower, it excels at maintaining peace. These craft are agile and quick, perfect for aerial pursuit. Though not heavily armored, they are symbols of local autonomy. The cloud car represents vigilance and civic defense.','The Storm IV Twin-Pod cloud car is a lightweight patrol craft designed to secure the airspace around Cloud City on Bespin. Recognizable by its twin-pod structure—one housing the pilot, the other the gunner—it serves as a symbol of Bespin\'s order and self-regulation. The vehicle is lightly armed, making it ideal for enforcing laws and guiding incoming ships rather than engaging in heavy combat. Its sleek design allows it to weave through the floating structures of Cloud City with ease. Cloud cars are not part of the Rebel Alliance or the Empire; they serve the interests of the gas mining colony. Their orange coloration and twin engines make them distinctive in the sky. Though limited in combat application, they are crucial in identifying threats and guiding operations. The cloud car’s presence is a reminder that even neutral cities must protect themselves. It is a vehicle of balance—keeping peace without waging war. Often underestimated, these cars embody readiness and swift justice in the skies.'),
	(24,'Sail barge','Modified Luxury Sail Barge','sail barge','Ubrikkian Industries Custom Vehicle Division','30','285000','26','500','100','2000000','Live food tanks','2014-12-18T10:44:14.217000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.684000Z','/images/vehicles/24-sail-barge.webp','The Sail Barge is a luxurious but dangerous vessel used by Jabba the Hutt. It cruises the deserts of Tatooine with opulence and armed guards. Its wide decks host parties, executions, and shady dealings. The barge is fitted with blasters and carried skiffs. It reflects decadence, power, and cruelty. The sail barge symbolizes dominance and excess.','The sail barge, most famously used by Jabba the Hutt, is a massive repulsorlift vessel that glides across the dunes of Tatooine. Combining leisure and menace, the barge features grand viewing decks, banquet halls, and multiple weapons emplacements. It was used by Jabba to host lavish gatherings and transport prisoners to the Great Pit of Carkoon. Its main purpose was display—of wealth, influence, and sadistic amusement. The vessel is protected by armed guards and carried smaller skiffs for close operations. Luke Skywalker and his companions were nearly executed from the sail barge before staging a daring rescue and destroying it. Though not designed for warfare, it is a tool of intimidation and spectacle. The barge’s grandeur hides the corruption and violence beneath. It represents a mobile throne of tyranny in the wastelands. The sail barge is a haunting reminder of what unchecked power can look like in lawless corners of the galaxy.'),
	(25,'Bantha-II cargo skiff','Bantha-II','repulsorcraft cargo skiff','Ubrikkian Industries','9.5','8000','5','16','250','135000','1 day','2014-12-18T10:48:03.208000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.688000Z','/images/vehicles/25-bantha-ii-cargo-skiff.webp','The Bantha-II cargo skiff is a flat, repulsorlift platform used for hauling goods. Jabba the Hutt employed it for prisoner transport and execution. It is open-air, lightly armed, and piloted by a single operator. Skiffs are nimble but exposed. They are often seen in desert regions. The cargo skiff represents utility twisted by cruelty.','The Bantha-II cargo skiff is a versatile repulsorlift vehicle originally intended for light transport and cargo duties. Designed with a simple flat deck and minimal shielding, it operates best in low-altitude environments such as Tatooine’s deserts. While useful for trade and logistics, Jabba the Hutt famously repurposed skiffs for prisoner transfers and executions, notably during the attempted sacrifice of Luke Skywalker at the Sarlacc pit. The skiff\'s lack of enclosure makes it vulnerable but easy to board and exit. Its speed and agility made it ideal for short-range movements across rugged terrain. Piloted from a small forward console, it can carry passengers or freight with equal ease. Despite its industrial origin, it has become associated with Hutt cruelty and spectacle. The skiff serves as an example of technology repurposed for malevolent intent. It remains an iconic vehicle due to its role in one of the saga’s most famous rescues. The Bantha-II cargo skiff is a stage where destinies clash in the desert sun.'),
	(26,'TIE/IN interceptor','Twin Ion Engine Interceptor','starfighter','Sienar Fleet Systems','9.6','unknown','1','0','1250','75','2 days','2014-12-18T10:50:28.225000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.691000Z','/images/vehicles/26-tie-in-interceptor.png','The TIE Interceptor is a faster, deadlier evolution of the TIE fighter. It features sharp, angled wings and advanced weaponry. With improved agility, it challenges Rebel starfighters more effectively. Interceptors are flown by elite Imperial pilots. They lack shields, but dominate through speed. The TIE Interceptor symbolizes Imperial refinement and lethal precision.','The TIE/IN Interceptor is an advanced space superiority fighter used by the Galactic Empire. Designed to outperform Rebel starfighters like the X-wing, it boasts dagger-like solar panels for increased maneuverability and intimidating aesthetics. It is equipped with four laser cannons, mounted on the wingtips, allowing for enhanced firepower. Like other TIE models, it lacks deflector shields and hyperdrives, focusing entirely on speed and offensive capability. TIE Interceptors are flown by highly trained pilots from elite squadrons. They often accompany or replace standard TIEs in critical engagements. Their introduction marked a strategic shift in Imperial starfighter philosophy—favoring quality over sheer quantity in certain cases. The design is both feared and admired across the galaxy. Its scream echoes through battlefields as a signal of efficient destruction. The TIE Interceptor reflects the Empire’s capacity for technological evolution and brutal design. It is a razor in the void, swift and merciless.'),
	(30,'Imperial Speeder Bike','74-Z speeder bike','speeder','Aratech Repulsor Company','3','8000','1','1','360','4','1 day','2014-12-18T11:20:04.625000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.693000Z','/images/vehicles/30-imperial-speeder-bike.png','The Imperial Speeder Bike is a fast, hovering scout vehicle. Used by stormtroopers for patrols and chases, it excels in speed. Common on Endor, it weaves through forests at deadly velocities. These bikes have forward blasters and rear stabilizers. Pilots require precision to avoid crashing. The speeder bike symbolizes speed and fragility under control.','The Imperial 74-Z speeder bike is a lightweight reconnaissance and patrol vehicle used extensively by scout troopers. Designed for rapid deployment and high-speed pursuit, it can reach speeds over 500 kilometers per hour. Equipped with forward-mounted blasters, steering vanes, and repulsorlift technology, it requires skilled piloting. The speeder bike gained notoriety during the Battle of Endor, where Rebel forces and native Ewoks clashed with Imperial scouts in the dense forest. Its agility allows it to skim close to the ground, maneuvering through trees and terrain with dangerous precision. Though fast, the bike is fragile—unprotected from blaster fire or obstacles. Used for surveillance, communications relay, and battlefield flanking, it offers tactical mobility. The roar of its engine is often the last sound heard before an ambush. The speeder bike reflects the Empire’s need for speed, reach, and domination in all environments. It remains an icon of swift, deadly patrol.'),
	(33,'Vulture Droid','Vulture-class droid starfighter','starfighter','Haor Chall Engineering, Baktoid Armor Workshop','3.5','unknown','0','0','1200','0','none','2014-12-19T17:09:53.584000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.697000Z','/images/vehicles/33-vulture-droid.png','The Vulture Droid is a droid starfighter used by the Separatists. It operates without a pilot, controlled by AI or central systems. These starfighters fold into walking mode on the ground. Fast and aggressive, they swarm enemies. Vultures lack shields but overwhelm through numbers. They represent the menace of machine warfare.','The Vulture Droid, officially known as the Variable Geometry Self-Propelled Battle Droid, Mark I, is a fully automated starfighter deployed by the Separatist Alliance. It requires no organic pilot and is operated either by a central droid control ship or limited onboard AI. In space, it performs dogfighting and escort missions with agility and coordinated aggression. On the ground, it transforms into a walking mode with legs that fold from its fuselage. Vultures are armed with blaster cannons and missile launchers, though they lack shields or durability. Their strength lies in swarming formations, targeting slower and less maneuverable enemies. Used extensively in the Clone Wars, they exemplify the efficiency and horror of droid warfare. These units can be mass-produced quickly and sacrificed without consequence. The Vulture Droid reflects the impersonal and strategic brutality of the Separatist war machine. It is a symbol of the technological tide in war.'),
	(34,'Multi-Troop Transport','Multi-Troop Transport','repulsorcraft','Baktoid Armor Workshop','31','138000','4','112','35','12000','unknown','2014-12-19T17:12:04.400000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.700000Z','/images/vehicles/34-multi-troop-transport.png','The Multi-Troop Transport (MTT) is a large vehicle used by the Trade Federation. It deploys battle droids from a front rack. Its heavy armor protects cargo but limits speed. MTTs are common in large-scale invasions. They are slow but imposing. The MTT represents the mechanical might of the droid army.','The Multi-Troop Transport, or MTT, is a heavily armored ground vehicle designed by Baktoid Armor Workshop for the Trade Federation. It is used to transport and deploy B1 battle droids in massive numbers. The MTT features a front-facing deployment rack, which slides forward to release dozens of battle droids in formation. Though slow and lumbering, its thick plating offers excellent protection during land invasions. MTTs are deployed from capital ships to establish control during planetary assaults. Most notably, they were used in the invasion of Naboo. These vehicles rely on numbers and synchronization rather than agility. Piloted by OOM-series command droids, they operate as part of larger mechanized forces. The MTT showcases the scale and cold efficiency of the Separatist military. It is a moving fortress of automation and strategy. Its very presence signals the arrival of overwhelming force.'),
	(35,'Armored Assault Tank','Armoured Assault Tank','repulsorcraft','Baktoid Armor Workshop','9.75','unknown','4','6','55','unknown','unknown','2014-12-19T17:13:29.799000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.703000Z','/images/vehicles/35-armored-assault-tank.png','The AAT is a sleek, heavy tank used by the Trade Federation and later the Separatists. It features forward blasters and a rotating turret. Piloted by battle droids, it dominates ground combat. AATs are known for their curved design and powerful presence. They are reliable, deadly, and mass-produced. The tank symbolizes technological dominance and cold precision.','The Armored Assault Tank, or AAT, is a primary ground vehicle for the Trade Federation and Separatist forces. With a low-slung, aerodynamic profile and central dome turret, the AAT combines sleek aesthetics with battlefield power. It carries multiple laser cannons, including a heavy turret for long-range bombardment and side blasters for anti-infantry use. The tank is piloted by B1 battle droids and operates effectively in both urban and open environments. AATs were prominently deployed during the Battle of Naboo, laying siege to Theed and suppressing the local forces. Their efficient design allows for mass production, and their firepower makes them a match for clone armor. The AAT is the Separatists’ ground equivalent of space superiority. Its presence signals the droid army’s relentless strategy and technical confidence. Though slow compared to speeders, it balances firepower and defense effectively. The AAT is a perfect image of precision, durability, and technological warfare.'),
	(36,'Single Trooper Aerial Platform','Single Trooper Aerial Platform','repulsorcraft','Baktoid Armor Workshop','2','2500','1','0','400','none','none','2014-12-19T17:15:09.511000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.705000Z','/images/vehicles/36-single-trooper-aerial-platform.png','The Single Trooper Aerial Platform (STAP) is a fast, hovering vehicle used by battle droids. It provides quick mobility on the battlefield. STAPs are armed with twin blasters and offer high agility. Pilots stand upright and exposed while operating the craft. They are used for recon and skirmishes. The STAP represents swift but fragile firepower.','The Single Trooper Aerial Platform, commonly known as the STAP, is a lightweight repulsorlift vehicle used by the Separatist battle droid forces. Designed for speed and maneuverability, it is mounted by a single battle droid who pilots it while standing upright. The STAP is equipped with dual blaster cannons for skirmish engagements and rapid-fire strikes. Though extremely agile, it lacks armor, making it vulnerable to even light resistance fire. STAPs are often used in the early phases of a ground assault to scout enemy positions, harass infantry, or flank larger units. Their small size and high speed make them difficult targets. The vehicle saw extensive use during the Battle of Naboo and throughout the Clone Wars. Because of its simplicity, STAPs could be deployed in massive numbers and operated by droid pilots without fear of casualties. The STAP is a symbol of the efficiency and expendability of the droid army. It embodies the tactics of rapid movement and overwhelming force.'),
	(37,'C-9979 landing craft','C-9979 landing craft','landing craft','Haor Chall Engineering','210','200000','140','284','587','1800000','1 day','2014-12-19T17:20:36.373000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.707000Z','/images/vehicles/37-c-9979-landing-craft.png','The C-9979 landing craft is a massive troop carrier used by the Trade Federation. It deploys droid armies and vehicles via forward ramps. With a winged design, it lands with dominating presence. Its size allows it to carry thousands of units. The craft reflects industrial strength and cold efficiency. It symbolizes the mechanized threat of the Separatists.','The C-9979 landing craft is a large-scale transport ship developed by the Trade Federation and heavily utilized during the Clone Wars. Built to deliver droid forces and vehicles in bulk, it features forward deployment ramps and a unique winged structure. Upon landing, the ship opens its massive doors to release Multi-Troop Transports, Armored Assault Tanks, and thousands of B1 battle droids. The ship’s heavy shielding protects its cargo during descent, though it is relatively slow and requires escort in hostile space. First seen during the invasion of Naboo, the C-9979 became a symbol of the Federation’s militarized commerce. It allows for the instant deployment of a full ground assault force. Though not heavily armed itself, its purpose is to overwhelm through volume. The landing craft reflects the doctrine of numerical superiority and logistical precision. Its intimidating size and presence represent the cold, impersonal nature of the droid war machine. It remains one of the most iconic vessels of the Separatist army.'),
	(38,'Tribubble bongo','Tribubble bongo','submarine','Otoh Gunga Bongameken Cooperative','15','unknown','1','2','85','1600','unknown','2014-12-19T17:37:37.924000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.710000Z','/images/vehicles/38-tribubble-bongo.png','The Tribubble bongo is a sleek underwater transport from Naboo. Built by the Gungans, it features three large compartments. It glides silently through aquatic tunnels. Often used for escorting dignitaries, it can navigate deep oceans. The bongo blends organic design with function. It symbolizes harmony between nature and technology.','The Tribubble bongo is an aquatic transport vehicle used by the Gungan people of Naboo. Crafted from organic materials and shaped to resemble sea creatures, it consists of three rounded compartments: a central cockpit and two side chambers. Powered by bio-electric engines and equipped with repulsorlift navigation fins, the bongo is both fast and agile underwater. It is used primarily for long-distance travel between underwater cities and the planet’s surface. The vehicle was notably used to escort Qui-Gon Jinn, Obi-Wan Kenobi, and Jar Jar Binks from Otoh Gunga to Theed during the invasion of Naboo. The bongo’s construction reflects the Gungan philosophy of ecological balance and craftsmanship. Its hull is sturdy enough to withstand sea creature attacks, and it has basic lighting and controls for guidance through dark waters. The Tribubble bongo represents peaceful exploration and the Gungans’ advanced yet nature-aligned technology. It is a symbol of cooperation, adaptability, and organic engineering.'),
	(42,'Sith speeder','FC-20 speeder bike','speeder','Razalon','1.5','4000','1','0','180','2','unknown','2014-12-20T10:09:56.095000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.712000Z','/images/vehicles/42-sith-speeder.png','The Sith speeder is a streamlined, jet-black vehicle used by Darth Maul. It is small, fast, and unarmed. Designed for stealth and speed, it suits Maul’s deadly missions. The speeder was used on Tatooine to track the Jedi. Its design is minimal and lethal. It represents secrecy, pursuit, and menace.','The Sith speeder, officially named the Bloodfin, is a custom-built repulsorlift bike used by Darth Maul during his missions for Darth Sidious. Small, unarmed, and extremely fast, the speeder is optimized for speed over firepower. Its sleek design and black finish allow it to move stealthily through enemy territory. Maul used it to pursue Queen Amidala and confront Jedi on Tatooine. Lacking armor or weapons, it relies solely on the skills and ferocity of its rider. The speeder has minimal profile and almost no support systems—designed solely for deadly efficiency. Its compact build allows it to be easily loaded onto larger vessels such as the Scimitar. The Sith speeder reflects Maul’s own nature—fast, deadly, and focused. It is not a tool of war, but a tool of assassination. The vehicle embodies Sith ideology: concealment, efficiency, and aggression.'),
	(44,'Zephyr-G swoop bike','Zephyr-G swoop bike','repulsorcraft','Mobquet Swoops and Speeders','3.68','5750','1','1','350','200','none','2014-12-20T16:24:16.026000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.714000Z','/images/vehicles/44-zephyr-g-swoop-bike.png','The Zephyr-G swoop bike is a high-speed racing vehicle. Anakin Skywalker rode one through Coruscant’s skies. Built for agility, it zips between traffic lanes. Though not armed, it’s favored by daredevils. It reflects freedom, control, and youthful rebellion. The Zephyr-G symbolizes thrill and recklessness.','The Zephyr-G swoop bike is a civilian high-performance airspeeder built for speed and maneuverability. It is a favorite among thrill-seekers and racers across the galaxy. Anakin Skywalker famously rode a Zephyr-G through the dense traffic of Coruscant while pursuing the assassin Zam Wesell. The bike\'s compact size, responsive steering, and speed make it ideal for tight urban environments. While unarmed and unshielded, it allows skilled riders to navigate perilous situations with sheer reflex. Often seen in the hands of young and bold pilots, it is symbolic of individuality and defiance. The Zephyr-G lacks military applications but is often repurposed in times of chaos. Its powerful repulsorlift engine gives it an edge over standard airspeeders. The vehicle represents the energy and risk of youth. In the hands of Anakin, it also foreshadows the fine line between control and recklessness.'),
	(45,'Koro-2 Exodrive airspeeder','Koro-2 Exodrive airspeeder','airspeeder','Desler Gizh Outworld Mobility Corporation','6.6','unknown','1','1','800','80','unknown','2014-12-20T17:17:33.526000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.716000Z','/images/vehicles/45-koro-2-exodrive-airspeeder.png','The Koro-2 Exodrive is a sleek Coruscanti airspeeder. Zam Wesell used one in an assassination attempt. It features speed and maneuverability in city environments. With enclosed cockpit and luxury design, it masks danger. It can evade authorities in traffic. The Exodrive represents disguise and deception.','The Koro-2 Exodrive airspeeder is a high-end civilian vehicle designed for luxury transport across the vertical cityscape of Coruscant. Its compact frame, powerful repulsorlift engine, and enclosed cockpit allow for seamless navigation through complex traffic layers. Zam Wesell piloted a heavily modified version while attempting to escape Anakin Skywalker and Obi-Wan Kenobi. Though typically unarmed, the vehicle can be customized with hidden compartments and defense countermeasures. Its elegant design masks potential menace, making it a favorite among undercover agents and criminals. The Exodrive excels in short-range evasive flight, ducking between buildings and speedways. It reflects the cosmopolitan luxury of the galactic capital, where wealth and secrecy intertwine. The vehicle’s role in the assassination plot underscores its duality—beautiful on the outside, lethal in function. The Koro-2 Exodrive is a symbol of sleek disguise and high-speed pursuit in the urban sprawl.'),
	(46,'XJ-6 airspeeder','XJ-6 airspeeder','airspeeder','Narglatch AirTech prefabricated kit','6.23','unknown','1','1','720','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T17:19:19.991000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.719000Z','/images/vehicles/46-xj-6-airspeeder.png','The XJ-6 airspeeder is a luxury personal vehicle. Supreme Chancellor Palpatine owned one for transport across Coruscant. It balances elegance and performance. The speeder features enclosed seating and refined controls. Its quiet engine allows discreet movement. The XJ-6 symbolizes status and veiled power.','The XJ-6 airspeeder is a personal transport vehicle favored by the elite of Coruscant. Sleek and quiet, it provides comfort and discretion in one package. Supreme Chancellor Palpatine used an XJ-6 for his private movements during the Clone Wars era. The vehicle features elegant design lines, enclosed seating, and an advanced control system. Though not meant for high-speed chases or combat, it offers reliable short-distance travel in the crowded city skies. The XJ-6 is emblematic of power hidden behind refinement. Its minimal emissions and sound signature make it perfect for unnoticed transit. Unlike military craft, its emphasis is on diplomacy and image. However, when driven by someone like Palpatine, it becomes a vessel of great consequence. The XJ-6 reflects how appearances can deceive—understated, but pivotal. It is the transport of shadowy figures who wield influence behind closed doors.'),
	(50,'LAAT/i','Low Altitude Assault Transport/infrantry','gunship','Rothana Heavy Engineering','17.4','unknown','6','30','620','170','unknown','2014-12-20T18:01:21.014000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.723000Z','/images/vehicles/50-laat-i.png','The LAAT/i is the Republic’s Low Altitude Assault Transport. It carries clone troopers into battle. Armed with blasters and missiles, it dominates the skies. LAAT/i gunships provide air support and rapid deployment. They are iconic symbols of the Clone Wars. The LAAT/i reflects unity, strength, and precision.','The LAAT/i, or Low Altitude Assault Transport/infantry, is a gunship developed for the Grand Army of the Republic during the Clone Wars. Designed for atmospheric operations, the LAAT/i is heavily armed with laser turrets, missile launchers, and bubble cannons, allowing it to clear landing zones and provide covering fire. It can carry a full platoon of clone troopers into battle, deploying them rapidly into hostile territory. Its versatility and resilience made it essential in ground campaigns across the galaxy. The LAAT/i saw action on Geonosis, Umbara, and countless other battlefronts. Its signature engine whine and hovering presence struck fear into Separatist droids. Beyond firepower, it became a symbol of Republic resolve and military might. Painted with unit insignias and nose art, each gunship became a representation of its troopers’ identity. The LAAT/i embodies the strength and coordination of the clone army. It is a vessel of courage, built for frontline duty and unwavering commitment.'),
	(51,'LAAT/c','Low Altitude Assault Transport/carrier','gunship','Rothana Heavy Engineering','28.82','unknown','1','0','620','40000','unknown','2014-12-20T18:02:46.802000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.725000Z','/images/vehicles/51-laat-c.png','The LAAT/c is a carrier variant of the Republic gunship. It transports heavy equipment like the AT-TE. Designed for battlefield logistics, it has no troop seating. With powerful clamps and lift capability, it ensures rapid deployment. It operates alongside frontline forces. The LAAT/c symbolizes Republic coordination and support.','The LAAT/c, or Low Altitude Assault Transport/carrier, is a specialized variant of the Republic\'s gunship developed during the Clone Wars. Unlike the infantry-focused LAAT/i, the LAAT/c is built to carry and deploy heavy ground equipment such as the All Terrain Tactical Enforcer (AT-TE). It features reinforced magnetic clamps and suspension rigs that hold vehicles securely during flight. Though unarmed compared to its combat sibling, the LAAT/c plays a vital role in battlefield logistics. It ensures that the Republic can project both firepower and armor with precision. The LAAT/c operates in tandem with assault waves, providing instant support where it\'s needed most. Its reliability and lift strength made it indispensable during large-scale invasions like the Battle of Geonosis. The LAAT/c reflects the industrial scale and strategic depth of the Republic war effort. It highlights how technology and coordination gave the clone army an edge. The carrier embodies strength through support.'),
	(53,'AT-TE','All Terrain Tactical Enforcer','walker','Rothana Heavy Engineering, Kuat Drive Yards','13.2','unknown','6','36','60','10000','21 days','2014-12-20T18:10:07.560000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.728000Z','/images/vehicles/53-at-te.png','The AT-TE is a six-legged walker used by the Republic. It provides armored ground assault and troop support. Armed with heavy cannons, it is slow but durable. The walker can scale rough terrain and resist enemy fire. AT-TEs lead clone forces in battle. They represent resilience, strength, and order.','The All Terrain Tactical Enforcer, or AT-TE, is a heavily armored walker developed for the Grand Army of the Republic. It features six articulated legs that allow it to traverse difficult terrain, including cliffs and ruins. The walker is equipped with a top-mounted heavy projectile cannon and multiple laser turrets for infantry defense. Its slow but steady advance makes it a key vehicle in siege and front-line operations. The AT-TE carries a squad of clone troopers inside and is often deployed from LAAT/c carriers. It was first used on Geonosis and remained a core asset throughout the Clone Wars. Its low profile compared to other walkers makes it less vulnerable to air strikes. Designed for durability and function, the AT-TE is a symbol of steady power and unrelenting advance. It embodies the Republic’s methodical and coordinated approach to warfare. Even after the Republic’s fall, these walkers remained in limited use, a testament to their engineering.'),
	(54,'SPHA','Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery','walker','Rothana Heavy Engineering','140','unknown','25','30','35','500','7 days','2014-12-20T18:12:32.315000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.731000Z','/images/vehicles/54-spha.png','The SPHA is a massive artillery walker used by the Republic. It fires heavy laser blasts over long distances. Designed for siege warfare, it moves slowly and deliberately. Its firepower can break through fortified positions. It appeared during major Clone Wars battles. The SPHA represents overwhelming force and strategy.','The Self-Propelled Heavy Artillery, or SPHA, is a towering mobile weapon platform developed for the Republic during the Clone Wars. Built on a walker chassis, the SPHA comes in various configurations, most notably the SPHA-T (turbolaser) variant. Its primary purpose is long-range bombardment and base assaults. Despite its limited mobility and slow pace, it delivers devastating firepower capable of breaching enemy strongholds and shielding armies. First seen during the Battle of Geonosis, it provided crucial fire support during the initial Republic victory. The SPHA is crewed by specialized gunners and engineers and typically escorted by infantry units. Its sheer scale makes it a target, but its armored hull offers significant protection. The walker emphasizes calculated, large-scale warfare. It shows how the Republic combined tactical discipline with technological might. The SPHA is the embodiment of deliberate and crushing strength on the battlefield.'),
	(55,'Flitknot speeder','Flitknot speeder','speeder','Huppla Pasa Tisc Shipwrights Collective','2','8000','1','0','634','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T18:15:20.312000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.735000Z','/images/vehicles/55-flitknot-speeder.png','The Flitknot speeder is a sleek vehicle used by droid scouts. It operates quietly and moves swiftly. Lightly armored, it focuses on mobility over combat. Seen on planets like Kashyyyk, it assists with reconnaissance. Its design reflects Separatist efficiency. The Flitknot symbolizes speed and surveillance.','The Flitknot speeder is a lightweight reconnaissance vehicle employed by the Separatist Alliance, primarily operated by B1 battle droids. Compact and agile, the speeder is designed for stealthy patrols and fast traversal of terrain rather than frontline combat. It features minimal weaponry, often limited to a small blaster, and lacks shielding or heavy plating. Flitknot speeders are typically deployed to scout enemy movements, relay positions, and patrol contested zones. During the Battle of Kashyyyk, these speeders were used to track Republic positions among the forest canopies. Their simple construction allows for mass production and expendability, consistent with Separatist military doctrine. While not imposing, the Flitknot’s presence often precedes larger droid deployments. It exemplifies the Separatist emphasis on automation and calculated reconnaissance. The vehicle stands as a reminder that even the smallest pieces on the board can shape the course of war through information.'),
	(56,'Neimoidian shuttle','Sheathipede-class transport shuttle','transport','Haor Chall Engineering','20','unknown','2','6','880','1000','7 days','2014-12-20T18:25:44.912000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.739000Z','/images/vehicles/56-neimoidian-shuttle.png','The Neimoidian shuttle is a transport vessel for high-ranking Trade Federation members. Sleek and discreet, it emphasizes security. It often carries Separatist leaders during the Clone Wars. Though lightly armed, it includes cloaking and shielding tech. The shuttle reflects wealth and secrecy. It symbolizes the elite class of commerce-driven war.','The Neimoidian shuttle is a personal transport used by senior Trade Federation executives and Separatist Council members. It is designed with elegance and safety in mind, providing luxury interiors and reinforced hull plating. The shuttle is often outfitted with defensive systems such as shield generators and stealth modules to avoid detection. It played a frequent role during the Clone Wars, ferrying key figures like Nute Gunray to and from battlefronts and negotiations. Though not a combat vessel, its ability to slip through contested areas makes it valuable. Its smooth curves and minimalist aesthetic match the Neimoidian taste for opulence and control. The ship serves as a visual contrast to the brute force of Separatist military craft. Its presence signals high-stakes diplomacy, scheming, or retreat. The Neimoidian shuttle represents the hidden hand of war—the part conducted behind curtains in boardrooms rather than on battlefields.'),
	(57,'Geonosian starfighter','Nantex-class territorial defense','starfighter','Huppla Pasa Tisc Shipwrights Collective','9.8','unknown','1','0','20000','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T18:34:12.541000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.742000Z','/images/vehicles/57-geonosian-starfighter.png','The Geonosian starfighter is a swift, curved craft used during the Clone Wars. Operated by winged Geonosians, it excels in swarm tactics. It has forward blasters and agility. These fighters defended Geonosis from Republic attack. Their design is insect-like and organic. The ship reflects native defiance and wild engineering.','The Geonosian starfighter is a nimble, atmospheric and space-capable ship built and piloted by native Geonosians. With its crescent wings and pointed fuselage, it mirrors the insectoid features of its creators. Lightly armored but highly maneuverable, it relies on quick strikes and evasive maneuvers. Armed with forward-mounted blaster cannons, these ships are often deployed in swarms to overwhelm targets. They saw significant action during the Battle of Geonosis, where they engaged Jedi starfighters and Republic gunships. The fighter\'s construction draws heavily from native Geonosian materials and organic design principles. Its cockpit accommodates Geonosian physiology, making it unsuitable for humanoid pilots. The ship is a symbol of Geonosian pride and resistance against Republic interference. While not standardized across the galaxy, its role in the Clone Wars marked it as a key component of localized defense. The Geonosian starfighter embodies ingenuity born of necessity and cultural identity expressed through flight.'),
	(60,'Tsmeu-6 personal wheel bike','Tsmeu-6 personal wheel bike','wheeled walker','Z-Gomot Ternbuell Guppat Corporation','3.5','15000','1','1','330','10','none','2014-12-20T19:43:54.870000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.745000Z','/images/vehicles/60-tsmeu-6-personal-wheel-bike.png','The Tsmeu-6 wheel bike is a hybrid walker-vehicle used by General Grievous. It combines speed with crawling grip. The spinning wheel offers fast pursuit, while claws stabilize it. It was seen in action on Utapau. The bike is terrifying in both design and function. It reflects mechanical aggression and chaos.','The Tsmeu-6 personal wheel bike is a one-of-a-kind transport used by General Grievous, designed by the Confederacy for high-speed personal travel. The vehicle features a massive rotating wheel flanked by mechanical legs that deploy for stability or rough terrain. It allows Grievous to chase enemies with terrifying speed while maintaining combat readiness. Armed with side-mounted cannons, it can function both as transport and mobile weapon platform. The bike\'s unique hybrid design makes it capable of scaling walls and navigating narrow corridors. On Utapau, it was used in Grievous’ final duel against Obi-Wan Kenobi. The bike’s chaotic movement and shrieking engine add to its intimidating presence. Though tailored for Grievous’ cyborg body, its concept reflects Separatist innovation at the edge of practicality. The wheel bike represents the unrelenting, unnatural, and brutal force that defines Grievous himself. It’s a machine of pursuit, built for fear and domination.'),
	(62,'Emergency Firespeeder','Fire suppression speeder','fire suppression ship','unknown','unknown','unknown','2','unknown','unknown','unknown','unknown','2014-12-20T19:50:58.559000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.749000Z','/images/vehicles/62-emergency-firespeeder.png','The Emergency Firespeeder is a rescue vehicle used in critical battles. Operated by medical droids, it responds to emergencies on the field. Equipped with water and flame-retardants, it is unarmed. It evacuated Anakin Skywalker on Mustafar. The speeder reflects mercy in chaos. It symbolizes aid, healing, and neutral duty.','The Emergency Firespeeder is a specialized rescue and emergency-response craft used during the Clone Wars and major conflicts. Piloted by droids, it is equipped with flame-retardant sprayers, stabilizers, and medical compartments. Its main function is to extract wounded individuals from active combat zones or burning wreckage. During the final moments of the Clone Wars, it was used to retrieve the gravely injured Anakin Skywalker from Mustafar after his duel with Obi-Wan Kenobi. The Firespeeder is lightly armored but focuses on life-saving tools and rapid deployment. Its presence in battlefields brings a moment of pause, signaling compassion amid destruction. It is neutral in allegiance, driven by programming to save lives regardless of politics. Often overlooked in the chaos of war, it represents a thread of empathy and care. The Emergency Firespeeder stands as a quiet but vital symbol of hope and medical neutrality.'),
	(67,'Droid tri-fighter','tri-fighter','droid starfighter','Colla Designs, Phlac-Arphocc Automata Industries','5.4','20000','1','0','1180','0','none','2014-12-20T20:05:19.992000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.752000Z','/images/vehicles/67-droid-tri-fighter.png','The Droid tri-fighter is an advanced Separatist starfighter. It features a unique three-wing design and internal droid brain. Agile and heavily armed, it excels in space combat. Often used against Jedi starfighters, it swarms with lethal precision. It has no cockpit and no pilot. The tri-fighter represents deadly automation and relentless pursuit.','The Droid tri-fighter is a space superiority starfighter developed by the Confederacy of Independent Systems. Its unique tri-wing configuration allows for superior maneuverability, and its gyro-stabilized central eye contains a powerful droid brain, eliminating the need for an organic pilot. Armed with laser cannons and warhead launchers, the tri-fighter is capable of engaging even the fastest enemy ships. It was deployed in large numbers during major battles such as Coruscant, often targeting Jedi pilots with focused aggression. Its internal systems allow for rapid targeting, evasive movement, and coordination in swarm formations. The ship’s compact design makes it difficult to hit and easy to mass-produce. It lacks shielding but compensates with speed and numbers. The tri-fighter symbolizes the Separatists’ evolution in droid warfare, pushing the boundaries of artificial combat efficiency. With no regard for life, it reflects the cold logic of mechanized destruction. Its presence signals high-stakes dogfights and technological menace.'),
	(69,'Oevvaor jet catamaran','Oevvaor jet catamaran','airspeeder','Appazanna Engineering Works','15.1','12125','2','2','420','50','3 days','2014-12-20T20:20:53.931000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.756000Z','/images/vehicles/69-oevvaor-jet-catamaran.png','The Oevvaor jet catamaran is a swift Wookiee aerial craft. Built from natural materials, it glides over Kashyyyk’s forests. Used for transport and battle, it carries troops through tree canopies. The craft combines tribal engineering with jet propulsion. Piloted by Wookiees, it embodies natural strength. It represents unity and resistance.','The Oevvaor jet catamaran is a uniquely Wookiee vehicle designed to navigate the dense treetop environments of Kashyyyk. Built with traditional Wookiee craftsmanship and augmented with repulsorlift and jet systems, it functions as both a transport and light combat platform. The craft’s twin-hull design gives it stability and maneuverability among the branches and canopies. It carries multiple Wookiee warriors and can be armed with repeating blasters or other mounted weapons. During the Clone Wars, these catamarans played a role in defending Kashyyyk against the Separatist invasion. The blend of natural aesthetics and high-tech propulsion symbolizes the harmony between Wookiee culture and tactical necessity. These crafts are often adorned with tribal markings and symbols of honor. Pilots rely on instinct, agility, and knowledge of the terrain. The Oevvaor jet catamaran reflects a society defending its roots while embracing innovation. It is both a symbol of heritage and rebellion.'),
	(70,'Raddaugh Gnasp fluttercraft','Raddaugh Gnasp fluttercraft','air speeder','Appazanna Engineering Works','7','14750','2','0','310','20','none','2014-12-20T20:21:55.648000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.759000Z','/images/vehicles/70-raddaugh-gnasp-fluttercraft.png','The Raddaugh Gnasp fluttercraft is a Wookiee scout vehicle. It uses beating wings to hover and maneuver. Designed for forest patrols, it is fast and agile. It supports ground troops and defends treetop villages. Operated by skilled Wookiees, it is light and swift. The fluttercraft symbolizes protection and adaptability.','The Raddaugh Gnasp fluttercraft is an aerial reconnaissance vehicle used by Wookiees on Kashyyyk. Unlike standard repulsorlift craft, it employs large, rapidly beating rotor wings reminiscent of insect flight. This design enables it to hover and dart through tight spaces in the forest canopy. Typically unarmed or lightly armed, the fluttercraft focuses on patrol, rapid response, and light troop deployment. It is often used in tandem with heavier vehicles like the Oevvaor jet catamaran. Crafted with Wookiee cultural influence, its design reflects the natural world and their connection to it. It’s quiet, fast, and blends seamlessly into the jungle environment. The fluttercraft saw use during the Clone Wars, especially in countering Separatist incursions. Though small, its contribution was vital in maintaining situational awareness across the complex terrain. It embodies vigilance, harmony with nature, and the quiet strength of Kashyyyk’s defenders.'),
	(71,'Clone turbo tank','HAVw A6 Juggernaut','wheeled walker','Kuat Drive Yards','49.4','350000','20','300','160','30000','20 days','2014-12-20T20:24:45.587000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.762000Z','/images/vehicles/71-clone-turbo-tank.png','The Clone turbo tank is a massive Republic ground vehicle. It boasts heavy armor, powerful weapons, and transport capacity. With ten wheels and advanced suspension, it travels rough terrain. It leads assaults and secures warzones. Used during major Clone Wars battles, it shows brute force. The tank symbolizes military might and defense.','Officially named the HAVw A6 Juggernaut, the Clone turbo tank is a colossal ground assault vehicle deployed by the Grand Army of the Republic. Measuring over 50 meters long and equipped with ten massive wheels, it combines the firepower of a heavy walker with the speed of a wheeled craft. Armed with laser turrets, missile launchers, and anti-infantry blasters, it can engage multiple threats simultaneously. It carries clone troopers, artillery, and command staff into enemy territory. The turbo tank was seen during the Battle of Kashyyyk, where it helped repel Separatist droid forces. Its reinforced armor and advanced terrain sensors allow it to navigate jungle, desert, and urban environments. Despite its size, it can maneuver over obstacles thanks to its suspension system. The vehicle embodies the Republic\'s industrial might and its strategy of overwhelming ground dominance. It stands as a symbol of unity, protection, and unstoppable resolve.'),
	(72,'Corporate Alliance tank droid','NR-N99 Persuader-class droid enforcer','droid tank','Techno Union','10.96','49000','0','4','100','none','none','2014-12-20T20:26:55.522000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.765000Z','/images/vehicles/72-corporate-alliance-tank-droid.jpeg','The Corporate Alliance tank droid is a treaded Separatist vehicle. It has twin cannons and side-mounted blasters. Designed for intimidation and frontline combat, it rolls over enemies. Its central eye scans targets autonomously. Built for mass production, it is ruthless and efficient. The tank droid represents corporate war automation.','The Corporate Alliance tank droid, also known as the NR-N99 Persuader-class, is a multi-role assault vehicle developed for the Confederacy of Independent Systems. With a massive central tread and two side-mounted blaster wheels, it combines brute force with flexibility. Its imposing sensor eye in the center of the chassis gives it an insect-like appearance. Armed with heavy laser cannons and repeating blasters, it crushes infantry and light vehicles alike. The tank droid was notably deployed in the Battle of Kashyyyk, supporting the droid armies in their attack. Operated by an internal control droid, it requires no pilot, reflecting the mechanized efficiency of Separatist design. Its modular structure allows for fast replication and easy repair. As a symbol, it represents the cold, impersonal nature of war waged by profit-driven entities. The Corporate Alliance tank droid is the embodiment of mass-produced terror, rolling over resistance with metallic inevitability.'),
	(73,'Droid gunship','HMP droid gunship','airspeeder','Baktoid Fleet Ordnance, Haor Chall Engineering','12.3','60000','0','0','820','0','none','2014-12-20T20:32:05.687000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.768000Z','/images/vehicles/73-droid-gunship.png','The droid gunship is a hovering Separatist aircraft. Shaped like a beetle, it delivers heavy firepower. Armed with missiles, blasters, and bombs, it is deadly in battle. It supports ground troops and suppresses resistance. It operates autonomously with droid AI. The gunship symbolizes oppressive precision and fear.','The Heavy Missile Platform, commonly known as the droid gunship, is a terrifying aerial weapon used by the Separatists during the Clone Wars. Designed for suppression, it carries a payload of laser cannons, missile launchers, and concussion bombs. Its rounded, beetle-like form glides ominously through the air, offering full overhead coverage to invading droid armies. The gunship is operated by onboard AI and requires no sentient crew. It appeared in numerous battles, including Kashyyyk, raining destruction upon entrenched Republic forces. Built for intimidation and devastation, it hovers with eerie silence before unleashing destruction. Its reinforced frame and targeting systems make it effective against both vehicles and infantry. Though not fast, its firepower compensates. The droid gunship embodies the Separatist vision of war—mechanized, merciless, and efficient. It is a terrifying reminder of the power wielded by those who automate violence.'),
	(76,'AT-RT','All Terrain Recon Transport','walker','Kuat Drive Yards','3.2','40000','1','0','90','20','1 day','2014-12-20T20:47:49.189000Z','2014-12-20T21:30:21.772000Z','/images/vehicles/76-at-rt.png','The AT-RT is a light walker used by clone scouts. Agile and fast, it provides reconnaissance and skirmish support. It carries a single pilot and blaster cannon. Used on battlefields like Kashyyyk, it moves swiftly. The AT-RT reflects clone adaptability and speed. It symbolizes nimble strength and alert defense.','The All Terrain Recon Transport, or AT-RT, is a compact and fast-moving walker developed for the Republic’s clone army. With two articulated legs and an open cockpit, it is piloted by a single trooper. Armed with a mounted blaster cannon, it excels at scouting, patrols, and light combat. Despite limited protection for the rider, its mobility makes it difficult to target. The AT-RT was frequently used in jungle terrain and urban operations, especially during the Battle of Kashyyyk. Its presence enables rapid response and field awareness. Though not suited for prolonged heavy combat, it complements larger vehicles like the AT-TE and turbo tank. The walker reflects the tactical agility of clone forces and their willingness to engage in risky missions. The AT-RT is a symbol of precision and field dominance at the tactical level, reminding all of the effectiveness of the Republic’s military strategy.');
